{"raw": {"https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509062": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Forest Productivity and Management", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant/Associate Professor of Forest Productivity and Management Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant/Associate Professor of Forest Productivity and Management Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This position will be based at the Bulloch County Extension Office in Statesboro, Georgia, serving non-industrial private landowners and stakeholders across the region. To ensure full consideration, candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of outreach interests (as Public Svc/Extension Philosophy), a statement of research interests, including strategies for obtaining external funding for research programs (statements totaling less than three pages), unofficial transcripts of all college-level work, copies of up to three recent publications, and contact information for three references by November 15, 2026. Individuals selected as finalists will be asked to submit official college transcripts to ofatranscripts@uga.edu. Letters of reference will be solicited by the search chair for finalists prior to interviews. Finalists will be required to provide a signed consent form authorizing the University to conduct a background check (www.hr.uga.edu). The background investigation will be conducted on a post-offer/pre-employment basis. The start date is August 1, 2027, but is negotiable. For additional information, please contact Dr. David Clabo, Chair, Forest Productivity and Management Search Committee (DAVID.CLABO@uga.edu). Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2837P Working Title Assistant/Associate Professor of Forest Productivity and Management Department Warnell-Sch Forestry & Nat Res About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Warnell School of Forestry and Natural Resources is a professional school with world class research, teaching, and outreach programs in natural resources conservation and is committed to inclusive excellence. The Warnell School is comprised of 70 faculty, 100 support staff, 265 undergraduates, and 240 graduate students (www.warnell.uga.edu). The school offers Bachelor of Science, Master of Forest Resources, Master of Natural Resources, Master of Science, and Doctor of Philosophy degrees in the areas of Forestry; Fisheries & Wildlife; Parks, Recreation & Tourism Management; and Natural Resource Management & Sustainability. The school manages over 17,000 acres of forestland across the state in support of its teaching, outreach, and research missions. The University of Georgia (www.uga.edu) is a top 20 ranked public land/sea/space grant institution comprised of 18 schools and colleges and designated as a Carnegie Very High Research Activity (R1) institution with strong community engagement. Athens is a diverse community of approximately 150,000 people located less than 75 miles from Atlanta. College/Unit/Department website www.warnell.uga.edu Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/12/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants This position will be based at the Bulloch County Extension Office in Statesboro, Georgia, serving non-industrial private landowners and stakeholders across the region. To ensure full consideration, candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of outreach interests (as Public Svc/Extension Philosophy), a statement of research interests, including strategies for obtaining external funding for research programs (statements totaling less than three pages), unofficial transcripts of all college-level work, copies of up to three recent publications, and contact information for three references by November 15, 2026. Individuals selected as finalists will be asked to submit official college transcripts to ofatranscripts@uga.edu. Letters of reference will be solicited by the search chair for finalists prior to interviews. Finalists will be required to provide a signed consent form authorizing the University to conduct a background check (www.hr.uga.edu). The background investigation will be conducted on a post-offer/pre-employment basis. The start date is August 1, 2027, but is negotiable. For additional information, please contact Dr. David Clabo, Chair, Forest Productivity and Management Search Committee ( DAVID .CLABO@uga.edu). Location of Vacancy Other South Georgia Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Candidates must possess a Ph.D. with an emphasis on forest productivity, silviculture, forest management, or a closely related natural resource discipline (e.g., biometrics, natural resource management and sustainability, water and soil resources). Position Summary The Warnell School of Forestry and Natural Resources at the University of Georgia invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in forest productivity and management at the Assistant or Associate Professor level, with outreach, research, and university and professional service expectations as part of a 9-month appointment. The position includes two additional months of renewable summer salary, consistent with faculty holding majority outreach appointments, with the opportunity to earn additional summer salary through extramural funding. This position is located at the Bulloch County Extension Office in Statesboro, Georgia, and is an off-campus appointment; occasional travel to Athens and elsewhere in the state and region will be required. Successful candidates will be expected to establish interdisciplinary collaborations in outreach and research with faculty in the Warnell School and across the UGA campus. Additional Requirements Candidates must possess at least one degree (B.S., M.S., or Ph.D.) in forest resource management or a closely related discipline and strong academic performance in core coursework as reflected on college transcripts; ABD candidates are encouraged to apply, with the expectation that the degree will be completed prior to the position start date. Appointment to Associate Professor requires a record consistent with promotion to Associate Professor at the Warnell School such as strong evidence of emerging stature as a regional/national authority, acquiring and administering external funding, ability to produce and communicate research, and excellence in outreach and working with stakeholders. The full Warnell School Guidelines can be found here . Service at the Associate Professor level for 1-2 years is preferred for this rank. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Individuals with expertise in forest productivity, forest economics, silviculture, prescribed fire, forest management, forest soils, or a closely related discipline are encouraged to apply, with particular interest in programming that serves non-industrial private landowners. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Candidates must demonstrate clear evidence of scholarship through peer-reviewed publications and/or technical publications, and the ability to attract extramural funding. Candidates must have authored or coauthored a journal article, proceedings paper, or scientific presentation. The successful candidate will demonstrate potential for outreach productivity, a clear understanding of the outreach mission as reflected in the required outreach and research statement and should have interest in outreach education and conducting and reporting research relevant to non-industrial private landowners. The candidate must also demonstrate potential and willingness to work closely with public and private partners, outreach professionals, and other constituent groups, and be able to successfully mentor students. Candidates who have developed and published outreach products (e.g., outreach publications, fact sheets, videos, podcasts) or delivered outreach presentations. Candidates who have worked or completed field work related to undergraduate or graduate degree requirements in the southeastern United States or who have worked in the region as a seasonal or full-time forestry technician, field forester, forestry consultant, or land manager. Candidates who have produced and published (as an author, rather than solely contributed to) a journal article, proceedings paper, or scientific presentation from a research project. Candidates who have the potential or have shown the ability to use modern, innovative outreach tools. Candidates who can integrate science and stakeholder values into their research program. Candidates whose research addresses forest productivity challenges affecting non-industrial private landowners at regional or larger spatial scales and demonstrate an ability to translate research into outcomes relevant to appropriate audiences. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Outreach responsibilities should be satisfied by developing educational activities, publications, and programs (a series of related activities building to develop competencies) which address the needs or requests of non-industrial private landowners, forest industry professionals, state and federal agencies, non-governmental organizations, and county extension personnel in Georgia and beyond. Excellence in outreach programming should involve using creative and innovative delivery strategies (face-to-face, online, video-based, podcasts, etc.) for reaching groups, along with individual, one-on-one consultations for technical assistance related to forest productivity and management. Percentage Of Time 70 Duties/Responsibilities Research responsibilities include development of an externally funded, regionally/nationally recognized program in forest productivity and management (e.g., intensive pine silviculture, forest fertilization and site productivity, forest soils and nutrition management, stand density and thinning economic decisions, regeneration and establishment, vegetation management, pine straw management, prescribed fire, etc.). Research and outreach programming/publications may be directly linked. Consultation and technical assistance will be defined as providing specialized knowledge to stakeholders within the scope of the Warnell School mission. The successful candidate will interact with and advise non-industrial private landowners, industry professionals, state and federal agencies, non-profit organizations, and extension professionals, state and federal agencies, non-profit organizations, and extension professionals. Percentage Of Time 25 Duties/Responsibilities Professional service includes serving on School/University committees and actively participating in professional/scientific societies among other like activities. Percentage Of Time 5 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Sample Publications Unofficial Transcripts List of References with Contact Information Research Portfolio/Philosophy Public Svc/Extension Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509037": {"title": "Associate Professor: Discipline-Based Education Research in Computational Biology, Biochemistry, or Chemistry", "description": "University of Georgia | Associate Professor: Discipline-Based Education Research in Computational Biology, Biochemistry, or Chemistry Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Associate Professor: Discipline-Based Education Research in Computational Biology, Biochemistry, or Chemistry Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must submit: 1) a cover letter summarizing the applicant\u2019s qualifications and interest in the position; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement of 3 pages or less that summarizes prior discipline-based education research accomplishments and planned research directions; and 4) a statement of 2 pages or less that summarizes prior and planned teaching and mentoring activities and how they integrate with UGA\u2019s core mission ( https://uga.edu/about/mission ). Applicants should also submit names and contact information for three references. The search committee will request references from specific applicants after an initial screening of applications, which may include a brief Zoom interview. Review of applications will begin on November 13, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Informal inquiries and questions can be addressed to the chair of the search committee (eldolan@uga.edu) or the Head of the BCMB department ( bcmb-head@uga.edu ). Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2840P Working Title Associate Professor: Discipline-Based Education Research in Computational Biology, Biochemistry, or Chemistry Department Franklin-Biochemistry About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department BCMB is a highly successful, multidisciplinary research-intensive academic unit at UGA that is comprised of over 60 affiliated members who lead innovative research programs across the spectrum of biochemistry and molecular biology including discipline-based education research. We maintain internationally recognized research programs in areas such as bioinformatics, enzymology, epigenetics, cancer biology, glycobiology, infectious disease, molecular medicine, STEM education, and structural biology. There are ample opportunities for collaboration with STEM education researchers within the unit and across the agricultural, life, engineering, medical, pharmaceutical, and veterinary sciences at UGA . The position will also benefit from interactions with the Artificial Intelligence for STEM Education (AI4STEM Education) center, the Center for Teaching and Learning ( CTL ), the Digital Humanities Lab, The Institute of Higher Education, the Owens Institute for Behavioral Research, and the Scientists Engaged in Education Research ( SEER ) center, whose collective goal is to improve and advance teaching and learning across the institution. FCAS is the academic home of BCMB and is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. FCAS has a rich history and boasts a strong and diverse research portfolio. With a vision for high-impact research and education, FCAS prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future and is strongly committed to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation. UGA is consistently ranked among the top public universities in the nation. Research at UGA spans a broad range of established and emerging disciplines and has expanded its research portfolio recently with the launch of a School of Medicine. UGA is part of the vibrant city of Athens, Georgia in the northern Piedmont region of the state, 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, Georgia. Athens is home to a culturally diverse population and thriving arts and music communities ( https://www.visitathensga.com/ ). College/Unit/Department website https://www.bmb.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/12/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants must submit: 1) a cover letter summarizing the applicant\u2019s qualifications and interest in the position; 2) a curriculum vitae; 3) a statement of 3 pages or less that summarizes prior discipline-based education research accomplishments and planned research directions; and 4) a statement of 2 pages or less that summarizes prior and planned teaching and mentoring activities and how they integrate with UGA\u2019s core mission ( https://uga.edu/about/mission ). Applicants should also submit names and contact information for three references. The search committee will request references from specific applicants after an initial screening of applications, which may include a brief Zoom interview. Review of applications will begin on November 13, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Informal inquiries and questions can be addressed to the chair of the search committee (eldolan@uga.edu) or the Head of the BCMB department ( bcmb-head@uga.edu ). Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Associate Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Associate Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track or Tenured Minimum Qualifications Applicants must possess a Ph.D. (or equivalent) in Biochemistry, Computational Biology, Chemistry, or other computational and/or molecular life science field. Position Summary Associate Professor \u2013 Discipline-Based Education Research in Computational Biology, Biochemistry, or Chemistry The Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology ( BCMB ) within the Franklin College of Arts and Sciences ( FCAS ) at the University of Georgia ( UGA ) invites applications for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position at the rank of Associate Professor beginning August 1, 2027. Applications from advanced Assistant Professors with strong dossiers for promotion to Associate Professor will also be considered. Expectations are that the position will lead a dynamic, externally funded and internationally recognized research program, contribute to education and mentoring of undergraduate students, graduate students, and other trainees, and participate in departmental and institutional service activities that are typical for the position. Additional Requirements Applicants must possess a Ph.D. (or equivalent) in Biochemistry, Computational Biology, Chemistry, or other computational and/or molecular life science field, or discipline-based education research in one of these fields. Applicants must have qualifications and academic credentials that are commensurate with the promotion and tenure (P&T) guidelines at the UGA ( https://provost.uga.edu/faculty-affairs/promotion-tenure-evaluation/promotion-and-tenure/promotion-guidelines/ ). To be eligible for tenure upon appointment, candidates must be appointed as an associate professor, have been tenured at a prior institution, and bring a demonstrably national reputation to the institution. Candidates must be approved for tenure upon appointment before hire. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Primary consideration will be given to outstanding applicants whose research advances teaching and learning of biochemistry and/or chemistry from a computational perspective. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509029": {"title": "Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, please submit a vita with a list of publications, a teaching statement, a research statement, and four letters of recommendation (one addressing the candidate\u2019s teaching skills), through mathjobs.org. Candidates will also need to submit an application through UGAJobs with a list of references who provided recommendation letters on mathjobs.org. Applicants should apply to this position through both MathJobs and UGAJobs; candidates who do not submit an application to UGAJobs cannot be considered for the position. Complete applications must be received by November 11, 2026, to ensure full consideration, but review will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2841P Working Title Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor Department Franklin-Mathematics About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Mathematics Department is a unit of the Franklin College of Arts and Sciences which is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The College has a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation. College/Unit/Department website https://www.math.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/12/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, please submit a vita with a list of publications, a teaching statement, a research statement, and four letters of recommendation (one addressing the candidate\u2019s teaching skills), through mathjobs.org. Candidates will also need to submit an application through UGAJobs with a list of references who provided recommendation letters on mathjobs.org. Applicants should apply to this position through both MathJobs and UGAJobs; candidates who do not submit an application to UGAJobs cannot be considered for the position. Complete applications must be received by November 11, 2026, to ensure full consideration, but review will continue until the position is filled. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank (Tenure Track) Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track or Tenured Minimum Qualifications Applicants should hold a Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in Mathematics or a related field at the time of appointment. Position Summary The Department of Mathematics at the University of Georgia invites applications for two tenure-track positions to start in August 2027. Appointments may be at the Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor level, depending on the experience of the candidate. Duties will consist of research and teaching in mathematics, as well as departmental service. Additional Requirements Candidates for the Associate Professor or Professor rank must have qualifications and academic credentials commensurate with the promotion and tenure guidelines at the University of Georgia and must be approved for tenure upon appointment before hire. These guidelines can be found at: https://provost.uga.edu/faculty-affairs/promotion-tenure-evaluation/promotion-and-tenure/promotion-guidelines/ Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Successful applicants will carry outstanding credentials in mathematical research and demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students. We are particularly interested in research that bridges fields and/or has connections to AI. For one of the positions, the ideal candidate will demonstrate expertise in analysis, geometry, or probability. For the other position, the ideal candidate will demonstrate expertise in probability, particularly stochastic analysis, high-dimensional probability, or mathematical finance. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/508823": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor in Biological Anthropology of Health and Human Variation", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant or Associate Professor in Biological Anthropology of Health and Human Variation Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant or Associate Professor in Biological Anthropology of Health and Human Variation Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, electronically submit application materials that will include: 1) cover letter, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) a 1-2p statement of prior research accomplishments and planned research directions and 4) a 1-2p combined teaching/mentorship statement that includes relevant courses previously taught and proposed courses at UGA. Applicants should also provide names for three references from whom letters of recommendation will be requested later in the search process. For questions about this faculty position, please contact Dr. Susan Tanner ( stanner1@uga.edu ). Applications received by December 2, 2026, will receive full consideration and review will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2838P Working Title Assistant or Associate Professor in Biological Anthropology of Health and Human Variation Department Franklin-Anthropology About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The College has a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation. College/Unit/Department website https://anthropology.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/09/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, electronically submit application materials that will include: 1) cover letter, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) a 1-2p statement of prior research accomplishments and planned research directions and 4) a 1-2p combined teaching/mentorship statement that includes relevant courses previously taught and proposed courses at UGA . Applicants should also provide names for three references from whom letters of recommendation will be requested later in the search process. For questions about this faculty position, please contact Dr. Susan Tanner ( stanner1@uga.edu ). Applications received by December 2, 2026, will receive full consideration and review will continue until the position is filled. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank (Tenure Track) Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications The applicant must possess a Ph.D. (or equivalent) in Anthropology or a related field. Position Summary The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences at the University of Georgia ( UGA ) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor in Biological Anthropology of Health and Human Variation in the Department of Anthropology, beginning August 1, 2027. This position contributes to Franklin College\u2019s interdisciplinary initiative in Applied Health Innovation for Societal Impact and its area of emphasis in Genomics, Epigenetics, and Biomes. This is a full-time equivalent position with a 50% instruction (12 credit hours), 45% research, and 5% service effort expectation per academic year. The successful candidate will develop an independent research program with strong potential for extramural support and interdisciplinary collaboration. The Department of Anthropology offers opportunities to connect this work with existing strengths in human biology and health, bioarchaeology, primate biology and behavior, and ecological and environmental anthropology. Across UGA , the candidate will have access to shared research infrastructure and core facilities supporting genomic, computational, bioinformatic, and related research, as well as opportunities to develop connections with researchers and emerging programs across the health and life sciences. The successful candidate will contribute to the Department of Anthropology\u2019s undergraduate and graduate programs. Teaching will include one large-enrollment undergraduate course per year as well as upper-level undergraduate and graduate courses in the candidate\u2019s areas of expertise. Opportunities also exist to contribute to developing interdisciplinary programs in Forensic Science and Health Humanities. Applicants should demonstrate potential for excellence in research, teaching and mentorship and for productive interdisciplinary collaboration. Additional Requirements This position is for a tenure-track Assistant or Associate Professor. Candidates must have qualifications and academic credentials that are commensurate with the promotion and tenure guidelines at the University of Georgia and must be approved for tenure upon appointment before hire. These guidelines can be found at https://provost.uga.edu/faculty-affairs/promotion-tenure/ . Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies We seek a biological anthropologist whose research examines how biological, social, ecological, and evolutionary processes interact to shape health and human variation across populations, environments, and/or over time. Areas of specialization are open and may include human biology; anthropological or population genomics; evolutionary genetics; epigenetics; microbiome research; molecular or biomarker approaches to health and adaptation; ancient biomolecular research; primate biology; or related areas. We particularly welcome scholarship that integrates biological evidence with evolutionary, ecological, social, archaeological, or biocultural perspectives. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/508624": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Design Anthropology", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant Professor of Design Anthropology Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant Professor of Design Anthropology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, electronically submit application materials that will include 1) cover letter, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) a 1-2p statement of prior research accomplishments and planned research directions and 4) a 1-2p combined teaching/mentorship statement that includes relevant courses previously taught and proposed courses at UGA. Applicants should also provide names for three references from whom letters of recommendation will be requested later in the search process. For questions about this faculty position, please contact Dr. Meredith Welch-Devine ( mwdevine@uga.edu ). Applications received by December 2, 2026 will receive full consideration and review will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2827P Working Title Assistant Professor of Design Anthropology Department Franklin-Anthropology About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The College has a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation. College/Unit/Department website https://anthropology.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/01/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, electronically submit application materials that will include 1) cover letter, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) a 1-2p statement of prior research accomplishments and planned research directions and 4) a 1-2p combined teaching/mentorship statement that includes relevant courses previously taught and proposed courses at UGA . Applicants should also provide names for three references from whom letters of recommendation will be requested later in the search process. For questions about this faculty position, please contact Dr. Meredith Welch-Devine ( mwdevine@uga.edu ). Applications received by December 2, 2026 will receive full consideration and review will continue until the position is filled. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Assistant Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications The applicant must possess a Ph.D. (or equivalent) in Anthropology or a related field. Position Summary The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences at the University of Georgia ( UGA ) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Design Anthropology in the Department of Anthropology, beginning August 1, 2027. The successful candidate will contribute to the development of design anthropology as an area of research and teaching within the Department of Anthropology while creating opportunities for interdisciplinary connections across UGA , including with the interdisciplinary Museum Studies Program. Areas of specialization within design anthropology are open and may engage material, visual, digital, or multimodal forms; technologies and infrastructures; museum anthropology, exhibition practice, and collections; or other designed environments and systems. Relevant work may employ ethnographic, participatory, collaborative, or experimental approaches to investigate the social, cultural, political, and ethical dimensions of design and to engage processes of making, intervention, community engagement, and imagining possible futures. The successful candidate will have opportunities to collaborate with faculty across anthropology and to develop research and teaching connections with UGA\u2019s museums, collections, laboratories, public-facing institutions, and community partners, including the interdisciplinary Museum Studies Program, Georgia Museum of Natural History, Laboratory of Archaeology, Georgia Museum of Art, Lamar Dodd School of Art, College of Environment and Design, and other relevant programs and units across campus. These settings offer opportunities to approach museums, collections, and other public-facing environments not simply as repositories or sites for presenting knowledge, but as spaces of encounter, ethnographic inquiry, collaborative experimentation, design, imagination, and public engagement. The successful candidate will be expected to develop an independent research program with strong potential for extramural support. The successful candidate will contribute to the Department of Anthropology\u2019s undergraduate and graduate programs and develop courses in design anthropology and the candidate\u2019s areas of expertise that can also create interdisciplinary connections with Museum Studies and other programs across UGA . Teaching will include one large-enrollment undergraduate course per year as well as upper-level undergraduate and graduate courses. This position is for a tenure-track Assistant Professor. This is a full-time equivalent position with a 50% instruction (12 credit hours), 45% research, and 5% service effort expectation per academic year. Additional Requirements The qualifications and academic expectations for ranks as well as the guidelines for promotion and tenure at the University of Georgia can be found at https://provost.uga.edu/faculty-affairs/promotion-tenure/ . Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies We seek an anthropologist whose research and teaching explore relationships among people, culture, design, and material, visual, digital, spatial, or experiential forms of knowledge and practice. We welcome candidates whose anthropologically grounded research examines how people imagine, make, use, experience, and transform objects, technologies, environments, institutions, and systems, and how anthropological knowledge and methods can contribute to processes of design, representation, experimentation, and public engagement. We seek scholars who approach design not only as an object of anthropological analysis but also as a mode of inquiry and collaboration. Applicants should demonstrate potential for excellence in teaching and mentoring and for engaging students in anthropological approaches to design, ethnography, material and visual culture, museums, technology, environments, and public-facing scholarship. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/508532": {"title": "Open Rank -Clinical Track Neurology Faculty", "description": "University of Georgia | Open Rank -Clinical Track Neurology Faculty Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Open Rank -Clinical Track Neurology Faculty Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Qualified applicants are invited to submit: (1) a letter of intent including professional interests and career goals, (2) a curriculum vitae, and (3) the name, mailing address, and contact information for three professional references. Questions regarding the position may be directed to Dr. Ben Brainard, search committee chairperson, by email (brainard@uga.edu) or telephone (706-202-5665). All applications received on or before November 15, 2026 will be fully considered; applications will be accepted until the position is filled. The successful candidate\u2019s employment starting date is negotiable; the position is available July 1, 2027. As required by the University of Georgia policy, the successful candidate will be subject to a background investigation. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2832P Working Title Open Rank -Clinical Track Neurology Faculty Department VetMed-Small Animal Med & Surg About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The University of Georgia College of Veterinary Medicine, founded in 1946, is dedicated to training future veterinarians, providing services to animal owners and veterinarians, and conducting investigations to improve the health of animals as well as people. The college benefits pets and their owners, food-producing animals, and wildlife by offering the highest quality hospital and diagnostic laboratory services. Equipped with the most technologically advanced facilities located on a university campus, the college is dedicated to safeguarding public health by studying emerging infectious diseases that affect both animal and human health. The Department of Small Animal Medicine and Surgery consists of 50 faculty members, 50 clinical residents, 10 rotating interns, 8 specialty interns, and 3 administrative staff members. Shared laboratory space and technical support are provided within the department, and there are 7 dedicated research technicians who assist in the research missions of the department\u2019s faculty. Other specialties within the department include anesthesia, dermatology, internal medicine, nutrition, medical and radiation oncology, ophthalmology, orthopedic surgery, radiology, soft tissue surgery, and zoological medicine, as well as a community practice program ( UGA Pet Health Center). The Department participates in the college-wide M.S. and Ph.D. programs. Members of the department also actively participate in highly successful collaborative efforts with faculty members from other departments within the college and other colleges on campus, including the College of Public Health, College of Engineering, and the Athens campus of the Medical College of Georgia. The department has a strong track record for teaching, research, and clinical service. The University of Georgia, the nation\u2019s first chartered state-supported university, is a research-intensive land grant and sea grant university situated in the vibrant college town of Athens. Only an hour from Atlanta, Athens is a progressive locale with a rich history and is centered among beautiful surrounding landscapes. The area abounds in local music, art, literature, and theatre and hosts many performances by national and international touring artists. The cost of living in Athens compares favorably with much of the rest of the country, ranking lower than the U.S. average ( http://www.bestplaces.net/city/georgia/athens-clarke_county ). Additional information about the Athens area can be found at http://www.visitathensga.com/ . The College of Veterinary Medicine values all members of the university community, recognizing that differences in experience and culture can only lead to a more well-rounded, accepting academic environment as embodied in our Principles of Community . College/Unit/Department website www.vet.uga.edu Posting Type Internal (PEP) Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary commensurate with experience and qualifications Anticipated Start Date 07/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/07/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Qualified applicants are invited to submit: (1) a letter of intent including professional interests and career goals, (2) a curriculum vitae, and (3) the name, mailing address, and contact information for three professional references. Questions regarding the position may be directed to Dr. Ben Brainard, search committee chairperson, by email (brainard@uga.edu) or telephone (706-202-5665). All applications received on or before November 15, 2026 will be fully considered; applications will be accepted until the position is filled. The successful candidate\u2019s employment starting date is negotiable; the position is available July 1, 2027. As required by the University of Georgia policy, the successful candidate will be subject to a background investigation. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Candidates must have a DVM or equivalent degree. Position Summary The Department of Small Animal Medicine and Surgery at the College of Veterinary Medicine, University of Georgia, invites applications for a clinical (non-tenure) track faculty position in veterinary neurology at the rank of assistant, associate, or full professor. The major responsibilities of this position will be to teach and provide service in the Veterinary Teaching Hospital, to teach pre-clinical didactic and laboratory courses in neurology to veterinary students, and to actively participate in the training of neurology and non-neurology house officers. Proportionate assignments for each area are based on the interests of the candidate, faculty assignment, and the missions of the neurology program and department. The successful candidate will join a neurology service with three full-time faculty members, three residents, and two dedicated technicians in support of the University of Georgia Veterinary Teaching Hospital, a 300,000 square foot state-of-the-art facility. The service enjoys ready access to a Siemens 3.0T MRI unit, 3rd generation 128-slice helical CT, Nicolet electrophysiological testing equipment ( EMG , nerve conduction, and EEG ), fluoroscopy, intraoperative C-arm, digital radiography, an ultrasonic aspirator and a Medtronic Stealth Trio stereotactic biopsy unit. This active clinical service provides medical neurology and neurosurgical care for approximately 500-600 new referral cases per year. The service is supported by 3 registered veterinary technicians (one technician has VTS certification in neurology. A second technician is in the process of obtaining VTS specialization in neurology). The neurology service benefits from collegial relations and the support of the other hospital services including oncology, radiation therapy, surgery, anesthesia, and critical care. Teaching is a priority of the neurology service. Neurology faculty teach in all years of the current veterinary curriculum.\u00a0 The neurology faculty has over 50 contact hours throughout the DVM curriculum including classroom lectures as well as laboratory instruction. Additionally, neurology services have an ACVIM approved residency program. There are 3 residents enrolled in the ACVIM Neurology residency program. The neurology faculty is involved in a number of graduate and post-graduate courses, including continuing education courses for graduate veterinarians. For all candidates, salary and entry rank will be commensurate with the applicant\u2019s experience and qualifications. Additional Requirements Candidates should have completed or be in the process of completing an approved residency of the American College of Veterinary Internal Medicine or European College of Veterinary Neurology, and have board certification or be eligible for board certification. Requirements for appointment for clinical assistant, associate, and full professor (non-tenure track) can be found in the Guidelines for Appointment and Promotion of Non-tenure Track Clinical Faculty in the Department of Small Animal Medicine and Surgery : https://vet.uga.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/capu-criteria-small-animal-medicine-surgery.pdf and the University of Georgia Guidelines for Appointment and Promotion of Clinical Faculty: https://provost.uga.edu/wp-content/uploads/appointment-promotion-guidelines-clinical-faculty.pdf . Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification State of Georgia Veterinary License or Veterinary Faculty License. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? Yes Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities The major responsibilities for this position are to teach and provide service in small animal neurology in the Veterinary Teaching Hospital, teach didactic and laboratory courses related to neurology topics to veterinary students, actively participate in the training of residents and interns, and develop a research program, which can be independent and/or collaborative with other faculty members. Percentage Of Time 100 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Optional Documents Cover Letter Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/508525": {"title": "Associate Professor of Nutritional Sciences and Nursing", "description": "University of Georgia | Associate Professor of Nutritional Sciences and Nursing Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Associate Professor of Nutritional Sciences and Nursing Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Full consideration will be given to applications received by December 1, 2026 . The application packet must include a cover letter of interest that details how the applicant\u2019s credentials and experience meet the teaching and research needs of the position as well as responsibilities and qualifications detailed in the posting; a current curriculum vitae; and contact information for three references. References will not be contacted without further correspondence with the applicant. Confidential requests for information may be directed to: Ali Berg, PhD Professor of Nutritional Sciences Chair, Search Committee Department of Nutritional Sciences The University of Georgia 280 Dawson Hall Athens, GA 30602 Alisoncberg@uga.edu. Information regarding fringe benefits may be viewed at http://www.hr.uga.edu . Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2834P Working Title Associate Professor of Nutritional Sciences and Nursing Department FACS-Nutritional Sciences About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. . About the College/Unit/Department The Victoria Kay Ivester School of Nursing at the University of Georgia is a new academic school established to advance nursing education, research, practice, and service while helping address the health and healthcare workforce needs of Georgia and beyond. As part of Georgia\u2019s flagship land-grant university, the Ivester School of Nursing is building a community of nurse educators, clinicians, scientists, and leaders committed to preparing an exceptionally qualified nursing workforce and generating knowledge that improves health and healthcare. The School\u2019s mission emphasizes innovative teaching, scholarly inquiry, clinical excellence, and statewide service, with particular attention to the needs of rural, underserved, and rapidly growing communities. The Ivester School of Nursing will welcome its inaugural students into nursing coursework in fall 2027 and is developing undergraduate and future graduate programs designed to prepare nurses, advanced practice nurses, educators, and scientists. A new School of Nursing building is planned for the UGA Health Sciences Campus, providing a future home for nursing education, simulation, research, and collaboration. The School is intentionally building a strong research enterprise, with tenure-track faculty expected to develop sustained programs of externally funded research and clinical faculty contributing scholarship in education, practice, quality improvement, and implementation. The College of Family and Consumer Sciences is committed to student success, holistic development and inclusive perspective taking. FACS develops leaders who focus on the science and art of helping individuals live well in a complex society. The Department of Nutritional Sciences is one of four departments in the College. The Department has 21 full-time and 3 part-time faculty, 408 undergraduate students majoring in Nutritional Sciences and Dietetics, as well as, 31 graduate students in the PhD and MS thesis graduate degree programs and 58 in the non-thesis MS degree programs including the on-line MS program in Community Nutrition. The Department of Nutritional Sciences has strong ties and opportunities for interdisciplinary research programs with Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, Genetics, Animal and Dairy Sciences, Kinesiology, Pharmacy, Food Science and Technology, Public Health, Veterinary Medicine, Gerontology, Psychology, the Biomedical and Health Sciences Institute and others. The University of Georgia is one of four institutions participating in the NIH -funded Georgia Clinical & Translational Alliance which leverages complementary strengths to accelerate clinical and translational research. The Clinical and Translational Research Unit ( CTRU ) located on the UGA Health Sciences Campus, supports investigators to conduct clinical and translational studies. In addition, health-related programing is disseminated and community-based participatory research is conduced though UGA Cooperative Extension . Department-based specialists in cooperation with county-based agents extend lifelong learning to the people of Georgia through research-based education on issues related to food and health, money, family and home. FACS Extension helps to improve the health of Georgians. College/Unit/Department website https://www.fcs.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Commensurate with experience and qualifications Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/07/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Full consideration will be given to applications received by December 1, 2026 . The application packet must include a cover letter of interest that details how the applicant\u2019s credentials and experience meet the teaching and research needs of the position as well as responsibilities and qualifications detailed in the posting; a current curriculum vitae; and contact information for three references. References will not be contacted without further correspondence with the applicant. Confidential requests for information may be directed to: Ali Berg, PhD Professor of Nutritional Sciences Chair, Search Committee Department of Nutritional Sciences The University of Georgia 280 Dawson Hall Athens, GA 30602 Alisoncberg@uga.edu. Information regarding fringe benefits may be viewed at http://www.hr.uga.edu . Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Associate Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Associate Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Applicants must hold an earned doctoral degree in nutrition or a related scientific field. Position Summary Associate Professor of Nutritional Sciences and Nursing (45% Research, 50% Teaching, 5% Service), 9-month academic year tenure-track appointment with a joint appointment in the Department of Nutritional Sciences in the College of Family and Consumer Sciences (60% appointment) and the Victoria Key Ivestor School of Nursing (40% appointment). RESPONSIBILITIES INCLUDE : 1) Develop a nationally recognized and externally-funded program focused on the role of nutrition and/or nutritional interventions in the prevention and management of chronic disease, including cardiovascular disease, cancer, stroke, diabetes, or other diet-related chronic diseases; 2) Direct and support research programs of PhD- and MS-level students; 3) Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in nutritional sciences both in the College of Family and Consumer Sciences and in the School of Nursing; 4) Engage in collaborative and interdisciplinary research with faculty in the Department of Nutritional Sciences in the College of Family and Consumer Sciences and the School of Nursing, as well as other UGA departments/colleges; 5) Contribute to activities that serve the department, college, school, university, the public and the profession. Additional Requirements QUALIFICATIONS : Candidates should have attained tenure at a comparable university or have at least four years of experience at the Assistant Professor rank; demonstrate scholarly competence and research productivity in chronic disease prevention research as evidenced by a high quality research publication record and a record of success with external funding; and demonstrate clear and convincing evidence of emerging stature as a regional or national authority as appropriate for the position. To be eligible for tenure on appointment, candidates must be appointed as an Associate Professor, have been tenured at a prior institution, and bring a demonstrably national reputation to the institution. Any request for tenure upon appointment must be approved before hire. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS : Candidates credentialed as a registered dietitian nutritionist by the Commission on Dietetics are preferred. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Candidates must show evidence of strong written and verbal communication skills. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/508490": {"title": "Associate Professor or Professor of Microbiology in Medical Mycology", "description": "University of Georgia | Associate Professor or Professor of Microbiology in Medical Mycology Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Associate Professor or Professor of Microbiology in Medical Mycology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates should submit the following application materials electronically: (1) a cover letter; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) a statement of research interests and goals, up to two pages; (4) a teaching and mentoring statement, up to one page, addressing approaches to fostering a supportive learning environment; and (5) the names and contact information of three references, who will be asked to provide letters of recommendation. Questions regarding the position may be directed to the Search Committee at: Xiaorong.Lin@uga.edu . Completed applications received by December 4, 2026, are assured full consideration. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2835P Working Title Associate Professor or Professor of Microbiology in Medical Mycology Department Franklin-Microbiology About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department UGA offers exceptional research facilities and extensive opportunities for collaboration across the life sciences, engineering, veterinary medicine, and medicine. Athens is a culturally diverse city renowned for its music, arts, and food scenes. It is located approximately one hour from Atlanta, less than two hours from the Blue Ridge Mountains, and within easy driving distance of the Atlantic coast. The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The Department of Microbiology and Franklin College have a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration, and academic innovation. College/Unit/Department website https://mib.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/07/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Candidates should submit the following application materials electronically: (1) a cover letter; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) a statement of research interests and goals, up to two pages; (4) a teaching and mentoring statement, up to one page, addressing approaches to fostering a supportive learning environment; and (5) the names and contact information of three references, who will be asked to provide letters of recommendation. Questions regarding the position may be directed to the Search Committee at: Xiaorong.Lin@uga.edu . Completed applications received by December 4, 2026, are assured full consideration. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank (Tenure Track) Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Applicants must hold a PhD (or equivalent) in Microbiology or a related field. Position Summary The Department of Microbiology at the University of Georgia invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-track position in Medical Mycology at the rank of Associate or Full Professor, with an anticipated start date of August 1, 2027. The successful candidate will contribute to the teaching, research, and service missions of the Department of Microbiology. Responsibilities include teaching courses in microbiology, mycology, infectious disease, or related topics, as well as participating in service and student mentoring. The successful candidate will also benefit from participation in the UGA Interdisciplinary Fungal Biology Group, which provides opportunities for scientific exchange, collaboration, and trainee development. Additional Requirements Candidates must have qualifications and academic credentials that are commensurate with the promotion and tenure guidelines at the University of Georgia and must be approved for tenure upon appointment before hire. These guidelines can be found at https://provost.uga.edu/faculty-affairs/promotion-tenure/ . Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies We seek an outstanding scientist whose research advances the fundamental and/or translational understanding of human fungal pathogens using experimental, computational, or integrative approaches. Candidates should have an established record of research productivity and extramural funding appropriate for appointment at the rank of Associate or Full Professor, together with a compelling vision for the future development of their research program. Evidence of excellence in graduate and undergraduate teaching and mentoring is also expected. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/508299": {"title": "Lecturer", "description": "University of Georgia | Lecturer Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Lecturer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications received by November 5, 2026, will receive full consideration. Review of applications will begin on November 6, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit the following as a single PDF document in the \"Other Documents #1\" section of the application: A cover letter addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relating to the responsibilities of the position, with a summary of accomplishments and future goals (2-page max) A detailed curriculum vitae A statement outlining teaching philosophy and experiences regarding instruction and mentoring (2-page max) The names, titles, and contact information for three professional references Questions about the position should be directed to: Jordan Khail, Pharm.D. Lecturer The University of Georgia College of Pharmacy 250 W. Green St. Athens, GA 30602 Phone: 706-542-5371 Email: Jordan.Khail@uga.edu Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2836P Working Title Lecturer Department Pharmacy-Clin & Admin Pharmacy About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The University of Georgia College of Pharmacy is a distinguished leader in pharmacy education, research, and service at the regional, national, and international levels. Primarily situated on the University of Georgia campus in Athens, the College also has extended campuses in Albany, Augusta, Savannah, and Metro Atlanta (Gwinnett). The College offers nationally recognized pharmacy and pharmaceutical and biomedical sciences, experimental therapeutics, social and administrative sciences, and regulatory sciences degree programs and provides a rigorous, research-based curriculum taught by accomplished faculty in an experiential learning environment. Enrollment across the undergraduate, professional and graduate degree levels in degree programs, minors, and certificates approaches 1000 students. Faculty and students are engaged in groundbreaking research spanning drug discovery, pharmacology, clinical pharmacy, and other areas that advance healthcare and medicine. Clinical training is provided through a network of sites across Georgia through established partnerships and agreements. Consistently ranked among the nation\u2019s top colleges of pharmacy, including 16th among 140 pharmacy programs by U.S. News & World Report , the College is committed to excellence in education, research, and service. For more information, visit https://rx.uga.edu/ . College/Unit/Department website https://rx.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 01/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/05/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications received by November 5, 2026, will receive full consideration. Review of applications will begin on November 6, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. Interested applicants should submit the following as a single PDF document in the \u201cOther Documents #1\u201d section of the application: A cover letter addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relating to the responsibilities of the position, with a summary of accomplishments and future goals (2-page max) A detailed curriculum vitae A statement outlining teaching philosophy and experiences regarding instruction and mentoring (2-page max) The names, titles, and contact information for three professional references Questions about the position should be directed to: Jordan Khail, Pharm.D. Lecturer The University of Georgia College of Pharmacy 250 W. Green St. Athens, GA 30602 Phone: 706-542-5371 Email: Jordan.Khail@uga.edu Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Lecturer FLSA Faculty Rank Lecturer Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Terminal degree in Pharmacy (Pharm.D.), Pharmaceutical Sciences, Health Sciences, Biomedical Sciences, Public Health, Health Administration, Healthcare Outcomes, Clinical Research, or a closely related discipline appropriate to the assigned teaching responsibilities. Position Summary The University of Georgia College of Pharmacy invites applications for a full-time, fiscal-year (12-month), non-tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Lecturer in the Department of Clinical and Administrative Pharmacy ( CAP ). This position will be based in Athens, Georgia. As the College continues to expand its educational programs and impact across Georgia, we seek an outstanding educator who is passionate about student success, innovative teaching, and preparing future pharmacists for contemporary healthcare practice. This position offers an exciting opportunity to contribute to one of the nation\u2019s leading colleges of pharmacy while working collaboratively with faculty, students, and healthcare professionals across multiple instructional sites. The primary responsibility of this position is to provide instruction and support for the Doctor of Pharmacy (Pharm.D.) curriculum. The Pharm.D. program includes didactic instruction, small-group learning, skills-based education, laboratory teaching, and experiential learning components. The third professional year of the curriculum is delivered synchronously across multiple campuses, creating opportunities for innovative and collaborative teaching approaches The successful candidate will contribute to the development, coordination, delivery, and assessment of coursework and educational activities within the professional curriculum. This position carries a significant level of autonomy and offers opportunities to collaborate with interdisciplinary faculty and instructional teams committed to educational excellence. Additional Requirements Degree preparation must support instruction within the Doctor of Pharmacy (Pharm.D.) curriculum and related educational activities. Candidates whose qualifications do not include a terminal degree customarily associated with the Lecturer rank must meet University requirements for consideration of a terminal degree exception, when applicable, and must be approved for a terminal degree exception before hire. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Professional licensure, certification, or credentials relevant to the teaching discipline, when applicable. Record of academic, clinical, professional, or educational accomplishments supporting success in a teaching-focused faculty role. Evidence of teaching, coordinating, or supporting content within a Doctor of Pharmacy (Pharm.D.) or other healthcare professional curriculum. Evidence of collaborating with interdisciplinary faculty, healthcare professionals, and students in a team-based educational environment. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Demonstrated ability to teach effectively in professional, graduate, health sciences, pharmacy, or related academic settings. Demonstrated ability to develop, coordinate, deliver, and assess academic coursework and educational programs. Knowledge of active-learning, team-based learning, simulation-based instruction, laboratory teaching, or other student-centered instructional methodologies. Demonstrated ability to contribute effectively within academic, healthcare, clinical, research, or interprofessional environments. Evidence of commitment to student learning, academic excellence, and continuous quality improvement of educational programs. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively in written, verbal, and instructional settings. Physical Demands Duties are performed primarily in classroom, laboratory, office, and meeting environments. Requires extended periods of standing, sitting, speaking, and computer use. Requires the ability to move between instructional and administrative locations. May require occasional lifting or transporting educational materials and equipment weighing up to 25 pounds. May require travel between College of Pharmacy instructional locations and University facilities as needed. Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Instruction and Course Coordination Develop, coordinate, deliver, and assess instruction within the Doctor of Pharmacy (Pharm.D.) curriculum. Provide didactic, laboratory, skills-based, and small-group instruction in assigned courses across the professional curriculum. Develop and maintain course materials, examinations, learning activities, and assessment tools that support student learning and achievement of curricular outcomes. Collaborate with faculty and instructional teams in the planning, delivery, and continuous improvement of team-taught courses. Assess student performance, provide academic feedback, and participate in curriculum assessment and accreditation-related activities as needed. Percentage Of Time 90 Duties/Responsibilities Service and Academic Citizenship Participate in departmental, college, and university committees, workgroups, and governance activities. Contribute to accreditation, assessment, student support, and other service initiatives that advance the educational mission of the College of Pharmacy and the University of Georgia. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Other Documents #1 Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/508244": {"title": "Associate Professor or Professor in the area of AI Systems and Causal Reasoning", "description": "University of Georgia | Associate Professor or Professor in the area of AI Systems and Causal Reasoning Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Associate Professor or Professor in the area of AI Systems and Causal Reasoning Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, submit the following: 1. Cover letter 2. Curriculum vitae 3. Statement of research interests and contributions 4. Statement of teaching philosophy and experience 5. Names and contact information for at least three references. Letters will only be requested for shortlisted candidates. Applications received by November 13, 2026 will receive full consideration, but review will continue until the position is filled. For questions about the position, contact Dr. Ting Zhang (tingzhang@uga.edu), Head of Department of Statistics and Dr. Prashant Doshi (pdoshi@uga.edu), Director of IAI. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2830P Working Title Associate Professor or Professor in the area of AI Systems and Causal Reasoning Department Franklin-Statistics About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Department of Statistics is a growing and vibrant department of 34 faculty within the Franklin College of Arts and Sciences at the University of Georgia. The Department offers B.S., M.S., and Ph.D. degrees in Statistics; B.S. and M.S. degrees in Data Science; and an online M.S. in Applied Data Science. The Department has a strong and growing research profile, with faculty conducting theoretical, methodological, computational and applied research across a broad range of areas. In addition to making foundational contributions to the field of statistics, our faculty also collaborate broadly across disciplines, with a strong and successful record of securing multidisciplinary research funding. Additional information is available at the Department of Statistics website at https://stat.uga.edu . The Institute for Artificial Intelligence ( IAI ) is a separate, interdisciplinary research and instructional unit managing the A.B. in Cognitive Science and two graduate AI degree programs housing nearly 300 students. The M.S. in AI is one of the oldest such programs in the country. The Ph.D. in AI was approved in 2022. The interdisciplinary nature of AI and Cognitive Science is reflected in the mission and composition of the Institute. Eight faculty with full or partial appointments with the Institute and more than a hundred affiliated faculty members who come from several departments and colleges across UGA offer an exceptional environment to collaborate. More details about IAI can be found on its website at https://ai.uga.edu . The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The College has a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation. College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/05/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, submit the following: 1. Cover letter 2. Curriculum vitae 3. Statement of research interests and contributions 4. Statement of teaching philosophy and experience 5. Names and contact information for at least three references. Letters will only be requested for shortlisted candidates. Applications received by November 13, 2026 will receive full consideration, but review will continue until the position is filled. For questions about the position, contact Dr. Ting Zhang (tingzhang@uga.edu), Head of Department of Statistics and Dr. Prashant Doshi (pdoshi@uga.edu), Director of IAI . Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank (Tenure Track) Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track or Tenured Minimum Qualifications Applicants should hold a Ph.D. in Statistics, Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, or a related field. Position Summary The Department of Statistics and the Institute for Artificial Intelligence ( IAI ) at the University of Georgia ( UGA ) invite applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor in the area of AI Systems and Causal Reasoning. The expected start date of the position is August 1, 2027. This is a joint position between the Department of Statistics and IAI , with the Department of Statistics serving as the tenure home. Additional Requirements Candidates for Associate Professor or Professor rank with tenure must have qualifications and academic credentials that are commensurate with promotion and tenure guidelines at UGA and must be approved for tenure upon appointment before hire. The guidelines are found at https://provost.uga.edu/faculty-affairs/promotion-tenure/ . Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies We seek an accomplished scholar whose research lies at the intersection of statistics and artificial intelligence, with an interest in advancing the statistics and computation of causal reasoning for AI systems. The successful candidate is expected to have a strong background in both statistics and artificial intelligence, with a research track record demonstrating significant contributions, or strong promise of significant contributions, to both fields. Relevant research may encompass mathematical, statistical, or computational foundations of artificial intelligence. In addition to high-quality publications, the successful candidate is expected to have an established record of external research funding and demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/508191": {"title": "Associate Research Scientist in Cancer Therapeutics and Chemical Biology", "description": "University of Georgia | Associate Research Scientist in Cancer Therapeutics and Chemical Biology Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Associate Research Scientist in Cancer Therapeutics and Chemical Biology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications received by November 4, 2026, will receive full consideration; review will begin on that date and continue until the position is filled. Required materials include a cover letter describing relevant qualifications and research interests, a curriculum vitae, and contact information for three references. Letters of recommendation may be requested later in the search process. For questions about the position, contact Dr. Jin Xie at jinxie@uga.edu . Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2831P Working Title Associate Research Scientist in Cancer Therapeutics and Chemical Biology Department Franklin-Chemistry About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The Department of Chemistry and Franklin College have a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation. College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 11/15/2026 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/05/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications received by November 4, 2026, will receive full consideration; review will begin on that date and continue until the position is filled. Required materials include a cover letter describing relevant qualifications and research interests, a curriculum vitae, and contact information for three references. Letters of recommendation may be requested later in the search process. For questions about the position, contact Dr. Jin Xie at jinxie@uga.edu . Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Researcher AC FLSA Faculty Rank Associate Research Scientist Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Applicants must hold a Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in cancer biology, immunology, pharmacology, chemical biology, biomedical sciences, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Position Summary The Department of Chemistry in the Franklin College of Arts and Sciences at the University of Georgia invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Associate Research Scientist. This is a 12-month appointment in Athens, Georgia, with an anticipated start date in November 2026. The successful candidate will work with Dr. Jin Xie and collaborating investigators to advance cancer therapeutic development, immunotherapy, and translational chemical biology. The successful candidate will lead the preclinical evaluation of new cancer therapeutics and combination strategies designed to enhance antitumor immunity. Responsibilities include designing and conducting in vitro, three-dimensional tumor organoid, and in vivo studies; evaluating therapeutic mechanisms, efficacy, dosing, pharmacodynamic responses, and treatment resistance; and applying appropriate xenograft, orthotopic, metastatic, syngeneic, and patient-derived xenograft models. The position will provide scientific leadership for research supported by two NIH grants and one Department of Defense grant, including experimental planning, data analysis and interpretation, troubleshooting, manuscript preparation, grant-related reporting, and coordination of research milestones. The appointee will contribute to the Department\u2019s broader chemical biology program by connecting chemical and nanomaterial innovation with mechanistic biology and therapeutic evaluation. Responsibilities also include developing collaborative projects with investigators at UGA , Emory University, and the University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill; generating preliminary data and preparing competitive grant applications; and serving as principal investigator, co-investigator, or other key personnel, as appropriate. The successful candidate will mentor graduate students and other trainees in cancer biology, tumor immunology, organoid and animal models, molecular imaging, and quantitative assessment of therapeutic response while ensuring compliance with institutional research and animal-use requirements. Additional Requirements Applicants must possess qualifications appropriate for appointment at the Associate Research Scientist rank. For more information about rank requirements, please see the UGA Guidelines for the Appointment and Promotion of Research Scientists: https://research.uga.edu/docs/policies/research/Research-Scientist-Appointment-Promotion.pdf . Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Candidates must demonstrate the ability to independently design, execute, and interpret mechanistic and preclinical cancer studies; proficiency in conducting in vitro cancer assays and in vivo tumor-model studies; a record of peer-reviewed publications in relevant research areas; scientific leadership in externally funded research; and trainee mentoring. Competitive applicants will demonstrate expertise in cancer immunotherapy, tumor organoid culture, and advanced mouse tumor models; the ability to integrate molecular imaging and pharmacokinetic/pharmacodynamic approaches into therapeutic evaluation; and a record of contributions to successful grant proposals and interdisciplinary research. Expertise in immune profiling, immune-checkpoint therapy, and targeted or nanoparticle-based cancer therapeutics is preferred. Strong scientific writing, quantitative analysis, project coordination, and communication skills are essential. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/508125": {"title": "Clinical Assistant Professor", "description": "University of Georgia | Clinical Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Clinical Assistant Professor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates should upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a clinical experiences and interests statement (as Other Documents #1), and a teaching experiences and interests statement. Candidates will also be asked to provide the names and email for three references who can provide letters of recommendation. References will be contacted later in the search process. Applications received by November 1, 2026 will receive full consideration, but review will continue the position is filled. For questions about the position, contact Cindy Suveg ( csuveg@uga.edu ), chair of the search committee. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2824P Working Title Clinical Assistant Professor Department Franklin-Psychology About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Department of Psychology has approximately 45 faculty members, 90 doctoral students, and approximately 2100 undergraduate Psychology majors. The Clinical Psychology Program has approximately 10 faculty and 35 graduate students. The department is committed to promoting the careers of junior faculty. Athens is well known for its quality of life, affordable cost of living, and easy access to both outdoor and urban activities ( www.visitathensga.com ; exploregeorgia.org ) It is an excellent place to relocate for those of all ages. The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The College has a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation. College/Unit/Department website http://www.psychology.uga.edu/clinic Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/30/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Candidates should upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, a clinical experiences and interests statement (as Other Documents #1), and a teaching experiences and interests statement. Candidates will also be asked to provide the names and email for three references who can provide letters of recommendation. References will be contacted later in the search process. Applications received by November 1, 2026 will receive full consideration, but review will continue the position is filled. For questions about the position, contact Cindy Suveg ( csuveg@uga.edu ), chair of the search committee. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Clinical Assistant Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Clinical Assistant Professor Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Successful candidates will have a PhD or PsyD in clinical or counseling psychology from an APA\u2010accredited program. Position Summary The Department of Psychology at the University of Georgia invites applications for a full-time, non-tenure-track Clinical Assistant Professor to join our clinical psychology Ph.D. training program. This position offers an exceptional opportunity for a psychologist who is passionate about supervision, clinical practice, mentorship, and teaching and who is seeking a rewarding, long-term career training the next generation of psychologists within a collaborative university environment. The successful candidate will play a central role in the training mission of the department\u2019s in-house Psychology Clinic ( http://www.psychology.uga.edu/clinic ), providing supervision and mentorship to doctoral students delivering evidence-based assessment and intervention services to children, adolescents, young adults, and families. Opportunities to offer specialized clinical services are also available, depending on the candidate\u2019s interests. The Clinical Assistant Professor will also teach clinically relevant and general psychology courses at the undergraduate and graduate levels, providing opportunities to contribute to the education and professional development of students across multiple stages of training. The position is designed to support a sustainable and rewarding clinical-academic career, with a Monday-Friday schedule. The University of Georgia also allows faculty to engage in up to one day per week of outside activities allowing the successful candidate to maintain or expand direct clinical practice or consulting activities alongside their teaching and supervision responsibilities if desired. The successful candidate will join a nationally prominent and productive faculty and department interested in promoting the careers of junior faculty. The Clinical Psychology Program has a clinical science model and is dually accredited by APA and the Psychological Clinical Science Accreditation System ( PCSAS ). Additional Requirements The candidate will be licensed or license\u2010eligible to practice in the State of Georgia. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Candidates should have a demonstrated record of conducting psychoeducational assessment and providing evidence-based clinical assessment and intervention. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? Yes Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Other Documents #1 Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/508122": {"title": "Clinical Assistant Professor in Special Education", "description": "University of Georgia | Clinical Assistant Professor in Special Education Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Clinical Assistant Professor in Special Education Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications received by November 18, 2026 are assured of full consideration. Applicants should submit all the following: A letter of interest that addresses the qualifications specified above and clearly describes the applicant\u2019s a) teaching philosophy, b) preparation, experience, and interests in higher education instruction, and c) areas of expertise in special education A curriculum vitae Names and contact information for three professional references will be collected as part of the application system. Letters of reference may be requested directly through the application system as part of the search process. Finalists will be unable to schedule an on-campus interview until all three letters have been received Unofficial Transcripts (official transcripts will be required from finalists) Questions may be addressed to the search committee chair, Dr. Georgette Morgan, at georgette.morgan@uga.edu. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2822P Working Title Clinical Assistant Professor in Special Education Department COE-Comm Sciences & Special Ed About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department As the 4th largest public college of education in the country and the 3rd largest college at UGA , the Mary Frances Early College of Education ( MFE COE ) improves the lives of residents of Georgia and beyond through our instruction, research, and service. The MFE COE is a comprehensive college with disciplines focused on teacher preparation, counseling and human development, communication sciences, human movement sciences, career development, student affairs, and educational administration and policy. We place significant emphasis on graduate education with approximately 40% of our students at the graduate level, making us the second largest college at UGA with respect to graduate education. The Special Education ( EDSE ) program prepares students at the undergraduate and graduate levels across a range of degree programs, including general curriculum, adapted curriculum, birth through kindergarten, and applied behavior analysis. The program also supports students across the College through coursework focused on foundational knowledge of special education and the effective inclusion of students with disabilities in educational settings. More information about the department can be found at www.coe.uga.edu/csse . Athens is known for its music, art, and food as well as its accessibility to the Atlanta area (see www.visitathensga.com and http://www.georgia.gov/ ). College/Unit/Department website https://coe.uga.edu/directory/communication-sciences-and-special-education/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/02/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/02/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications received by November 18, 2026 are assured of full consideration. Applicants should submit all the following: A letter of interest that addresses the qualifications specified above and clearly describes the applicant\u2019s a) teaching philosophy, b) preparation, experience, and interests in higher education instruction, and c) areas of expertise in special education A curriculum vitae Names and contact information for three professional references will be collected as part of the application system. Letters of reference may be requested directly through the application system as part of the search process. Finalists will be unable to schedule an on-campus interview until all three letters have been received Unofficial Transcripts (official transcripts will be required from finalists) Questions may be addressed to the search committee chair, Dr. Georgette Morgan, at georgette.morgan@uga.edu. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Clinical Assistant Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Clinical Assistant Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications An earned doctorate (Ph.D. or equivalent) in special education or a related field by the start date Position Summary The Department of Communication Sciences and Special Education at the University of Georgia invites applications for the position of Clinical Assistant Professor in Special Education, beginning in August 2027. The Special Education ( EDSE ) program prepares students at the undergraduate and graduate levels across a range of degree programs, including general curriculum, adapted curriculum, birth through kindergarten, and applied behavior analysis. The program also supports students across the College through coursework focused on foundational knowledge of special education and the effective inclusion of students with disabilities in educational settings. This position requires teaching the equivalent of four courses per semester in the program or college and delivering both face-to-face and online instruction. The candidate\u2019s teaching assignment will include the preparation of both special education and non-special education teachers, including coursework related to foundational knowledge of special education and inclusive practices, as well as supervision of special education students in field-based experiences. The area of specialization is otherwise open. A valid driver\u2019s license and reliable transportation are required. The appointment will be for the 2027-28 academic year, beginning August 1, 2027. This position is contingent upon the availability of funding. Additional Requirements At least three years of teaching experience in P-12 schools in special education as a fully certified teacher. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Required Qualifications: Evidence of promise of teaching undergraduate and/or graduate courses and mentoring students Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Preferred Qualifications: Specialization in mathematics instruction for students with disabilities Prior role supervising preservice teachers in field-based placements Current knowledge of evidence-based practices and professional standards for teacher preparation, including those established by the Council for Exceptional Children ( CEC ). Physical Demands Driving as needed to perform job duties. Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? Yes Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses (face-to-face, online, and/or blended) and mentor and advise students, as assigned Instruct and supervise students in P\u201312 school-based field experiences, both in person and virtually Engage in departmental, college, university, and professional service Comply with university, regulatory, and accreditation agency standards Percentage Of Time 100 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/508051": {"title": "Assistant Professor - Speech-Language Pathology", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant Professor - Speech-Language Pathology Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant Professor - Speech-Language Pathology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications will require all of the following: A letter of application specifically responsive to the position\u2019s responsibilities, required qualifications, and preferred qualifications, as described above. This should include clear descriptions of the applicant\u2019s a) program of research, b) preparation, demonstrated success, and/or future plans for pursuing external funding; and c) experiences and interests in teaching. A complete curriculum vitae Unofficial copies of all undergraduate and graduate transcripts Names and contact information for three professional references will be collected as part of the application system. The application system will contact the listed references directly and provide them with instructions for submitting their letters through the system. Finalists will be unable to schedule an on-campus interview until all three letters have been received. Applications received by November 3, 2026 are assured of full consideration. Questions may be addressed to the search committee chair Dr. Hannah Krimm, hannah.krimm@uga.edu. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2821P Working Title Assistant Professor - Speech-Language Pathology Department COE-Comm Sciences & Special Ed About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Mary Frances Early College of Education ( MFE COE ), one of the nation\u2019s largest colleges of education, consistently ranks in the top ten national Elementary Education and Curriculum and Instruction programs. The College offers significant possibilities for interdisciplinary research collaborations, program development, and school-community partnerships. The college\u2019s Research Office provides strong pre- and post-award grant support. The College is named for the University of Georgia\u2019s first African American graduate, a pioneering educator who played an integral role in the campaign for racial equality in Georgia and across the South. The department and college are recognized leaders in developing partnerships with local communities and schools to provide pre-service and in-service professional development, and to expand students\u2019 experiential learning and service-learning opportunities. As the 4th largest public college of education in the country and the 3rd largest college at UGA , the Mary Frances Early College of Education ( MFE COE ) improves the lives of residents of Georgia and beyond through our instruction, research, and service. The MFE COE is a comprehensive college with disciplines focused on teacher preparation, counseling and human development, communication sciences, human movement sciences, career development, student affairs, and educational administration and policy. We place significant emphasis on graduate education with approximately 40% of our students at the graduate level, making us the second largest college at UGA with respect to graduate education. The Communication Sciences and Disorders program offers a bachelor\u2019s degree, a CAAaccredited master\u2019s degree, an educational specialist degree, a pre-professional speechlanguage pathology certificate program, and a research doctorate degree. The program is part of an interdisciplinary department within a college that includes a range of health, clinical, professional, and educational programs. More information about the department can be found at www.coe.uga.edu/csse . As a Research I university, UGA provides an exceptional environment for interdisciplinary collaboration and innovation. Shared research resources available to investigators include the Bioimaging Research Center, the Center for Teaching and Learning, the Institute for Artificial Intelligence, and numerous core facilities that support advanced research across the biomedical, engineering, agricultural, and social sciences. These resources foster cutting edge scholarship and facilitate collaborations that accelerate scientific discovery and translation. Athens is known for its music, art, and food as well as its accessibility to the Atlanta area (see www.visitathensga.com and http://www.georgia.gov/ ). College/Unit/Department website https://coe.uga.edu/directory/communication-sciences-and-special-education/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/02/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/02/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications will require all of the following: A letter of application specifically responsive to the position\u2019s responsibilities, required qualifications, and preferred qualifications, as described above. This should include clear descriptions of the applicant\u2019s a) program of research, b) preparation, demonstrated success, and/or future plans for pursuing external funding; and c) experiences and interests in teaching. A complete curriculum vitae Unofficial copies of all undergraduate and graduate transcripts Names and contact information for three professional references will be collected as part of the application system. The application system will contact the listed references directly and provide them with instructions for submitting their letters through the system. Finalists will be unable to schedule an on-campus interview until all three letters have been received. Applications received by November 3, 2026 are assured of full consideration. Questions may be addressed to the search committee chair Dr. Hannah Krimm, hannah.krimm@uga.edu. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Assistant Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications An earned doctorate (Ph.D. or equivalent) in speech-language pathology or closely related field (or degree to be awarded before the position\u2019s start date). Position Summary The Department of Communication Sciences and Special Education invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor with expertise in Speech-Language Pathology. The area of specialization in speech-language pathology is open, with a preference for a scholar with expertise in one or more of the following areas: speech disorders, AAC , or dysphagia. This is an academic year (9 month) full-time tenure-track position to begin Fall semester 2027. Additional opportunities for summer employment may be available. Additional Requirements Required Qualifications include all of the following: Evidence of high-quality scholarly research, including peer-reviewed journal articles and professional presentations commensurate with experience. Evidence or strong potential for seeking and attracting external funding. Evidence of potential may include success with small-scale proposals, training and preparation for seeking external funds, and research into high-interest areas for funding sources. Evidence or the promise of successful teaching at the university level. A record of collaborative, professional interactions or service supporting students, the institution, or the discipline. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Research and teaching expertise in one of the following clinically relevant areas: speech disorders, AAC , dysphagia. Certificate of Clinical Competence ( CCC - SLP ). Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? Yes Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Develop and sustain a line of research that contributes to scientific advancement in an area related to communication and/or swallowing disorders. Actively pursue external funding for research. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses (face-to-face, online, and/or blended). Advise students and direct thesis and dissertation research. Engage in departmental, college, university, and professional service. Other related assignments Percentage Of Time 100 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/CV Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/508006": {"title": "Associate Professor/Professor of Innovation and Technology for Translational Research in Biomedicine", "description": "University of Georgia | Associate Professor/Professor of Innovation and Technology for Translational Research in Biomedicine Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Associate Professor/Professor of Innovation and Technology for Translational Research in Biomedicine Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicant screening will begin immediately. The application packet should include a curriculum vitae, a cover letter addressing how the applicant\u2019s credentials and experience meet the responsibilities and qualifications of the position and contact information for at least three (3) professional references. Please note that references will only be contacted with applicant\u2019s prior consent. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2828P Working Title Associate Professor/Professor of Innovation and Technology for Translational Research in Biomedicine Department SOM-Research About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The University of Georgia School of Medicine was founded in 2024 and received preliminary accreditation in 2026. The establishment of a new public medical school at UGA comes as the state faces a significant shortage of medical professionals. The population of Georgia, the nation\u2019s eighth-largest state, has surged to approximately 11 million residents, straining existing medical infrastructure and resulting in longer wait times for appointments and reduced access to care. Georgia currently ranks 39th in the nation for the number of active patient care physicians per capita and 41st for the number of public medical students per capita. As a top-20 public university with a thriving research enterprise and vast public service network, the University of Georgia is well-positioned to produce more highly trained physicians, alleviate physician shortages, and improve the state\u2019s ability to provide quality health care for its citizens. The School of Medicine is located on UGA\u2019s Health Sciences Campus in Athens. In its inaugural year, the UGA School of Medicine will enroll 60 students per class, but a new $100 million medical school building will enable the UGA School of Medicine to grow to 120 students per class in the future. College/Unit/Department website https://medicine.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Salary is commensurate with education, experience, and achievements. Anticipated Start Date 01/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/01/2026 Job Closing Date 11/04/2026 Open until filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Applicant screening will begin immediately. The application packet should include a curriculum vitae, a cover letter addressing how the applicant\u2019s credentials and experience meet the responsibilities and qualifications of the position and contact information for at least three (3) professional references. Please note that references will only be contacted with applicant\u2019s prior consent. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank (Tenure Track) Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Minimum Qualifications: Earned PhD or equivalent terminal degree in a field relevant to digital health, artificial intelligence, biomedical informatics, engineering, environmental health sciences, communication science, behavioral science, public health, or related discipline. Position Summary The BRIDGE Center Director and Translational Research Faculty Member serves as a senior scientific leader within the planned School of Medicine\u2019s Institute for Multidisciplinary Translational Medicine ( MTM Institute), and holds a joint faculty appointment between the School of Medicine and the Grady College of Journalism and Mass Communication providing strategic vision and leadership for the advancement of translational biomedical research. This position is responsible for establishing and sustaining an internationally recognized, externally funded research program that leverages emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence (AI), robotics, biomedical wearables, sensors, digital biomarkers, immersive virtual environments, and multimodal data analytics to accelerate scientific discovery and improve human and animal health outcomes through a One Health framework. The incumbent directs the BRIDGE Center and is expected to secure extramural funding for the center, lead multidisciplinary research initiatives, expand environmental health sciences research capacity, foster collaborations across academic, clinical, community, government, and industry partners, and support the successful renewal and/or growth of center funding. The position requires leadership of complex research programs and teams, development of a translational research infrastructure, management of scientific cores and pilot programs, oversight of budgets and compliance activities, and promotion of innovative approaches that bridge laboratory discoveries to clinical, veterinary, and community applications. As a senior faculty member at tenure-track rank of Associate Professor or Professor, the individual contributes to the School of Medicine\u2019s and Grady College of Journalism and Mass Communication\u2019s educational mission through mentoring students, trainees, and junior faculty, developing educational programs in translational science, biomedical informatics, responsible AI, digital health, and environmental health sciences, and fostering the next generation of physician-scientists and biomedical researchers. The position also provides leadership, strengthens partnerships and shared resources, and represents the BRIDGE Center to federal agencies, university leadership, and external stakeholders. Additional Requirements Additional Requirements: History of serving as Principal Investigator or Multi-PI on federally funded research grants. Minimum of 5 years of progressively responsible research leadership experience For information regarding requirements for faculty ranks, please see the University of Georgia Guidelines for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Knowledge of artificial intelligence, machine learning, predictive analytics, data science, and multimodal data integration. Knowledge of biomedical wearables, sensors, digital biomarkers, robotics, human-robot interaction, immersive technologies, and emerging healthcare innovations. Strategic leadership success in building, leading, and advancing large-scale research centers, interdisciplinary initiatives, and high-performing multidisciplinary teams. Demonstrated ability to develop and sustain collaborative partnerships across academic, healthcare, government, industry, community, and other stakeholder groups. Demonstrated success in grant development and securing extramural funding from federal, foundation, and industry sources. Ability to manage multiple priorities, deadlines, budgets, compliance requirements, and complex administrative responsibilities. Excellent strategic, organizational, and communication skills with the ability to develop innovative research initiatives and align emerging technology, data science, and translational research activities with institutional priorities. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/507989": {"title": "Open Rank", "description": "University of Georgia | Open Rank Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Open Rank Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should upload: A cover letter describing their research agenda and teaching philosophy; A curriculum vitae; and A list of references with contact information. Three letters of reference addressed to the University of Georgia School of Social Work Faculty Search Committee will be required at the time of interview. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questionsmay be directed to Dr. Hee Yun Lee, Search Committee Chair, at heeyunlee@uga.edu. Pleaseinclude \u201cFaculty Search\u201d in the subject line. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2820P Working Title Open Rank Department Social Work-Dean's Office About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The University of Georgia is the state\u2019s flagship institution of higher education and a Carnegie-classified research university located in Athens, Georgia. The School of Social Work serves more than 500 students through its CSWE -accredited B.S.W. and M.S.W. programs, Ph.D. program, and Master of Nonprofit Management and Leadership program. The School also offers joint M.S.W. degree programs with the School of Law, the College of Public Health, and the Terry College of Business through its M.B.A. program. Nationally and internationally recognized for excellence in research, teaching, public service, and international programs, the School of Social Work is committed to hiring faculty who work toward advancing social and economic disparities through scholarship/research, teaching, public service and/or administrative responsibilities. College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Minorities & Females Advertised Salary Commensurate with Experience Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/28/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should upload: A cover letter describing their research agenda and teaching philosophy; A curriculum vitae; and A list of references with contact information. Three letters of reference addressed to the University of Georgia School of Social Work Faculty Search Committee will be required at the time of interview. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Questionsmay be directed to Dr. Hee Yun Lee, Search Committee Chair, at heeyunlee@uga.edu. Pleaseinclude \u201cFaculty Search\u201d in the subject line. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track or Tenured Minimum Qualifications A Ph.D. in social work or cognate discipline (e.g. psychology, sociology, public health, neuroscience, economics). Position Summary The University of Georgia School of Social Work invites applications for one tenure-track faculty position at the rank of assistant, associate, or full professor. The successful candidate will hold a joint appointment in the School of Social Work and the newly established School of Medicine. We seek a scholar who will establish and lead an externally funded program of human-subjects research focused on the design, evaluation, implementation, and scaling of evidence-based digital interventions and clinical decision-support tools for prevention, treatment, and recovery. Areas of inquiry may include digital therapeutics; mobile- and web-based interventions; conversational agents for psychoeducation, screening, or triage; EHR -enabled measurement-based care; sensors and other digital biomarkers; and recovery platforms that connect individuals with treatment, peer support, and harm-reduction resources. The successful candidate may employ rigorous and responsible artificial intelligence methods, including natural language processing, predictive modeling, risk stratification, relapse forecasting, recommender systems, and just-in-time adaptive interventions, to improve early detection, treatment engagement, care coordination, and sustained recovery. Related areas of research may include artificial intelligence (AI)-assisted clinical documentation and workflow optimization, digital phenotyping, integration of multimodal clinical and patient-reported data, and safe and transparent clinical decision support. The joint appointment will create opportunities for close collaboration with clinical, behavioral, and data science investigators in the School of Medicine while advancing a Social Work research agenda focused on community-based implementation, behavioral health equity, practice integration, recovery-oriented care, and the ethical and responsible use of digital technologies and AI. Teaching responsibilities may include undergraduate and graduate courses in digital behavioral health, SUD and co-occurring conditions, implementation science, research methods, and the ethical and equitable delivery of digitally enabled care. The faculty member will also contribute to the development of new curricula, certificates, and short courses that translate emerging research and technologies into practice-ready competencies. The successful candidate will mentor students and trainees across social work, public health, medicine, nursing, informatics, and data science programs and support interdisciplinary research and career development. The faculty member will also be expected to build and sustain partnerships with hospitals, federally qualified health centers, health departments, community-based organizations, and peer-led recovery programs. Through these partnerships, the faculty member may co-design, pilot, implement, and evaluate digital interventions and lead dissemination activities that produce practical resources such as implementation toolkits, train-the-trainer materials, and evaluation dashboards. The successful candidate will join an exceptionally talented and committed community of scholars and staff. Opportunities for collaboration within the School of Social Work include the Center for Human Trafficking Research & Outreach; the Center for Social Justice, Human and Civil Rights; and the Institute for Nonprofit Organizations. Across the University, faculty collaborate with colleagues in the College of Pharmacy, College of Public Health, newly established College of Nursing, College of Engineering, College of Family and Consumer Sciences, Mary Frances Early College of Education, and School of Law. Additional opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration are available through the Owens Institute for Behavioral Research, the Institute for Artificial Intelligence, and other university centers and institutes. Faculty are expected to engage in teaching, research, field liaison duties and/or academic advising, and service. They may teach across the educational continuum at our Athens, Gwinnett, and Online campuses. The successful candidate is expected to share the University and School\u2019s commitment to excellence in teaching, research, service, and engagement. Additional Requirements Candidates for the Assistant Professor rank must have a Ph.D. in social work or cognate discipline (e.g. psychology, sociology, public health, neuroscience, economics). Candidates for the Associate Professor rank must also be engaged in teaching, research, and service consistent with an appointment at the rank of associate professor. Candidates for the Professor rank must also be engaged in teaching, research, and service consistent with a tenured faculty appointment at the rank of a tenured professor. Tenure on appointment must be approved before hire, the faculty member must be appointed as an associate or full professor, must have already been tenured at a prior institution, and must bring a demonstrable national reputation to the institution. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification An M.S.W. degree with two years post master\u2019s practice experience strongly preferred but not required. We welcome applications from strong candidates in two areas: (1) Digital Mental Health and (2) Digital Behavioral Health for Substance Use Disorder ( SUD ). Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies The candidate selected for this faculty position will be an outstanding scholar and teacher. Applicants must demonstrate exceptional research capacity and potential for external funding. We welcome applications from scholars whose research advances digital behavioral health, withparticular attention to substance use disorders ( SUD ), co-occurring mental health conditions,and recovery across the lifespan. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Serve as instructor for courses in the BSW , MSW , and/or PhD programs and teach undergraduate and graduate courses in digital mental health, SUD science, co-occurring conditions, implementation methods, and research ethics and equity in digital care; and develop new curricula and short courses that translate emerging evidence into practice-ready skills, and serve as student advisor. Percentage Of Time 45 Duties/Responsibilities Engage in independent research agenda in areas of human-subjects research that advances digital mental health across the lifespan, and develop, evaluate, and scale digital behavioral health tools. Disseminate findings and pursue external funding as appropriate and available. Percentage Of Time 45 Duties/Responsibilities Provide service to the School, university, community, and profession. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/507966": {"title": "Lecturer in Chemistry", "description": "University of Georgia | Lecturer in Chemistry Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Lecturer in Chemistry Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. For full consideration, applicants must submit: (1) a cover letter summarizing the applicant\u2019s scientific background, strengths, interests, and teaching experience; (2) a curriculum vitae; and (3) a teaching statement of no more than 2 pages describing the applicant\u2019s approach to effective teaching and providing either evidence of teaching effectiveness or specific examples of how they would implement their approach in the classroom. Optional: applicants may also include or append representative teaching materials, such as an assignment, activity, assessment, or set of instructional slides, that further illustrate their approach to teaching; this document should be no more than 5\u20138 pages. Applicants should provide contact information for three references. Letters of recommendation will be requested after immediately and will be used in the review. Applications received by November 15, 2026, will receive full consideration, but review will continue until the position is filled. Informal inquiries and questions may be addressed to the chair of the search committee at Chemistry-LecturerSearch@uga.edu Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2826P Working Title Lecturer in Chemistry Department Franklin-Chemistry About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The College has a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation. College/Unit/Department website https://www.franklin.uga.edu/chemistry Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/01/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants For full consideration, applicants must submit: (1) a cover letter summarizing the applicant\u2019s scientific background, strengths, interests, and teaching experience; (2) a curriculum vitae; and (3) a teaching statement of no more than 2 pages describing the applicant\u2019s approach to effective teaching and providing either evidence of teaching effectiveness or specific examples of how they would implement their approach in the classroom. Optional: applicants may also include or append representative teaching materials, such as an assignment, activity, assessment, or set of instructional slides, that further illustrate their approach to teaching; this document should be no more than 5\u20138 pages. Applicants should provide contact information for three references. Letters of recommendation will be requested after immediately and will be used in the review. Applications received by November 15, 2026, will receive full consideration, but review will continue until the position is filled. Informal inquiries and questions may be addressed to the chair of the search committee at Chemistry-LecturerSearch@uga.edu Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Lecturer FLSA Faculty Rank Lecturer Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications The successful applicant will have earned a PhD in Chemistry by the start date. Position Summary The Department of Chemistry at the University of Georgia in Athens, GA invites applications for multiple Lecturer positions. The positions are non-tenure accruing and begin August 1, 2027. Lecturers will teach in the Department\u2019s General Chemistry and/or Organic Chemistry Course sequence and participate in service to the Department, School, and University. Active participation in departmental activities, maintaining a collegial work environment, and professional development are expected. Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies The successful applicant will have a background teaching in both large and small classes utilizing active learning pedagogy. Excellent oral, written and interpersonal communication skills are essential. Strong applicants will have the ability to utilize technology in teaching. Competitive applicants will demonstrate: (1) evidence of effective teaching in a variety of instructional settings, including the use of active and inclusive teaching practices; (2) the ability to effectively integrate instructional technology into teaching; (3) the ability and willingness to work collaboratively in coordinated courses and curriculum improvement efforts; and (4) strong communication skills and engagement in ongoing professional development related to teaching and learning. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Other Documents #1 Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/507868": {"title": "Assistant Professor in Industrial-Organizational Psychology", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant Professor in Industrial-Organizational Psychology Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant Professor in Industrial-Organizational Psychology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please upload each of the following as a separate document: a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a research statement, a teaching statement, and up to three sample publications. Applicants will also be asked to provide contact information for three references as part of their application; letters of recommendation will be requested later in the search process. Applications received by November 1, 2026 will receive full consideration, but review will continue until the position is filled. For questions about the position, contact Dr. Steve Beach (srhbeach@uga.edu), chair of the search committee. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2825P Working Title Assistant Professor in Industrial-Organizational Psychology Department Franklin-Psychology About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Department of Psychology has approximately 45 faculty members, 90 doctoral students, and approximately 2,100 undergraduate Psychology majors. Athens is well known for its quality of life, affordable cost of living, and easy access to both outdoor and urban activities (www.visitathensga.com; exploregeorgia.org). It is an excellent place to relocate for those of all ages. The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The College has a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation. College/Unit/Department website www.uga.edu/psychology Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/01/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Please upload each of the following as a separate document: a cover letter, a curriculum vitae, a research statement, a teaching statement, and up to three sample publications. Applicants will also be asked to provide contact information for three references as part of their application; letters of recommendation will be requested later in the search process. Applications received by November 1, 2026 will receive full consideration, but review will continue until the position is filled. For questions about the position, contact Dr. Steve Beach (srhbeach@uga.edu), chair of the search committee. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Assistant Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Candidates should hold a PhD in Industrial-Organizational Psychology or a related field (e.g., organizational behavior, organizational science, or management) by the start of the appointment. Position Summary The Department of Psychology at the University of Georgia ( www.uga.edu/psychology ) invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Industrial-Organizational Psychology, to begin Fall 2027. The successful candidate will contribute to the Program and Department\u2019s teaching and mentoring needs at both the undergraduate and graduate levels. Area of research is open, though we are especially interested in candidates whose substantive or methodological expertise would extend the program\u2019s strengths, and an ability to collaborate with current faculty would be seen as a positive. The successful candidate will join a nationally prominent and productive research faculty and department that is committed to promoting the careers of junior faculty. Collaboration within the department and across the University is encouraged Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Competitive candidates will have an established and strong record of research commensurate with career stage with potential for external funding. Candidates with a demonstrable ability to build partnerships with emerging or established research centers and units on campus (including the medical and nursing schools, the Institute for Artificial Intelligence, or other campus partners) will receive particular attention. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Sample Publications Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/507867": {"title": "Visiting Limited-Term Assistant Professor", "description": "University of Georgia | Visiting Limited-Term Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Visiting Limited-Term Assistant Professor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three letters of reference, and a teaching portfolio (including descriptions of three to four potential courses). Applications received by December 1, 2026 will receive full consideration, and the position will remain open until filled. Inquiries should be addressed to the committee chair Dr. Aaron Rubin (aaron.rubin@uga.edu). Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F-PT/LT02221P Working Title Visiting Limited-Term Assistant Professor Department Franklin-Religion About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The College has a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/01/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications should include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, contact information for three letters of reference, and a teaching portfolio (including descriptions of three to four potential courses). Applications received by December 1, 2026 will receive full consideration, and the position will remain open until filled. Inquiries should be addressed to the committee chair Dr. Aaron Rubin (aaron.rubin@uga.edu). Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Limited Term Faculty (EX) FLSA Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Contract Type None (position not eligible for annual contract) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications A Ph.D. degree. Position Summary The Department of History and Department of Religion at the University of Georgia invites applications for a one-year Visiting Limited-Term Assistant Professor of Jewish History, renewable for up to two additional years. The anticipated start date is August 1, 2027. This position will be a joint appointment in the Departments of History and Religion, with an undergraduate teaching load of four courses per academic year (two per semester). The successful candidate will be expected to develop new course offerings that expand the Jewish Studies curriculum, as well as to assist with student and public event planning. Additional Requirements Advanced Ph.D. candidates must be approved for a terminal degree exception before hire. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies The successful candidate should have a documented record of teaching and an ability to offer courses in diverse areas, including, but not limited to fields such as American Jewish History (of any period), Global Jewish History, Holocaust Studies, Jewish migration, Modern Judaism, and Jewish-Christian Relations. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/507735": {"title": "Assistant Dean for Faculty Affairs", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant Dean for Faculty Affairs Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant Dean for Faculty Affairs Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application materials should include: Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover letter describing how the applicant\u2019s qualifications and experience meet the responsibilities and qualifications of the position Contact information for three (3) professional references. Please note that references will only be contacted with applicant\u2019s prior consent. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2765P Working Title Assistant Dean for Faculty Affairs Department SOM-Academic Affairs About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The University of Georgia School of Medicine was founded in 2024 and received preliminary accreditation in 2026. The establishment of a new public medical school at UGA comes as the state faces a significant shortage of medical professionals. The population of Georgia, the nation\u2019s eighth-largest state, has surged to approximately 11 million residents, straining existing medical infrastructure and resulting in longer wait times for appointments and reduced access to care. Georgia currently ranks 39th in the nation for the number of active patient care physicians per capita and 41st for the number of public medical students per capita. As a top-20 public university with a thriving research enterprise and vast public service network, the University of Georgia is well-positioned to produce more highly trained physicians, alleviate physician shortages, and improve the state\u2019s ability to provide quality health care for its citizens. The School of Medicine is located on UGA\u2019s Health Sciences Campus in Athens. In its inaugural year, the UGA School of Medicine will enroll 60 students per class, but a new $100 million medical school building will enable the UGA School of Medicine to grow to 120 students per class in the future. College/Unit/Department website https://medicine.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Academic rank and salary will be commensurate with the qualifications and experience of the selected candidate. Anticipated Start Date 04/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/30/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Application materials should include: Curriculum Vitae (CV) Cover letter describing how the applicant\u2019s qualifications and experience meet the responsibilities and qualifications of the position Contact information for three (3) professional references. Please note that references will only be contacted with applicant\u2019s prior consent. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Assoc/Asst Dean AC FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications MD, DO, PhD, or other terminal degree in a health professions or related field. Position Summary The Assistant Dean for Faculty Affairs is a key leadership role within the UGA School of Medicine ( UGA SOM ). This position provides professional support and guidance to SOM faculty across three interrelated domains: faculty affairs and academic advancement, faculty well-being, and career success. Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Established record of providing consultation and guidance to faculty and academic leaders regarding promotion, tenure, career progression, performance improvement, and professional development. Knowledge of faculty affairs policies, procedures, and best practices in academic medicine and higher education, including promotion, tenure, and academic advancement processes. Exceptional interpersonal and relationship-building skills with the ability to establish credibility and trust with faculty, department chairs, senior leadership, and administrative partners. Strong consultation, coaching, and advising skills to support faculty career development, advancement, and professional success. Ability to collaborate effectively across departments, disciplines, and administrative units to achieve institutional goals. Commitment to promoting faculty well-being, engagement, and belonging. Ability to use data and assessment measures to evaluate program effectiveness and recommend continuous improvements. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Faculty Onboarding In coordination with UGA SOM Department Chairs and Human Resources, manage and update annually a welcoming, comprehensive onboarding experience for newly appointed faculty that facilitates early success and connection to the UGA SOM community. Develop and maintain standardized onboarding protocols, orientation materials, and a new faculty career success series tailored to the UGA SOM context Serve as an important point of contact for new faculty during their initial appointment period, connecting them to institutional policies, resources, and key personnel Develop/revise the UGA SOM faculty handbook and other website resources Collaborate with Department Chairs, Human Resources, and administrative offices to ensure timely credentialing and completion of institutional requirements Solicit and act on feedback from new faculty to continually improve the onboarding experience Academic Advancement and Promotion In collaboration with the department chairs, advise faculty at all ranks on promotion pathways, forms, systems, timelines, criteria, and portfolio preparation in accordance with UGA SOM and UGA policies Provide individual consultations to faculty at critical career junctures including onboarding, pre-promotion, CV review, scholarship development, career challenges, and intent-to-leave conversations Provide workshops or other mechanisms to support faculty in building competitive promotion packets Provide timely updates to faculty regarding available promotion and tenure development opportunities at UGA Be a conduit to the UGA Faculty Offices to clarify or mediate any promotion/tenure applications Provide advocacy for faculty career opportunities both inside and outside the UGA SOM Faculty Well-Being Champion programs and initiatives that sustain faculty engagement, belonging, and well-being across all career stages. Foster a culture of faculty recognition by celebrating achievements, milestones, and contributions to the school\u2019s mission Partner with UGA SOM Office of Personalized Health & Well Being and UGA Office of Faculty Affairs to promote wellness activities and resources to ensure faculty have access to well-being support and community Faculty Success Career Services Serve as a resource to UGA SOM HR, Department Chairs, and faculty members to help faculty members develop habits and behaviors for career success and help them manage career obstacles: Coordinate mentorship pairing and peer integration to promote early engagement and belonging Use data to monitor success of the mentorship and revise as needed Provide faculty vitality programming including career development workshops, leadership development, and mid- and late-career resources Coordinate with HR on exit interviews and use data from interviews to inform improvements to increase faculty retention In coordination with Office of UME , Office of GME , Assistant Dean of Faculty Development, and Department Chairs, develop and promote programs that support the engagement and success of volunteer adjunct clinical faculty Offer Unit level mediation services and conflict resolution support to faculty members Advise the SOM Dean, Department Chairs and HR on USG , UGA and UGA SOM on updated faculty policies, particularly when addressing academic productivity, timelines and behaviors With the SOM Department Chairs and HR, analyze collated reports on faculty success milestones including professionalism, advancement, promotion/tenure, productivity and significant achievements; report these periodically to the Dean and faculty Serve as an ad hoc (non-voting) member of the Faculty Honors and Awards Committee Offer faculty success educational programming that includes best practices and habits for career success Provide professionalism education programming for faculty, including content on communication, conflict resolution, and inclusive professional conduct Serve as a resource and advisor to Department Chairs on early identification of struggling faculty and best practices for improvement Other Lead LCME accreditation work for standards involving faculty affairs issues Collaborate with offices responsible for evaluation and continuous quality improvement to measure program effectiveness Percentage Of Time 100 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/507714": {"title": "Academic Professional", "description": "University of Georgia | Academic Professional Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Academic Professional Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Prospective candidates should submit the following in electronic form: a cover letter that addresses the minimum and preferred qualifications for this position, a curriculum vita, a recent publication or research-related writing sample, a teaching portfolio, transcripts, and a list of three letter writers, who will separately provide letters of recommendation (in electronic form). Questions can be sent to Bill Zachmann, Administrative Specialist/Office Manager, Department of International Affairs, University of Georgia, 219 Candler Hall, Athens, GA 30602 ( zachmann@uga.edu ). Applications received by November 9, 2026 will receive full consideration. Review will continue until position is filled. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2823P Working Title Academic Professional Department SPIA-International Affairs About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Department of International Affairs is home to faculty with expertise across comparative politics, international relations, and area studies, including a growing concentration of scholars who focus on the Middle East. The Department plays a central role in SPIA\u2019s efforts to build interdisciplinary academic and co-curricular programming on Israel and the Middle East, in coordination with the Franklin College of Arts and Sciences\u2019 Jewish Studies program. For more information about the Department and the School of Public and International Affairs, visit our website. College/Unit/Department website http://spia.uga.edu/department-of-international-affairs/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/29/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Prospective candidates should submit the following in electronic form: a cover letter that addresses the minimum and preferred qualifications for this position, a curriculum vita, a recent publication or research-related writing sample, a teaching portfolio, transcripts, and a list of three letter writers, who will separately provide letters of recommendation (in electronic form). Questions can be sent to Bill Zachmann, Administrative Specialist/Office Manager, Department of International Affairs, University of Georgia, 219 Candler Hall, Athens, GA 30602 ( zachmann@uga.edu ). Applications received by November 9, 2026 will receive full consideration. Review will continue until position is filled. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Academic Professional AC FLSA Faculty Rank Academic Professional Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in political science, the study of Israel, or the study of the Middle East by August 1, 2027. Position Summary The Department of International Affairs in the UGA School of Public and International Affairs ( SPIA ) seeks a colleague for a new position at the Academic Professional rank. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching, mentor students, and collaborate across departments, programs, and research centers, including the University\u2019s Jewish Studies-related curricular and co-curricular initiatives. In particular, candidates who can build academic and co-curricular programming in the politics of Israel and the Middle East, direct independent studies and undergraduate research, and represent the University to public and professional audiences in this field are encouraged to apply. Additional Requirements Substantive expertise in Israeli politics and society, including the ways in which culture, history, or identity intersect with politics in Israel and the Middle East. Hebrew language proficiency and direct experiences in Israel, the Middle East, and North Africa. The Academic Professional rank emphasizes teaching, outreach, and program development over traditional research metrics alone; requirements for appointment and review at this rank are outlined here: https://provost.uga.edu/wp-content/uploads/appointment-promotion-guidelines-academic-professionals.pdf Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification A research and publication record that spans both the cultural/historical dimensions of Israeli national identity and contemporary Israeli foreign policy and regional diplomacy. We welcome applications from candidates whose scholarship and teaching combine research on contemporary Israeli foreign policy and regional diplomacy with grounding in the cultural and historical dimensions of Israeli national identity, and who bring direct experiences from Israel, the Middle East, and North Africa. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies The Department invites applications from a non-traditional social scientist with substantive expertise at the intersection of politics, state, and society in Israel and the broader Middle East, and whose training bridges political science with humanistic approaches to the study of Israel and the region. Preferred qualifications include: Demonstrated ability to teach and mentor undergraduate students, including in courses on Israeli politics, Israeli culture, the history of Zionism, U.S.-Israel political relations, and Middle Eastern politics. Demonstrated record for program-building and public scholarship at the intersection of politics and culture in Israel and the Middle East. Demonstrated success developing and leading study abroad. Evidence of community and donor engagement related to Israel and Middle East studies. Potential to create synergies with existing UGA departmental, school, and University faculty, including the Franklin College of Arts and Sciences\u2019 Jewish Studies program. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Writing Sample Unofficial Transcripts List of References with Contact Information Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Other Documents #1 Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/507405": {"title": "Business Consultant-Savannah", "description": "University of Georgia | Business Consultant-Savannah Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Business Consultant-Savannah Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The cover letter should address the following: Our employees say empathy\u2014an understanding of and service to others\u2014is important in their role at the SBDC. In your letter, please describe instances where empathy is evidenced in your work and discuss why you are interested in supporting the mission and culture of our organization. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2814P Working Title Business Consultant-Savannah Department PSO-Small Business Dev Center About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary $80,000 Anticipated Start Date 12/01/2026 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/24/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants The cover letter should address the following: Our employees say empathy\u2014an understanding of and service to others\u2014is important in their role at the SBDC . In your letter, please describe instances where empathy is evidenced in your work and discuss why you are interested in supporting the mission and culture of our organization. Location of Vacancy Savannah Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Public Service Professional AC FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications A master\u2019s degree in business or a related field. A bachelor\u2019s degree is acceptable for a Public Service Provisional appointment (see Additional Requirements for more information on this provisional appointment). Position Summary The University of Georgia Small Business Development Center seeks an experienced, results-driven management professional with strong business skills to serve the Savannah area as a Business Consultant . If you\u2019re ready to apply your business expertise in a role that supports Georgia\u2019s economic growth, we encourage you to. A Small Business Development Center ( SBDC ) Business Consultant is a public service faculty position responsible for providing counseling and delivering programs to individuals, businesses, communities, organizations, and other public agencies in their assigned geographic territory. As a Business Consultant, you\u2019ll work directly with business owners to provide expert guidance in areas such as financial analysis, business planning, marketing strategy, and operations management. You\u2019ll also develop and lead educational programs tailored to the needs of the local business community. This position is located in Savannah, Georgia. Multi-county travel is required. Additional Requirements See the University of Georgia Guidelines for Appointments and Promotions for Public Service and Outreach Academic Rank for information regarding the Public Service Faculty ranks. Progression towards earning an advanced degree is expected while in a provisional faculty position. When a public service professional receives an advanced degree, recommendation for a public service faculty appointment can be initiated according to the public service faculty appointment process (see \u201cAppointment and Promotion upon Receiving an Advanced Degree\u201d on page 17 of the Guidelines ). Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification A master\u2019s degree is preferred. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies This charge requires a broad base of business knowledge, excellent analytical skills, and effective management of multiple projects simultaneously. Knowledge of University and SBDC programs and operating philosophy and/or relevant management background preferred. Strong knowledge of core business functions (finance, marketing, operations). Excellent communication and project management skills. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Provide high quality individual instruction and educational support to entrepreneurs, business owners, and business managers. Analyze situations, make recommendations, and educate clients with regard to business plans, market feasibility, financial viability, operations management, and legal structures, to name but a few topics. Maintain an appropriate level and mix of clients as noted by annual goals and strategic plan objectives. Responsible for developing and refining a consulting practice that yields impactful results. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Develop and deliver high quality business training programs that are responsive to the needs of the business community served. Generate curricula for business programs, seminars, conferences, etc. for the local business interests. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Determine and initiate, topics, agendas, instructors, instructional materials, location, time and other resources required. Create and produce instructional materials. Serve as an instructor of business training programs and secure qualified outside instructors, as needed. Effectively market business training programs within assigned communities, so as to meet annual goals. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities In addition to maintaining a broad base of business knowledge, develop specific and relevant area(s) of expertise within the arena of business development. Apply this knowledge through development and delivery of new training programs, consulting tools, research projects, co-consulting and/or other impact measures. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Direct clients to other appropriate sources of business information and assistance. Disseminate pertinent information to the business community via various media. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Serve as an advocate of business development, expansion and retention in the area, thereby becoming a visible leader in the local business community. Work collaboratively with private-sector businesses, other economic development assistance units of the University System, and other units of State Government to further the economic well-being of Georgia\u2019s citizens. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Engage in public relations activities such as, speeches, presentations, active committee participation, and direct discussions. Relevant audiences include bankers, colleges and universities, chambers of commerce, economic development authorities, downtown development organizations, government agencies, local political offices, civic organizations, local media and potential program sponsors. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Assist in the continued development, implementation, and updating of the organization\u2019s strategic plan. Ensure that organizational goals and objectives are accomplished in a timely and thorough manner. Work with colleagues to develop and deploy annual action and marketing plans that align with the organizational strategic plan, are tailored to meeting the specific small business needs within the assigned geography, and capitalize on the skills of SBDC personnel. Prepare and execute individual work plans, including professional development initiatives, which align with area office objectives. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Support organizational improvement efforts through active involvement with internal committees, center reviews, special projects, and various assessments as directed by the state office. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Actively participate in the development and execution of sponsorship acquisition strategies in support of area office and state goals. Initiate co-sponsorship of programs with private businesses, economic development organizations, and other government entities. Seek and apply for grants relevant to entrepreneurship and business development. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Document activities via electronic information system (Unity) in a timely, accurate, and comprehensive manner. Maintain client files as per SBA and SBDC guidelines. Provide impact information for required SBA reporting including but not limited to success stories. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Perform all responsibilities efficiently and effectively within assigned area office. Ensure that administrative policies are followed, that programs are innovative and responsive, and that top quality services are delivered. Utilize client and management feedback in striving for continuous improvement. Maintain positive, professional relations with other institutions. Represent the Area Director when required Percentage Of Time Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/507375": {"title": "Associate Professor or Professor in Genetics, Synthetic Biology, and Biological Engineering", "description": "University of Georgia | Associate Professor or Professor in Genetics, Synthetic Biology, and Biological Engineering Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Associate Professor or Professor in Genetics, Synthetic Biology, and Biological Engineering Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications must include: 1) cover letter, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) statement of research interests and goals (up to 2 pages), and 4) a combined teaching and mentoring statement (up to 2 pages), which should integrate ideas and efforts that support UGA\u2019s values and enrich our missions of teaching, research, and service ( https://uga.edu/about/mission ). Candidates should also submit names and contact information for three references. The search committee will contact references after the initial screening of applications. Applications received by November 1, 2026 will receive full consideration, but review will continue until the position is filled. Informal inquiries and questions may be addressed to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Kelly Dawe ( kdawe@uga.edu ) or the Head of Genetics, Dr. Kelly Dyer ( kdyer@uga.edu ). Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2819P Working Title Associate Professor or Professor in Genetics, Synthetic Biology, and Biological Engineering Department Franklin-Genetics About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Department of Genetics is a highly collaborative community with broad strengths spanning genetics, epigenetics, genomics, and molecular, computational, and evolutionary biology. Faculty benefit from extensive university resources in genomics, bioinformatics, high-performance computing, microscopy, and other advanced technologies, as well as opportunities for collaboration across the life sciences, agriculture, engineering, data science, and artificial intelligence. The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The College has a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation. College/Unit/Department website https://www.genetics.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/25/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications must include: 1) cover letter, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) statement of research interests and goals (up to 2 pages), and 4) a combined teaching and mentoring statement (up to 2 pages), which should integrate ideas and efforts that support UGA\u2019s values and enrich our missions of teaching, research, and service ( https://uga.edu/about/mission ). Candidates should also submit names and contact information for three references. The search committee will contact references after the initial screening of applications. Applications received by November 1, 2026 will receive full consideration, but review will continue until the position is filled. Informal inquiries and questions may be addressed to the chair of the search committee, Dr. Kelly Dawe ( kdawe@uga.edu ) or the Head of Genetics, Dr. Kelly Dyer ( kdyer@uga.edu ). Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track or Tenured Minimum Qualifications Applicants must have a Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in genetics, genomics, biology, computational biology, bioengineering, or a related discipline. Position Summary The Department of Genetics at the University of Georgia invites applications for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor, beginning August 1, 2027. Candidates at the advanced Assistant Professor level who are poised for promotion to Associate Professor are also encouraged to apply. Successful candidates will be expected to establish or maintain an internationally recognized, externally funded research program; contribute to the intellectual community of the Department of Genetics; mentor graduate students and postdoctoral researchers; participate in undergraduate and graduate education; and engage in collaborative research across the University of Georgia. Additional Requirements Candidates for appointment with tenure must have a record of research, scholarship, teaching, and professional achievement commensurate with appointment at the Associate Professor or Professor level at the University of Georgia. Advanced Assistant Professors should demonstrate a trajectory consistent with promotion to Associate Professor. Candidates must have qualifications and academic credentials that are commensurate with the promotion and tenure guidelines at the University of Georgia and must be approved for tenure upon appointment before hire. These guidelines can be found at https://provost.uga.edu/faculty-affairs/promotion-tenure/ . Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies We seek an outstanding scientist whose work advances fundamental understanding of biological systems using genetic, genomic, evolutionary, molecular, computational, or quantitative approaches, and has the potential to inform applications in synthetic biology, biotechnology, or biological engineering. Research programs using any appropriate experimental or computational system are welcome. Candidates need not identify primarily as synthetic biologists or engineers. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/507372": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Religion", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant Professor of Religion Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant Professor of Religion Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should upload a CV, cover letter, teaching statement, one writing sample, and contact information for three references. Letters of reference and other supporting materials may be requested from a smaller pool of applicants at a later date. Applications received by November 9, 2026 will receive full consideration. Review will continue until the position is filled. For questions about the search, contact the Chair of the Search Committee, Dr. Ingie Hovland, at ingiehovland@uga.edu. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2818P Working Title Assistant Professor of Religion Department Franklin-Religion About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Department of Religion, housed in the Franklin College of Arts and Sciences, offers undergraduate majors and minors as well as MA and PhD programs in religion. Additional information is available at https://religion.uga.edu . The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The College has a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation. College/Unit/Department website https://religion.uga.edu. Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/25/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should upload a CV, cover letter, teaching statement, one writing sample, and contact information for three references. Letters of reference and other supporting materials may be requested from a smaller pool of applicants at a later date. Applications received by November 9, 2026 will receive full consideration. Review will continue until the position is filled. For questions about the search, contact the Chair of the Search Committee, Dr. Ingie Hovland, at ingiehovland@uga.edu. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Assistant Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Candidates must hold a PhD or equivalent terminal degree in religion, religious studies, or a closely related field by the position\u2019s start date. Position Summary The Department of Religion at the University of Georgia invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Religion specializing in religion, ethics, and politics, with an anticipated start date of August 1, 2027. The successful candidate will maintain an active research program in which religion is central and will teach courses addressing the relationships among religion, ethics, and politics. The position carries a 2/2 teaching load and includes regular responsibility for a large-enrollment Religious Ethics course of approximately 150 to 300 students. Other responsibilities include mentoring graduate students; contributing to curricular and program development; and participating in departmental, college, university, and professional service. Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Competitive applicants will demonstrate a coherent research agenda centered on religion and its ethical and political dimensions; evidence of effective college-level teaching; the ability to teach a large-enrollment Religious Ethics course; and the capacity to contribute to the department\u2019s undergraduate and graduate programs. Demonstrated engagement with methods or theories from humanities or social sciences will strengthen an application, although candidates with other academic backgrounds will be considered. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Writing Sample Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/507177": {"title": "Director of Trial Advocacy", "description": "University of Georgia | Director of Trial Advocacy Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Director of Trial Advocacy Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please note that successful applicants are responsible for ensuring their eligibility to work in the United States (i.e., a citizen or national of the United States, a lawful permanent resident, a foreign national authorized to work in the United States without need of employer sponsorship) on or before the effective date of your appointment, and maintain eligibility without sponsorship throughout your appointment. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2817P Working Title Director of Trial Advocacy Department Law School-General About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Commensurate with Experience Anticipated Start Date 01/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/24/2026 Job Closing Date 10/30/2026 Open until filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Please note that successful applicants are responsible for ensuring their eligibility to work in the United States (i.e., a citizen or national of the United States, a lawful permanent resident, a foreign national authorized to work in the United States without need of employer sponsorship) on or before the effective date of your appointment, and maintain eligibility without sponsorship throughout your appointment. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Academic Professional AC FLSA Faculty Rank Academic Professional Associate Contract Type Law Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications J.D. from an ABA -accredited law school. Position Summary The Director of Trial Advocacy leads the School of Law\u2019s trial advocacy program and mock trial competition team. The position oversees advocacy competitions, student development, program operations, and strategic initiatives that enhance the program\u2019s reputation under the supervision of the Director of Advocacy who oversees both the Trial and Appellate Advocacy Programs. The Director teaches trial advocacy and related experiential courses while developing curriculum that prepares students for litigation and dispute-resolution practice. The Director collaborates with faculty, practitioners, and alumni to provide training and experiential learning opportunities. The Director also contributes to the School of Law through committee service and alumni engagement. The position requires the Director to work frequent evenings and weekends during the academic year. Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification 3 years of experience in legal practice or litigation/courtroom experience. Demonstrated success in trial advocacy coaching, teaching, or competition leadership. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Coaching and mentoring skills. Ability to develop experiential learning opportunities for law students. Ability to build consensus among faculty, coaches, alumni, and advocacy students. Exceptional oral advocacy and courtroom presentation skills. Strong written communication and legal writing skills. A background in trial advocacy pedagogy and experiential legal education. Knowledge of Law School advocacy competition formats and judging standards. Budget management and strategic planning skills. Physical Demands Ability to travel for competitions (nationally) Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Administration of the Law School\u2019s Trial Advocacy Program Manage program operations, budgets, competition funding, and resource allocation. Develop long-term strategies to enhance the national reputation and visibility of the trial advocacy program in coordination with the Director of Advocacy. Direct and oversee mock trial, trial advocacy, and other advocacy competition programs. Recruit, select, train, and mentor student competitors. Coordinate participation in regional and national advocacy competitions. Support student professional development, leadership growth, and career placement opportunities related to litigation and advocacy practice. Recruit, train, and evaluate adjunct faculty, volunteer attorneys, judges, alumni, and competition coaches who support advocacy programming. Foster and support alumni engagement. Percentage Of Time 50 Duties/Responsibilities Instruction of School of Law Courses Instruct School of Law Courses in trial advocacy and other litigation-focused or experiential subjects. Develop an advocacy curriculum that prepares students for courtroom and dispute-resolution practice. Percentage Of Time 40 Duties/Responsibilities Service Serve on Law School or campus-related committees. Support accreditation, assessment, and reporting activities related to experiential education. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/507175": {"title": "Limited-Term Instructor", "description": "University of Georgia | Limited-Term Instructor Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Limited-Term Instructor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications should include the following: 1. Cover Letter 2. Curriculum Vitae 3. Three References with Contact Information This position is open until filled. For questions about the position, please contact Dr. Belinda Stillion Southard, search committee chair at bss@uga.edu. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F-PT/LT02208P Working Title Limited-Term Instructor Department Franklin-Communication Studies About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The College has a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation. College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 01/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/24/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications should include the following: 1. Cover Letter 2. Curriculum Vitae 3. Three References with Contact Information This position is open until filled. For questions about the position, please contact Dr. Belinda Stillion Southard, search committee chair at bss@uga.edu. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Limited Term Faculty (EX) FLSA Faculty Rank Instructor Contract Type None (position not eligible for annual contract) Tenure Status Minimum Qualifications M.A. or PhD in Communication Studies or related discipline by the time of appointment. Position Summary The Department of Communication Studies at the University of Georgia invites applications for a Limited-Term Instructor of Communication Studies to begin in January 2027. The course load is up to 12 credit hours per semester, primarily focusing on COMM 1110, Introduction to Public Speaking and/or COMM 1500, Introduction to Interpersonal Communication. Responsibilities include teaching and monitoring students. Limited-term faculty may be renewed annually for a maximum of two years. Any request for reappointment beyond the second year requires pre-approval by the Provost. Additional Requirements At least two years of college-level public speaking teaching experience. Candidates must be currently legally eligible to work in the United States. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies The successful candidate is expected to demonstrate excellence in college level teaching and possess specialized knowledge in public speaking and/or interpersonal communication. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/507087": {"title": "Limited Term Clinical Instructor &amp; Internal Medicine PGY4 Chief Resident", "description": "University of Georgia | Limited Term Clinical Instructor &amp; Internal Medicine PGY4 Chief Resident Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Limited Term Clinical Instructor & Internal Medicine PGY4 Chief Resident Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The application packet should include a curriculum vitae, Program Director recommendation letter, and USMLE/COMLEX transcript (please use Other Documents #1 & #2 for the letter and transcript). Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F-PT/LT02213P Working Title Limited Term Clinical Instructor & Internal Medicine PGY4 Chief Resident Department SOM-GME About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The University of Georgia School of Medicine was founded in 2024 and received preliminary accreditation in 2026. The establishment of a new public medical school at UGA comes as the state faces a significant shortage of medical professionals. The population of Georgia, the nation\u2019s eighth-largest state, has surged to approximately 11 million residents, straining existing medical infrastructure and resulting in longer wait times for appointments and reduced access to care. Georgia currently ranks 39th in the nation for the number of active patient care physicians per capita and 41st for the number of public medical students per capita. As a top-20 public university with a thriving research enterprise and vast public service network, the University of Georgia is well-positioned to produce more highly trained physicians, alleviate physician shortages, and improve the state\u2019s ability to provide quality health care for its citizens. The School of Medicine is located on UGA\u2019s Health Sciences Campus in Athens. In its inaugural year, the UGA School of Medicine will enroll 60 students per class, but a new $100 million medical school building will enable the UGA School of Medicine to grow to 120 students per class in the future. College/Unit/Department website https://medicine.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Commensurate with experience Anticipated Start Date 07/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) 06/30/2028 Job Posting Date 09/23/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants The application packet should include a curriculum vitae, Program Director recommendation letter, and USMLE / COMLEX transcript (please use Other Documents #1 & #2 for the letter and transcript). Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Limited Term Clinical Faculty (EX) FLSA Faculty Rank Clinical Instructor Contract Type None (position not eligible for annual contract) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Minimum Qualifications MD, DO, or equivalent degree is required because of the role as a Chief Resident and patient care in the Internal Medicine Residency Program. Position Summary The PGY4 Chief Resident assists the Program Director in the administration of the Internal Medicine Residency Program, development of curriculum, and participates in academic didactic conferences as a moderator and mentor. The position involves supervision of residents, assessing and addressing resident morale, and direct patient care duties including precepting residents and medical students in the residents\u2019 clinic. This position offers enormous possibilities for developing and enhancing clinical, teaching, and administrative skills, leadership ability, and personal growth. During the academic year, the PGY4 Chief Resident develops his/her personal leadership style, learns the complexities of conflict negotiation and resolution, and gains skills involved in administration, management, and pedagogy. The position is a one-year, non-tenure track appointment at the rank of clinical instructor and offers a unique blend of education, patient care, and administration. Additional Requirements Additional Requirements Will have successfully completed an ACGME accredited categorical Internal Medicine Residency Program Certified or eligible for American Board of Internal Medicine ( ABIM ) Board Certification in Internal Medicine or one of its subspecialties Possess or be able to obtain an unrestricted license to practice medicine in the State of Georgia Possess or be able to obtain appropriate hospital credentials and privileges Possess or be able to obtain an unrestricted Drug Enforcement Administration License Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Broad knowledge base Desire for medical education Superb presentation skills Commitment to collaboration Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? Yes Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities The PGY4 Chief Resident is responsible for assisting Program Administration in the supervision and education of residents of the Internal Medicine Residency Program. The PGY4 Chief Resident assists Program Administration in academic and career mentoring for each resident and supports the continued accreditation of the program through application of ACGME Common and Specialty Requirements. Responsibilities include but not limited to: Prepare, organize, and teach at didactic conferences for the Internal Medicine Residency Program Provide patient care for patients in the residency clinic, Community Internal Medicine of Athens Provide supervision, teaching, and mentorship for residents and medical students Serve as a role model for residents and medical students Attend program committee meetings after normal business hours Attend various academic and professional society conferences Percentage Of Time 100 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Other Documents #1 Other Documents #2 Optional Documents Cover Letter Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/507031": {"title": "Lecturer", "description": "University of Georgia | Lecturer Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Lecturer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications received by October 15, 2026, are assured full consideration. However, applications will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Interested candidates should upload their cover letter, curriculum vita, teaching evaluations, and contact information for three references (including email addresses).\u00a0 Applications submitted in other ways will not be considered. References will be contacted at the appropriate time during the search process. Please address any questions about the position to the search committee chair, Professor Charles Lyons (cwl@uga.edu). Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2800P Working Title Lecturer Department Terry-Management About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The University of Georgia is the first public-chartered university in the nation, and the Terry College is the state\u2019s flagship business school, with undergraduate, full-time MBA , professional MBA , and executive MBA programs consistently ranked among the top 20 public universities. The Terry College is housed in new, state-of-the-art facilities. To learn more about the University, College, Department, and specific programs, please visit https://www.terry.uga.edu/departments/management/ . Athens, Georgia is generally regarded as one of the best college towns in the United States. It is nicknamed \u201cThe Classic City\u201d because of its architecture and vibrant music, art, and food scene. Athens is located about 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with affordable real estate prices and a low cost of living. College/Unit/Department website https://www.terry.uga.edu/departments/management/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/14/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications received by October 15, 2026, are assured full consideration. However, applications will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Interested candidates should upload their cover letter, curriculum vita, teaching evaluations, and contact information for three references (including email addresses).\u00a0 Applications submitted in other ways will not be considered. References will be contacted at the appropriate time during the search process. Please address any questions about the position to the search committee chair, Professor Charles Lyons (cwl@uga.edu). Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Lecturer FLSA Faculty Rank Lecturer Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications A Ph.D. in Management or related area. See Additional Requirements for alternative credentials. Position Summary The Department of Management in the Terry College of Business at the University of Georgia invites applications for a full time, non-tenure track faculty position at the lecturer level starting August 2027. We seek individuals who can provide high-quality instruction at the undergraduate and MBA levels within the general management area with broad teaching interests in principles of management, human resources management, leadership, ethics, or strategy as well as other topics, as needed. The successful candidate will also be proactively involved in departmental service and undergraduate or master student mentoring. The position may be renewed annually, contingent on performance, and promotion to Senior Lecturer is possible after six years of service. Compensation is competitive. Additional Requirements If not terminally degree qualified, at a minimum, a Master\u2019s degree is required with 5 or more years of private- or public-sector work experience in management or related areas. Candidates with a master\u2019s degree must document exceptional accomplishments in management or a related area and must be approved for a terminal degree exception before hire. For information regarding the requirements for each faculty rank, please see the University of Georgia Guidelines for Appointment and Promotion of Lecturers Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Candidates with a Ph.D. in Management or related areas are preferred. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Evidence of a successful teaching record is required in the form of student surveys/evaluations, peer evaluations, or annual reviews; research is not a consideration. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/CV Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/507027": {"title": "E. Garrard Hall Professor in Early Childhood Education", "description": "University of Georgia | E. Garrard Hall Professor in Early Childhood Education Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits E. Garrard Hall Professor in Early Childhood Education Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit: Letter of application Curriculum Vitae Five recent publications, combined and uploaded as one PDF Contact information for five references. References will not be contacted until the candidate, if a finalist, has been notified. All materials should be submitted electronically via this application. Applications received by Monday, October 26, 2026 will be assured full consideration, but this position is open until filled. Address questions to the search committee chair, Dr. Kyunghwa Lee ( kyunghwa@uga.edu ). Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2815P Working Title E. Garrard Hall Professor in Early Childhood Education Department COE-Educational Theory & Pract About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department As the 4th largest public college of education in the country and the 3rd largest college at UGA , the MFECOE improves the lives of residents of Georgia and beyond through our instruction, research, and service. The MFE COE is a comprehensive college with disciplines focused on teacher preparation, counseling and human development, communication sciences, human movement sciences, career development, student affairs, and educational administration and policy. We place significant emphasis on graduate education with approximately 40% of our students at the graduate level, making us the second largest college at UGA with respect to graduate education. ETAP has contributed to this stature locally, nationally, and internationally. The department is characterized by critical, forward-thinking research and innovative, dynamic teaching. ETAP is committed to making equity, access, and belonging visible in its courses, programs, policies, and practice. Our outreach and research include a variety of multifaceted collaborations, including those with local school districts and local community-based informal education projects, as well as projects that extend across the state of Georgia, the United States, and a variety of international contexts. The Elementary Education program at UGA , which includes Early Childhood Education, has been ranked among the nation\u2019s top 10 elementary education programs by U.S. News and World Report for more than a decade. Our mission in the Elementary Education program is to blend theory and practice grounded in our shared philosophy of critical pedagogy. Upon program completion, we expect our students to demonstrate teaching competencies related to habits of reflexive practice, integrating scholarship and research, engaging in professional collaboration, and appreciating and supporting multiple backgrounds and perspectives. These elements of thought and action are viewed as key to supporting critically informed and equitable teacher decision-making. The Elementary Education program is designed to offer theoretically and clinically rich experiences in diverse environments. By the end of the program, teachers are prepared to enact these commitments as leaders in their classrooms, schools, and communities. The Elizabeth Garrard Hall Professor will be expected to advance and extend the program\u2019s national and international visibility and reputation by producing high-quality and rigorous research and actively participating in the broad community of scholars in education in general, and early childhood/elementary education in particular. College/Unit/Department website https://coe.uga.edu/directory/educational-theory-and-practice/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/23/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit: Letter of application Curriculum Vitae Five recent publications, combined and uploaded as one PDF Contact information for five references. References will not be contacted until the candidate, if a finalist, has been notified. All materials should be submitted electronically via this application. Applications received by Monday, October 26, 2026 will be assured full consideration, but this position is open until filled. Address questions to the search committee chair, Dr. Kyunghwa Lee ( kyunghwa@uga.edu ). Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenured Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate in early childhood education, elementary education, or a related field. Position Summary The University of Georgia Department of Educational Theory and Practice ( ETAP ) invites applications for the Elizabeth Garrard Hall Professorship in Early Childhood Education. The candidate for this endowed position must be eligible for appointment at the rank of Full Professor at the University of Georgia beginning August 2027 (or a date to be negotiated with the candidate). The successful candidate will conduct high-impact, collaborative research and provide intellectual leadership in the Mary Frances Early College of Education ( MFE COE ) and beyond. The Elizabeth Garrard Hall Professor will receive endowment support to engage in innovative teaching and scholarship, including mentoring graduate students, preparing teachers and other educational professionals, and collaborating with faculty on research related to the mission of the Department of Educational Theory and Practice and the MFE COE . Elizabeth Garrard Hall was an extraordinary Georgia native whose experiences growing up during the Great Depression shaped her into a hardworking, resourceful, and deeply compassionate person. After earning her B.A. in Latin from the UGA College of Arts and Sciences in 1934 and beginning her career as a high school teacher in Fayetteville, GA, she and her husband, a chemist with the Coca-Cola Company, shared a commitment to expanding educational opportunities for young people. Having supported an orphaned child, she later continued this effort by generously helping impoverished children in Haiti. Ms. Hall\u2019s love for education, respect for intellectual curiosity, and innate pragmatism has been honored through this permanent endowment. Additional Requirements Established program of research through strong publications and presentations Record of externally funded research Record of service and leadership in national and international organizations in the field Eligibility for tenure and appointment at the rank of Full Professor in the Department of Educational Theory and Practice Please review the Department of Educational Theory and Practice\u2019s promotion and tenure guidelines and the University of Georgia Guidelines for Appointment, Promotion, and Tenure of Academic Rank Faculty for more information on requirements for tenure and the rank of Professor. Any request for tenure must be approved before hiring. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies We seek an established scholar and leader in early childhood education with expertise in grades PreK-5. The candidate will have a strong, sustained record of research, including outstanding scholarly accomplishments through publications and presentations, as well as an active research agenda that includes developing proposals for external funding and overseeing project implementation. The candidate will also demonstrate a strong record of professional service and leadership within national and international professional organizations in the field. Physical Demands Work is primarily sedentary and performed in an office, classroom, or digital environment. Requires extended periods of sitting, standing, and using standard office equipment and technologies (such as computers and projectors) throughout the workday. May involve occasional movement within campus facilities and the ability to lift or move light materials (e.g., laptops, textbooks, or instructional supplies) weighing up to 25 pounds. Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Sample Publications List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Other Documents #1 Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/506847": {"title": "Clinical Assistant Professor - English Education (LLE)", "description": "University of Georgia | Clinical Assistant Professor - English Education (LLE) Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Clinical Assistant Professor - English Education (LLE) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit: A letter of application specifically responsive to the position responsibilities and qualifications as described above A teaching philosophy statement A complete curriculum vitae The contact information for three persons who will serve as references Official transcripts and letters of recommendation will be required only from finalists. Applications received by October 24, 2026, will be given full consideration. Questions may be directed to the search committee co-chairs, Drs. Jamie Hogan (jjordanhogan@uga.edu) and Ryan Schey (ryanschey@uga.edu). Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2816P Working Title Clinical Assistant Professor - English Education (LLE) Department COE-Language & Literacy Educ About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Mary Frances Early College of Education ( MFE COE ) is committed to promoting diversity in education and society through its Office of Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion, through its research and teaching missions, and through collaborative work with community residents and organizations. It consistently ranks nationally in the top ten Elementary Education and Curriculum and Instruction programs. The excellence of the faculty has enabled the MFE COE to recruit doctoral students nationally and internationally and place them in a variety of prestigious positions following graduation, further enhancing the College\u2019s outstanding reputation around the globe. As the 4th largest public college of education in the country and the 3rd largest college at UGA , the Mary Frances Early College of Education ( MFE COE ) improves the lives of residents of Georgia and beyond through our instruction, research, and service. The MFE COE is a comprehensive college with disciplines focused on teacher preparation, counseling and human development, communication sciences, human movement sciences, career development, student affairs, and educational administration and policy. We place significant emphasis on graduate education with approximately 40% of our students at the graduate level, making us the second largest college at UGA with respect to graduate education. The Department of Language and Literacy Education has contributed to this stature locally, nationally, and internationally. Many faculty collaborate with other MFE COE departments in program development, research partnerships, and other associations. The department has developed programs that meet the University of Georgia\u2019s mission to expand students\u2019 Experiential Learning through service-learning projects, community inquiry programs, summer programs designed to serve the local community, and related initiatives. The faculty have long held leadership roles in national and international organizations dedicated to language and literacy education. Departmental faculty have also developed international collaborations with educators in Russia, Mexico, Columbia, Uzbekistan, Argentina, Chile, Cyprus, and other locations. College/Unit/Department website https://coe.uga.edu/directory/language-and-literacy-education Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Commensurate with Experience Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/22/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit: A letter of application specifically responsive to the position responsibilities and qualifications as described above A teaching philosophy statement A complete curriculum vitae The contact information for three persons who will serve as references Official transcripts and letters of recommendation will be required only from finalists. Applications received by October 24, 2026, will be given full consideration. Questions may be directed to the search committee co-chairs, Drs. Jamie Hogan (jjordanhogan@uga.edu) and Ryan Schey (ryanschey@uga.edu). Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Clinical Assistant Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Clinical Assistant Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications An earned doctorate (Ph.D. or equivalent) in English Education, adolescent literacy, or a related field completed by the start of employment Position Summary The Department of Language and Literacy Education at the University of Georgia invites applications for the position of Clinical Assistant Professor with expertise in the preparation of secondary English Education grades 6-12 teachers. This is a full-time position that begins as early as August 1, 2027. English Education is the discipline responsible for the teaching of composition, literature, other textual forms, and language for secondary-level students (grades 6-12). Responsibilities will include the following, as well as other duties as assigned: Teach undergraduate and graduate courses (face-to-face and/or online) Mentor and advise undergraduate and graduate students Purposefully engage school and community partners Collaborate with English Education faculty in innovative development and redesign of curriculum, particularly in the initial certification of secondary English language arts education teachers across the state of Georgia Engage in departmental, college, university and professional service Additional Requirements Required Qualifications for this position include: An earned doctorate (Ph.D. or equivalent) in English Education, adolescent literacy, or a related field completed by the start of employment A minimum of three years of in-field literacy teaching experience as a fully certified secondary English/Language Arts (Grades 6-12) teacher in school settings Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Experience and Preferred Competencies for this position include: Demonstrated expertise in initial teacher preparation in secondary English/Language Arts (Grades 6-12) within a university setting. Supervision of secondary English/Language Arts (Grades 6-12) teacher candidates in clinical settings Demonstrated professional commitment to centering positive social change and culturally and socially responsive education that can be brought to people, communities, and institutions Three years of in-field literacy teaching experience as a fully certified secondary English/Language Arts (Grades 6-12) teacher in public school settings Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? Yes Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate courses (face-to-face and/or online) Mentor and advise undergraduate and graduate students Collaborate with English Education faculty in innovative development and redesign of curriculum, particularly in the initial certification of secondary English language arts education teachers across the state of Georgia Percentage Of Time 80 Duties/Responsibilities Purposefully engage school and community partners Engage in departmental, college, university, and professional service Percentage Of Time 20 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/506684": {"title": "Assistant Research Scientist", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant Research Scientist Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant Research Scientist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit a cover letter describing their qualifications and research interests, a curriculum vitae, a brief research statement, and contact information for three professional references. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2812P Working Title Assistant Research Scientist Department Franklin-Physics & Astronomy About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The College has a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration, and academic innovation. College/Unit/Department website https://www.physast.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 01/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/21/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit a cover letter describing their qualifications and research interests, a curriculum vitae, a brief research statement, and contact information for three professional references. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Researcher AC FLSA Faculty Rank Assistant Research Scientist Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Applicants should have a Ph.D. in physics, materials science, electrical engineering, chemistry, or a closely related field. Position Summary Research faculty-level position in the Department of Physics and Astronomy at the University of Georgia supporting an active interdisciplinary experimental research program spanning quantum materials, nano/quantum-optics, neuromorphic devices, nano/microfluidics, soft materials, polymers, and liquid-phase spectroscopies. We seek a highly motivated experimental scientist with expertise in one or more areas including nano- and microfluidic device design and fabrication, polymer and soft-material synthesis and device integration, liquid-phase optical and vibrational spectroscopy, nano-optical characterization, and functional materials. The successful candidate will conduct high-level experimental research; develop and implement novel experimental platforms integrating fluidics, materials, devices, and spectroscopy; and maintain and operate advanced instrumentation. Research opportunities include liquid-phase nano-optics and spectroscopy, polymer and soft-material devices, ionically and chemically responsive systems, neuromorphic devices, quantum and strongly correlated materials, and van der Waals materials. The Research Scientist will also contribute to the NSF -funded Quantum Networks Training and Research Alliance in the Southeast (QuaNTRASE), participate in research proposals and publications, and mentor undergraduate and graduate students. The position is particularly suited for a scientist with strong experimental and technical expertise who can work independently while collaborating with faculty, students, and multidisciplinary research teams. Responsibilities include conducting advanced experiments, maintaining research productivity, supporting specialized instrumentation, coordinating research activities, preparing manuscripts and proposals, and providing technical guidance to students. The position is expected to play an important role in sustaining and expanding UGA\u2019s experimental quantum-science program and in strengthening research and student training in emerging quantum and neuromorphic technologies. Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Applicants should have a strong record of experimental research and scholarly publications. Demonstrated ability in one or more of the following areas is particularly desirable: nano-optics and near-field optical microscopy, quantum materials, neuromorphic materials and devices, strongly correlated materials, van der Waals materials, optical spectroscopy, or advanced nanoscale characterization. Demonstrated ability operating and developing sophisticated experimental instrumentation and mentoring graduate or undergraduate researchers is also highly desirable. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/506682": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant Professor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin October 28 th and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2813P Working Title Assistant Professor Department SPIA-Political Science About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Department of Political Science at the University of Georgia offers AB, BS, MA and PhD degrees with specializations in American politics, law and courts, and political theory. Known for the quality of their research, the faculty have published in all major political science journals and with leading university presses, have consistently ranked among the most productive in the nation, and have authored several widely used texts. Department faculty have won every major teaching award offered by the University and several Lilly Teaching Fellowships. College/Unit/Department website https://spia.uga.edu/departments-centers/department-of-political-science/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/21/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin October 28 th and will continue until the position is filled. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Assistant Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in political science before August 2027. Position Summary The Department of Political Science in the UGA School of Public and International Affairs ( SPIA ) seeks a colleague for a new tenure-track position at the Assistant Professor level. The Department invites applications from scholars with substantive interests in any subfield in American politics, political methodology, or theory who also possess a specialization in artificial intelligence (AI). We welcome applications from candidates whose research and teaching inform the use of AI research tools to address questions in their areas of expertise. We also welcome applications from candidates who conduct research that explores the effects of artificial intelligence on the functioning of democracy in the U.S. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching, mentor students, and collaborate across departments and research centers. In particular, candidates who can contribute to the graduate and undergraduate curricula in AI related courses and political methodology are encouraged to apply. Requirements for each rank and tenure are outlined here: https://provost.uga.edu/faculty-affairs/promotion-tenure-evaluation/promotion-and-tenure Additional Requirements Strong research-related skills with scholarly interests in AI and U.S. politics/methodology/theory. Ability to teach and mentor undergraduate and graduate students. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Demonstrated record or potential for excellence in teaching and scholarship Demonstrated record or potential for external funding of research Potential to contribute to the graduate and undergraduate curricula in AI related courses and political methodology Potential to create synergies with existing departmental, school, or University faculty Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Writing Sample Unofficial Transcripts List of References with Contact Information Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/506646": {"title": "Assistant Research Scientist - Altizer", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant Research Scientist - Altizer Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant Research Scientist - Altizer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2802P Working Title Assistant Research Scientist - Altizer Department CAES-Entomology About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 11/01/2026 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/21/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Researcher AC FLSA Faculty Rank Assistant Research Scientist Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Terminal degree awarded in the discipline Position Summary The Department of Entomology at the University of Georgia seeks an Assistant Research Scientist (non-tenure track) to conduct innovative research in insect behavior, chemical ecology, genetics, and evolutionary biology, with a primary emphasis on invasive fire ants. This is a 100% research appointment initially supported through July 31, 2027, by National Science Foundation award RNSFX000167780A to Drs. Sonia Altizer and Ken Ross. Continued appointment beyond the grant period is expected to be supported through competitive extramural funding secured by the successful candidate. The Assistant Research Scientist is expected to establish and sustain a nationally and internationally recognized, externally funded research program that complements and strengthens existing departmental expertise while expanding interdisciplinary collaborations across the University of Georgia and with national and international research partners. Research is expected to integrate laboratory, field, computational, genomic, and quantitative approaches to address fundamental questions in insect behavior, chemical ecology, genetics, and invasive species biology. The successful candidate will publish high-impact, peer-reviewed research; secure competitive external funding to support an independent research program; mentor graduate and undergraduate researchers; and contribute to the research mission of the Department of Entomology. The position will serve as a critical component of the department\u2019s research enterprise by advancing understanding of invasive fire ant biology and fostering collaborations that generate scientific discoveries with applications to biodiversity conservation, invasive species management, and public health in Georgia and beyond. Research activities will be conducted primarily within the Fire Ant Laboratory located in the Riverbend Building, utilizing laboratory space assigned to Dr. Ken Ross under an existing Memorandum of Understanding with the UGA Office of the Vice President for Research. The successful candidate will also have access to personnel, shared equipment, and research facilities supported through other Entomology faculty members. Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification 3-5 years postdoctoral research experience is preferred. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Demonstrable capability in empirical and quantitative skills for biological research including molecular analysis, organizing and executing field sampling and experiments, data compilation and analysis, and data visualization are required. A demonstrated track record in project design, publishing, and obtaining extramural funding, so it cannot be achieved by a research associate or other junior-level researcher. The department seeks applicants with a strong academic record in research and mentoring, particularly in the areas of ant biology, animal behavior, and evolutionary ecology. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Establish and sustain an independent, nationally and internationally recognized research program that complements existing strengths within the Department of Entomology. Develop innovative research questions; formulate hypotheses; and design rigorous laboratory, field, computational, and quantitative studies to investigate insect behavior, chemical ecology, genetics, and invasive species biology. Design, conduct, and oversee research utilizing behavioral, molecular, genomic, ecological, computational, and statistical approaches. Collect, manage, analyze, interpret, and disseminate research data from laboratory, field, and meta-analytical studies. Develop and apply appropriate computational methods for complex behavioral, ecological, and genetic datasets. Prepare and submit competitive proposals to federal agencies and other funding organizations to support and expand the research program. Secure competitive extramural funding to sustain the position and support long-term research activities. Publish high-impact, peer-reviewed scientific manuscripts on a regular basis. Collaborate with faculty within the Department of Entomology, across the University of Georgia, and with domestic and international collaborators to advance knowledge of insect behavior, chemical ecology, evolutionary genetics, fire ant biology, and management. Conduct research that contributes to improved invasive species management, biodiversity conservation, and public health. Percentage Of Time 80 Duties/Responsibilities Recruit, mentor, supervise, and train graduate and undergraduate students participating in research. Serve on graduate student advisory committees and provide scientific and professional mentorship. Supervise undergraduate researchers and provide instruction in research methods, experimental design, quantitative analysis, and behavioral biology. Foster a collaborative, inclusive, and intellectually stimulating research environment. Percentage Of Time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Participate actively in professional scientific societies and organizations. Present research findings at regional, national, and international scientific conferences. Establish and maintain productive working relationships with faculty, staff, students, collaborators, and stakeholders. Participate in departmental, college, and university committees as appropriate. Engage in outreach activities that communicate research findings to scientific, governmental, industry, and public audiences. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/506522": {"title": "Clinical Assistant Professor", "description": "University of Georgia | Clinical Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Clinical Assistant Professor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit: A letter of application specifically responsive to the position\u2019s responsibilities and required qualifications as described above A curriculum vitae Two writing samples The names and contact information of three persons who could provide letters of reference (transcripts and letters of reference will be required only from selected finalists) All material should be submitted electronically via uploading pdf's to this application. Applications received by Sunday, October 25, 2026, will be assured full consideration, but this position is open until filled. Address questions to the search committee chair, Dr. Beth Tolley btolley@uga.edu . Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2811P Working Title Clinical Assistant Professor Department COE-Educational Theory & Pract About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department As the 4th largest public college of education in the country and the 3rd largest college at UGA , the Mary Frances Early College of Education ( MFE COE ) improves the lives of residents of Georgia and beyond through our instruction, research, and service. The MFE COE is a comprehensive college with disciplines focused on teacher preparation, counseling and human development, communication sciences, human movement sciences, career development, student affairs, and educational administration and policy. We place significant emphasis on graduate education with approximately 40% of our students at the graduate level, making us the second largest college at UGA with respect to graduate education. ETAP has contributed to this stature locally, nationally, and internationally. The department is characterized by critical, forward-thinking research and innovative, dynamic teaching. ETAP is committed to making equity, access, and belonging visible in its courses, programs, policies, and practice. Our outreach and research include a variety of multifaceted collaborations, including those with local school districts and local community-based informal education projects, as well as projects that extend across the state of Georgia, the United States, and a variety of international contexts. Information about the department is available at https://coe.uga.edu/directory/educational-theory-and-practice/. The Elementary Education program at UGA , which includes Early Childhood Education, has been ranked among the nation\u2019s top 10 elementary education programs by U.S. News and World Report for more than a decade. Our mission in the Elementary Education program is to blend theory and practice grounded in our shared philosophy of critical pedagogy. Upon program completion, we expect our students to demonstrate teaching competencies related to habits of reflexive practice, integrating scholarship and research, engaging in professional collaboration, and appreciating and supporting multiple backgrounds and perspectives. These elements of thought and action are viewed as key to supporting critically informed and equitable teacher decision-making. The Elementary Education program is designed to offer theoretically and clinically rich experiences in diverse environments. By the end of the program, teachers are prepared to enact these commitments as leaders in their classrooms, schools, and communities. College/Unit/Department website https://coe.uga.edu/directory/educational-theory-and-practice/. Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/18/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit: A letter of application specifically responsive to the position\u2019s responsibilities and required qualifications as described above A curriculum vitae Two writing samples The names and contact information of three persons who could provide letters of reference (transcripts and letters of reference will be required only from selected finalists) All material should be submitted electronically via uploading pdf\u2019s to this application. Applications received by Sunday, October 25, 2026, will be assured full consideration, but this position is open until filled. Address questions to the search committee chair, Dr. Beth Tolley btolley@uga.edu . Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Clinical Assistant Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Clinical Assistant Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications An earned doctorate in Early Childhood Education, Elementary Education, or a related field by the time of employment. Position Summary ( UGA ) invites applications for the position of Clinical Assistant Professor in its Elementary Education program. We are seeking an individual with expertise in PreK-5 teaching, integrating theory and practice in teacher education programs, and experience with the scholarship of teaching or engagement. This is a nine-month academic contract, renewable appointment for the 2027-28 academic year that begins August 2027. In recognition of the important role that clinical faculty play, starting salaries for clinical faculty match those for tenure-track faculty, and the University has a well-structured promotion system for individuals in clinical track positions to advance to clinical associate professor and clinical full professor ranks. Opportunities exist for summer teaching appointments. Additional Requirements 5 years of relevant experience in early childhood/elementary educational settings or educator preparation Demonstrated potential for making significant contributions to the mission of the department, including but not limited to clinical practices in early childhood and elementary education settings, program improvement, and innovation Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Record of experience working with pre-service and/or in-service teachers in educational or professional learning contexts Record of experience working across a variety of educational settings and with diverse student, family, and community populations. Background in and/or expertise that relates to one or more of the following areas: clinical supervision and teacher preparation; STEAM (science, technology, engineering, arts, mathematics); school-university partnerships; positive early childhood/elementary learning environments for students and educators; early childhood/elementary education for children and youth from working-class and impoverished families and communities and/or bilingual and multilingual communities; family and community engagement; or assessment. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Fluency with research literature in teacher education Knowledge of teacher certification programs, state and federal standards and mandates, and/or an awareness of current developments in student assessment and teacher evaluation Physical Demands Work is primarily sedentary and performed in an office, classroom, or digital environment. Requires extended periods of sitting, standing, and using standard office equipment and technologies (such as computers and projectors) throughout the workday. May involve occasional movement within campus facilities and the ability to lift or move light materials (e.g., laptops, textbooks, or instructional supplies) weighing up to 25 pounds. Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate courses (face-to-face, online, and/or blended) and mentor and advise students, as assigned Instruct and supervise teacher candidates in clinical practice in PreK-5 settings Provide service to the program, department, college, university, and the profession Work across departmental and institutional boundaries and participate in sustained engagement with public schools Percentage Of Time 100 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Writing Sample List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Other Documents #1 Other Documents #2 Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/506518": {"title": "Assistant Professor", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant Professor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit all the following: A letter of interest addressing the qualifications described, including a statement of the applicant's (a) research agenda and scholarly accomplishments, (b) teaching experiences and interests, and (c)record of securing external funding, along with plans for pursuing future sponsored research. A statement of research and how your research interests contribute to the field of Adult Learning, Leadership, and Organization Development. A curriculum vitae. Sample publications (maximum 3), combined and uploaded as one PDF. Three letters of recommendation submitted directly by your references through UGA Jobs. Unofficial transcripts (Note: Official transcripts will be required of finalists). Questions may be addressed to the search committee chair, Dr. Aliki Nicolaides: alikin@uga.edu Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2810P Working Title Assistant Professor Department COE-Lifelong Ed, Admin&Policy About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department As the 4th largest public college of education in the country and the 3rd largest college at UGA , the Mary Frances Early College of Education ( MFE COE ) improves the lives of residents of Georgia and beyond through our instruction, research, and service. The MFE COE is a comprehensive college with disciplines focused on teacher preparation, counseling and human development, communication sciences, human movement sciences, career development, student affairs, and educational administration and policy. We place significant emphasis on graduate education with approximately 40% of our students at the graduate level, making us the second largest college at UGA with respect to graduate education. College/Unit/Department website https://coe.uga.edu/academics/concentrations/learning-leadership-and-organization-development/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Commensurate with Experience Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/18/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit all the following: A letter of interest addressing the qualifications described, including a statement of the applicant\u2019s (a) research agenda and scholarly accomplishments, (b) teaching experiences and interests, and \u00a9record of securing external funding, along with plans for pursuing future sponsored research. A statement of research and how your research interests contribute to the field of Adult Learning, Leadership, and Organization Development. A curriculum vitae. Sample publications (maximum 3), combined and uploaded as one PDF . Three letters of recommendation submitted directly by your references through UGA Jobs. Unofficial transcripts (Note: Official transcripts will be required of finalists). Questions may be addressed to the search committee chair, Dr. Aliki Nicolaides: alikin@uga.edu Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Assistant Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications An earned doctorate (Ph.D. or similar) at the time of employment with a specialization in Adult Learning, Leadership, and Organization Development or a related field such as adult education, human resource development, or organization development. Position Summary The University of Georgia\u2019s Learning, Leadership, and Organization Development ( LLOD ) Program in the Department of Lifelong Education, Administration, and Policy invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position specializing in Adult Education and Human Resource Development. The successful candidate will join the faculty on August 1, 2027. Additional Requirements Demonstrated scholarship in adult learning, leadership, and organization development, preferably with interest in examining complex societal challenges affecting adult learners in organizational, collaborative, and/or societal contexts. Evidence of the promise of moving towards a strong record of scholarly research that advances the fields of Adult Education and Human Resource Development and related areas. This includes an active record of scholarship and productivity in terms of peer-reviewed publications in academic journals and professional presentations commensurate with experience. Evidence or strong potential for seeking and attracting external funding. Evidence of potential may include success with small-scale proposals, training/preparation relative to seeking external funds. Evidence or the promise of teaching graduate courses and mentoring students, either as an instructor of record or as a teaching assistant. Evidence may include a record of presentations and training, course evaluations, informal mentoring in terms of working with others on projects and advising students towards degree completion. Excellent oral and written communication and interpersonal skills. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities This position requires (a) teaching the equivalent of two courses per semester in the program or department and (b) the delivery of face-to-face, hybrid, and online instruction on our Athens, Gwinnett, and Online campuses. Tenure-track faculty members in our department are full-time 9-month (academic year) faculty members who have a strong academic background, professional experience in LLOD , and a commitment to facilitating learning, leadership, and change with adults, groups, organizations, and communities in complex, shifting, transformative times. As with all faculty positions in the department, tenure-track faculty engage in scholarly activities; teach courses across LLOD programs; provide academic advising to students as assigned; and engage in service to the department, the University, and the profession. Percentage Of Time 100 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Portfolio Sample Publications Unofficial Transcripts List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/506516": {"title": "Extension Specialist and Director of the UGA Weather Network", "description": "University of Georgia | Extension Specialist and Director of the UGA Weather Network Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Extension Specialist and Director of the UGA Weather Network Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2809P Working Title Extension Specialist and Director of the UGA Weather Network Department CAES-Weather Network About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Commensurate with Experience Anticipated Start Date 01/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/18/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Griffin Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Public Service Professional AC FLSA Faculty Rank Senior Public Service Associate Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications M.S. in meteorology, atmospheric science, agricultural engineering, climate science or a closely related field with training and background in developing and conducting Extension programs and weather/climate effects on agricultural production systems. Position Summary The University of Georgia College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences ( UGA CAES ) is seeking a dynamic individual for the position of Extension Specialist and Director of the UGA Weather Network. This position reports directly to the Assistant Dean for Extension. The incumbent will be responsible for providing visionary leadership for the UGA CAES Weather Network, timely communications, and targeted guidance to agricultural stakeholders statewide using both traditional and cutting-edge technologies to increase data accessibility and application. The University of Georgia Weather Network consists of 91 automated weather stations located around the state. The network provides weather data directly to users, publishes weather and associated climate information on a website, http://weather.uga.edu/, and is operated as a public-private partnership. Five full-time staff are employed to manage the network and data distribution, including the Director. The network is based at the UGA Griffin Campus and the Director works with research and extension programs at Griffin, Athens, and Tifton campuses. The Director has direct responsibility for the overall operation of the network and will have the option for adjunct status in the Department of Crop and Soil Sciences to teach, mentor and serve on graduate student committees. Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Ph.D. in meteorology, atmospheric science, agricultural engineering, climate science or a closely related field with training and background in developing and conducting Extension programs and weather/climate effects on agricultural production systems. The successful candidate will have a working understanding of the field of climate-services and the ability to transform data into accessible and actionable tools to aid decision making processes for agricultural producers and other stakeholders. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Candidates with a demonstrated record of collaborative applied research/Extension/instruction/administrative programming, extramural grant success, and program development that integrates applied science and Extension are preferred. Familiarity with managing weather networks and data acquisition of weather and climate observations and an understanding of climatology and the ability to use climate products ( NOAA Climate Prediction Center, IPCC , mesonets, etc.) to identify agricultural impacts is highly desirable. Candidates should be interested in collaborating with research faculty to jointly develop and deploy climate-related decision support tools for producers and other stakeholders. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? Yes Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Collaborating with faculty and Agricultural and Natural Resource Extension Agents on research and extension issues related to weather and climate in the fields of agriculture, environment, human and animal health and other areas. Percentage Of Time 40 Duties/Responsibilities Managing the financial aspects of the network, including budgeting, securing and spending extramural funding, and negotiating data purchases. Percentage Of Time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Developing and providing network-related data and outreach resources in coordination with extension agents and external stakeholder groups. Percentage Of Time 15 Duties/Responsibilities Managing network staff and overseeing the operation fo the network, including hiring of new staff members as needed. Percentage Of Time 15 Duties/Responsibilities Adding stations to the network and modernizing the station hardware, data handling operations and user interfaces to maximize accessibility. Percentage Of Time 5 Duties/Responsibilities Monitoring the operation of sites that form part of three national networks, including EPA Clean Air Status and Trends Network ( CASTNET ), National Atmospheric Deposition Site ( NADP ), and a USDA -funded UV-B Monitoring and Research Program ( UVMRP ) site. Percentage Of Time 5 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Public Svc/Extension Philosophy Optional Documents Certification Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/506505": {"title": "Public Service Faculty - Strategic Management and Organizational Effectiveness Unit Manager", "description": "University of Georgia | Public Service Faculty - Strategic Management and Organizational Effectiveness Unit Manager Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Public Service Faculty - Strategic Management and Organizational Effectiveness Unit Manager Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Compensation will be determined by the qualifications and experience of the successful applicant. Candidates will be considered for the position until it is filled. Application materials should include a cover letter, curriculum vita, a brief writing sample from a technical report, and three references with contact information. The finalists for the position will be required to provide three letters of recommendation. All applicants must apply through UGAJobs to be considered for the position. Please note that successful applicants are responsible for ensuring their eligibility to work in the United States (i.e., a citizen or national of the United States, a lawful permanent resident, a foreign national authorized to work in the United States without need of employer sponsorship) on or before the effective date of your appointment, and maintain eligibility without sponsorship throughout your appointment. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2807P Working Title Public Service Faculty - Strategic Management and Organizational Effectiveness Unit Manager Department PSO-Carl Vinson Inst of Govt About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The UGA Carl Vinson Institute of Government \u2013 Who We Are As a Public Service and Outreach unit at the University of Georgia, the UGA Institute of Government contributes directly to the university\u2019s overarching public service mission of improving people\u2019s lives by helping to create jobs and prosperity, developing leaders, and addressing critical issues. This public service mission, and the Institute of Government\u2019s role in its success, is at the heart of UGA\u2019s land-grant and sea-grant mission to serve the State of Georgia and its residents. We have a wide range of experts who inform, inspire, and innovate every day so that governments, large and small, can be more efficient and responsive to their citizens, address current and emerging challenges, and serve the public with excellence. We are uniquely positioned to provide impartial support to local governments and state agencies and convene multi-disciplinary and intragovernmental groups to plan for and address many of the challenges faced by communities across Georgia. Our areas of expertise and focus include workforce and economic development; infrastructure and community resilience; government operations and organizational effectiveness; measuring and reporting on impact and outcomes; building skills, knowledge and capacity of government leaders and teams; and maximizing technology and data for governments and their leaders. Whether it is through our award-winning PROPEL (Planning Rural Opportunities for Prosperity and Economic Leadership) program for rural communities, our CyberArch student program that helps Georgia communities increase their cybersecurity, our efforts to build a visionary plan for military and community partnerships to spur economic prosperity and resilient infrastructure, our financial management certificate program to build the capacity of public officials, or hosting educational events about e-mobility strategies for local governments \u2026. We Know Georgia. Fulfilling our land-grant and sea-grant mission to serve the State of Georgia is more than a project. It\u2019s our purpose. We are growing and excited to add individuals to our team who share our commitment to public service \u2013 building stronger communities, inspiring economic resilience, and improving quality of life for communities across Georgia and beyond. Our Culture \u2013 How We Operate We disseminate knowledge through research, scholarship, and instruction. We collaborate internally across our areas of expertise and across the university with academic researchers to bring best practices and expert insights to the governments and communities we serve. We are committed to fielding a team of experts who have a variety of professional and academic experiences and are grounded in our culture of excellence and approach our work with Georgia\u2019s governments in a comprehensive and objective fashion. College/Unit/Department website www.CVIOG.uga.edu Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Compensation will be determined by the qualifications and experience of the successful applicant Anticipated Start Date 12/01/2026 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/18/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Compensation will be determined by the qualifications and experience of the successful applicant. Candidates will be considered for the position until it is filled. Application materials should include a cover letter, curriculum vita, a brief writing sample from a technical report, and three references with contact information. The finalists for the position will be required to provide three letters of recommendation. All applicants must apply through UGAJobs to be considered for the position. Please note that successful applicants are responsible for ensuring their eligibility to work in the United States (i.e., a citizen or national of the United States, a lawful permanent resident, a foreign national authorized to work in the United States without need of employer sponsorship) on or before the effective date of your appointment, and maintain eligibility without sponsorship throughout your appointment. Location of Vacancy Atlanta Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Public Service Professional AC FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in public administration, political science, education, finance, accounting, business administration, organizational development, industrial/organizational psychology, sociology, public policy, or a closely related field. Position Summary The Government Services and Research ( GSR ) Division of the Carl Vinson Institute of Government provides applied research, organizational consulting, strategic planning, and decision-support services that help state and local governments strengthen organizational effectiveness, improve operational performance, and address complex public-sector challenges. The Strategic Management and Organizational Effectiveness Unit Manager provides strategic leadership for the Unit and is responsible for the development, delivery, and continuous enhancement of organizational consulting services that support government clients throughout Georgia. The Unit Manager establishes the strategic direction for the Unit\u2019s consulting practice, leads organizational assessments, strategic planning initiatives, process improvement efforts, performance management projects, and other management consulting engagements designed to improve organizational effectiveness and public service delivery. Responsibilities include supervising and developing public service faculty and professional staff; managing client relationships, contracts, and project portfolios; providing executive consultation; conducting applied research; facilitating executive-level planning and organizational development initiatives; and building collaborative partnerships with state agencies, local governments, University partners, and other stakeholders. The Unit Manager identifies emerging client needs, develops innovative service offerings, and contributes to the continued success, innovation, and long-term effectiveness of the Government Services and Research Division. As a Public Service Faculty member, this position advances the mission of the Carl Vinson Institute of Government by providing objective, data-informed consultation, applied research, and organizational expertise that strengthen government operations, improve public sector performance, and enhance the capacity of Georgia\u2019s state and local governments to serve their communities. Position is located in our Atlanta Office: 18 Capitol Square SW, Atlanta, GA 30334 Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification \u2022 Master\u2019s degree in public administration, political science, education, finance, accounting, business administration, organizational development, industrial/organizational psychology, sociology, public policy, or a closely related field. \u2022 Ten or more years of progressively responsible experience providing organizational consulting, strategic planning, process improvement, performance management, or organizational effectiveness services to state or local government or similarly complex organizations. \u2022 Background leading multidisciplinary consulting engagements and supervising professional staff or project teams. \u2022 Demonstrated success developing client relationships, securing new business opportunities, and managing contracts or externally funded projects. \u2022 Background facilitating executive leadership teams, governing boards, elected officials, or other senior-level stakeholder groups. \u2022 Background designing and implementing organizational assessments, management studies, and data-informed decision support tools. \u2022 Background conducting applied research and translating complex findings into practical recommendations for executive audiences. \u2022 Background utilizing human-centered design, Lean Six Sigma, Kaizen, or other continuous improvement methodologies. \u2022 Background designing and delivering professional education, executive training, or leadership development programs for adult learners. \u2022 Proficiency with quantitative and qualitative research methods, data visualization, and analytical software used to support organizational decision-making. \u2022 Background working with executive leadership within state government, local government, or similarly complex public-sector organizations. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies \u2022 Knowledge of organizational effectiveness, strategic planning, process improvement, and performance management principles and practices. \u2022 Knowledge of state and local government operations, organizational structures, and emerging public sector issues. \u2022 Ability to assess organizational challenges, analyze complex information, and develop practical, data-informed solutions. \u2022 Ability to lead organizational assessments, facilitate strategic planning initiatives, and manage complex consulting engagements. \u2022 Ability to build and maintain collaborative relationships with governmental agencies, University partners, and other stakeholders. \u2022 Ability to supervise, mentor, and develop faculty, professional staff, and project teams. \u2022 Strong project management, organizational, and prioritization skills with the ability to manage multiple concurrent initiatives. \u2022 Excellent written, verbal, facilitation, and presentation skills, including the ability to communicate complex concepts to executive and public-sector audiences. \u2022 Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and experience using data analysis, reporting, and visualization tools to support decision-making. \u2022 Ability to exercise sound judgment, work independently, and collaboratively lead interdisciplinary teams in a dynamic client-service environment. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? Yes Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Strategic Leadership and Consulting \u2022 Lead organizational assessments, strategic planning initiatives, process improvement efforts, performance management projects, and other management consulting engagements for state and local government clients. \u2022 Provide executive consultation and technical assistance to government agencies on organizational effectiveness, operational performance, and strategic decision-making. \u2022 Apply research, analysis, and data-informed decision models to identify organizational challenges and develop practical, innovative solutions. \u2022 Develop strategic plans, organizational assessments, and data strategies while preparing applied research reports and presenting findings and recommendations to elected officials, executive leadership, governing boards, and other stakeholders. \u2022 Facilitate executive planning sessions, stakeholder meetings, and organizational development initiatives using evidence-based and human-centered approaches. Percentage Of Time 50 Duties/Responsibilities Unit Leadership and Operations \u2022 Direct the daily operations of the Strategic Management and Organizational Effectiveness Unit, ensuring the successful delivery of consulting services and project outcomes. \u2022 Supervise, mentor, develop, and evaluate public service faculty, research professionals, staff, and student employees. \u2022 Establish unit priorities, manage project portfolios, oversee workload distribution, and ensure quality and timely completion of deliverables. \u2022 Manage unit resources and utilize financial and operational data to support effective decision- making and continuous improvement. Percentage Of Time 25 Duties/Responsibilities Business Development and Client Engagement \u2022 Develop and maintain collaborative relationships with state agencies, local governments, University partners, and professional organizations. \u2022 Meet with prospective and existing clients to assess organizational needs and develop responsive consulting solutions. \u2022 Develop proposals, pursue grant and contract opportunities, prepare project resource plans, and oversee contract development and deliverables. \u2022 Identify opportunities to expand the Unit\u2019s consulting services and strengthen long-term client partnerships. Percentage Of Time 15 Duties/Responsibilities Organizational Leadership and Collaboration \u2022 Represent the Carl Vinson Institute of Government in meetings, presentations, conferences, and professional organizations. \u2022 Develop collaborative partnerships across the Institute, Public Service and Outreach, and the University of Georgia to enhance interdisciplinary service to government clients. \u2022 Stay informed of Institute expertise, emerging public-sector issues, and evolving client needs to support strategic growth and innovation. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this vacant position? UGAJobs (UGA's job board) LinkedIn Handshake Indeed.com HigherEdJobs A current UGA employee Other (please provide resource) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Writing Sample List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/505816": {"title": "Public Service Faculty - Economic Development Training", "description": "University of Georgia | Public Service Faculty - Economic Development Training Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Public Service Faculty - Economic Development Training Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Compensation will be determined by the qualifications and experience of the successful applicant. Candidates will be considered for the position until it is filled. Application materials should include a cover letter, curriculum vita, a brief writing sample from a technical report, and three references with contact information. The finalists for the position will be required to provide three letters of recommendation. All applicants must apply through UGAJobs to be considered for the position. Please note that successful applicants are responsible for ensuring their eligibility to work in the United States (i.e., a citizen or national of the United States, a lawful permanent resident, a foreign national authorized to work in the United States without need of employer sponsorship) on or before the effective date of your appointment, and maintain eligibility without sponsorship throughout your appointment. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2805P Working Title Public Service Faculty - Economic Development Training Department PSO-Carl Vinson Inst of Govt About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The UGA Carl Vinson Institute of Government \u2013 Who We Are As a Public Service and Outreach unit at the University of Georgia, the UGA Institute of Government contributes directly to the university\u2019s overarching public service mission of improving people\u2019s lives by helping to create jobs and prosperity, developing leaders, and addressing critical issues. This public service mission, and the Institute of Government\u2019s role in its success, is at the heart of UGA\u2019s land-grant and sea-grant mission to serve the State of Georgia and its residents. We have a wide range of experts who inform, inspire, and innovate every day so that governments, large and small, can be more efficient and responsive to their citizens, address current and emerging challenges, and serve the public with excellence. We are uniquely positioned to provide impartial support to local governments and state agencies and convene multi-disciplinary and intragovernmental groups to plan for and address many of the challenges faced by communities across Georgia. Our areas of expertise and focus include workforce and economic development; infrastructure and community resilience; government operations and organizational effectiveness; measuring and reporting on impact and outcomes; building skills, knowledge and capacity of government leaders and teams; and maximizing technology and data for governments and their leaders. Whether it is through our award-winning PROPEL (Planning Rural Opportunities for Prosperity and Economic Leadership) program for rural communities, our CyberArch student program that helps Georgia communities increase their cybersecurity, our efforts to build a visionary plan for military and community partnerships to spur economic prosperity and resilient infrastructure, our financial management certificate program to build the capacity of public officials, or hosting educational events about e-mobility strategies for local governments \u2026. We Know Georgia. Fulfilling our land-grant and sea-grant mission to serve the State of Georgia is more than a project. It\u2019s our purpose. We are growing and excited to add individuals to our team who share our commitment to public service \u2013 building stronger communities, inspiring economic resilience, and improving quality of life for communities across Georgia and beyond. Our Culture \u2013 How We Operate We disseminate knowledge through research, scholarship, and instruction. We collaborate internally across our areas of expertise and across the university with academic researchers to bring best practices and expert insights to the governments and communities we serve. We are committed to fielding a team of experts who have a variety of professional and academic experiences and are grounded in our culture of excellence and approach our work with Georgia\u2019s governments in a comprehensive and objective fashion. College/Unit/Department website www.CVIOG.uga.edu Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Compensation will be determined by the qualifications and experience of the successful applicant Anticipated Start Date 12/01/2026 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/14/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Compensation will be determined by the qualifications and experience of the successful applicant. Candidates will be considered for the position until it is filled. Application materials should include a cover letter, curriculum vita, a brief writing sample from a technical report, and three references with contact information. The finalists for the position will be required to provide three letters of recommendation. All applicants must apply through UGAJobs to be considered for the position. Please note that successful applicants are responsible for ensuring their eligibility to work in the United States (i.e., a citizen or national of the United States, a lawful permanent resident, a foreign national authorized to work in the United States without need of employer sponsorship) on or before the effective date of your appointment, and maintain eligibility without sponsorship throughout your appointment. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Public Service Professional AC FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Master\u2019s degree or terminal degree in public administration, political science, education, finance, accounting, business management, higher education, or a closely related field. Position Summary The Public Service Faculty member develops, coordinates, delivers, and evaluates training, education, and professional development opportunities for adult learners serving local and state governments, economic development organizations, and other public sector partners throughout Georgia. This position utilizes current research, data, emerging trends, and best practices to inform, inspire, and equip elected and appointed officials, economic development professionals, and public sector leaders with the knowledge and skills needed to address current and emerging challenges. Creating engaging learning environments that expand participants\u2019 knowledge and strengthen their ability to address complex economic development and leadership challenges is foundational to success in this role. Through the design, development, delivery, and continuous improvement of curriculum and educational programming, the incumbent applies adult learning principles to ensure training is relevant, practical, and responsive to the evolving needs of Georgia\u2019s communities. Responsibilities include developing curriculum and instructional materials, coordinating and delivering courses, evaluating program effectiveness and participant outcomes, and supporting learners across multiple Institute programs. This position establishes and maintains collaborative relationships with local and state government officials, economic development organizations, professional associations, University partners, and other stakeholders to identify emerging training needs and expand the Institute\u2019s impact. Responsibilities include developing, coordinating, marketing, and delivering customized training programs, certificate programs, and contracted educational services while identifying opportunities to establish, negotiate, and implement new partnerships and client engagements. As a member of the Institute\u2019s Public Service Faculty, the incumbent is responsible for understanding the evolving needs of Georgia\u2019s governments and developing innovative programs and services that strengthen leadership capacity, organizational effectiveness, and economic prosperity. The position also contributes to the Institute\u2019s mission through technical assistance, webinars, professional presentations, applied scholarship, publications, and other activities that advance knowledge and enhance public service throughout Georgia. Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Previous experience in an economic development field is essential, with a minimum of ten years of progressively responsible economic development experience is preferred. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies \u2022 Extensive knowledge of economic development within the state, including, but not limited to issues, trends and challenges related to general economic development, business recruitment and retention, downtown development and tourism. \u2022 Demonstrated ability in designing, developing, and delivering training and professional development programs for diverse audiences, including curriculum development, educational materials creation, instruction, facilitation, and service delivery that promotes understanding of tools, resources, and practices that support positive change within Georgia communities. \u2022 Proficiency in managing and administering educational programs, contracts, grants, budgets, and complex long-term projects and initiatives. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to establish, manage, and maintain effective relationships with clients, stakeholders, and prominent University and governmental officials while exercising sound judgment, diplomacy, and professionalism. \u2022 Ability to learn, adapt, and apply new learning technologies and innovative approaches to training and development service delivery. \u2022 Demonstrated ability to work independently, exercise significant initiative and judgment, and develop creative solutions to highly complex organizational, operational, and community challenges within the framework of University policies and procedures. \u2022 Advanced skills in leadership, economic development, strategic planning, and marketing. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Curriculum Development & Training This position maintains a heavy focus on design, development and delivery of training and content to adult learners within economic development and adjacent fields. Content may be part of existing certificate programs or as stand-alone training, depending upon the needs of the client. Percentage Of Time 80 Duties/Responsibilities Stakeholder Engagement & Business Development This position requires the incumbent to identify economic development opportunities for content delivery. This consists of securing contracts for both ongoing training opportunities, agreements for one-time course offerings, and maintaining relationships with professional organizations. Percentage Of Time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Technical Assistance & Service Delivery The position requires the incumbent to listen critically to the needs expressed by leadership in economic development leadership to satisfy training needs, but also to identify opportunities for the Institute as a whole. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this vacant position? UGAJobs (UGA's job board) LinkedIn Handshake Indeed.com HigherEdJobs A current UGA employee Other (please provide resource) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Writing Sample List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/505815": {"title": "Director of Economic Development", "description": "University of Georgia | Director of Economic Development Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Director of Economic Development Below you will find the details for the position including 