S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The College of Pharmacy at the University of Georgia ( UGA ) is a distinguished institution known for its excellence in pharmacy education, research, and community service. We are at the forefront of pharmaceutical research, with faculty and students engaged in groundbreaking studies that contribute to advancements in healthcare and medicine. Research areas include drug discovery, pharmacology, and clinical pharmacy. The college is highly ranked, placing 15th out of 141 pharmacy programs nationwide according to US News & World Report, underscoring our reputation for excellence. These elements make the UGA College of Pharmacy a unique and enriching place for students to pursue their pharmacy education and careers. College/Unit/Department website https://rx.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2026 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/07/2025 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications must be submitted through the UGA Jobs website. Application materials submitted in other ways will not be accepted. For full consideration, please apply by November 15, 2025. Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2025 and continue until the position is filled. A complete application includes: Cover Letter Curriculum vitae Two-page research statement One-page statement of teaching philosophy The names, titles, and contact information for three professional references Please direct inquiries to the search committee chair: Dexi Liu, Ph.D. dliu@uga.edu Professor Department of Pharmaceutical and Biomedical Sciences College of Pharmacy University of Georgia Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Assistant Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications A Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in biology, medicine, chemistry, physics, bioengineering, or a related field. Position Summary The Department of Pharmaceutical and Biomedical Sciences in the College of Pharmacy at the University of Georgia invites applications for a full-time tenure-track position at the level of Assistant Professor. We seek an individual who will build and maintain a strong extramurally-funded research program in the area of pharmaceutical and biomedical sciences, such as AI drug discovery, cancer biology, medicinal chemistry, pharmacology, or pharmacokinetics. The successful candidate will complement and build upon the Department\u2019s existing research strengths, which include active programs in chemical biology, pharmacology and pharmaceutics, cancer biology, and infectious diseases. Research Areas of Interest Areas of particular interest include, but are not limited to: AI/computational drug discovery Computational or virtual drug screening Chemical biology Pharmacology Immunology Cancer biology Drug formulation or drug delivery Medicinal chemistry Toxicology Systems biology The Department offers a competitive salary, excellent laboratory space, and a generous start-up package to support the successful candidate\u2019s research program. Additional Requirements Minimum of 3 years of postdoctoral training. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Evidence of strong potential for independent research and high-impact publications. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Support the delivery of the undergrad and graduate programs of the College of Pharmacy. Percentage Of Time 50 Duties/Responsibilities Develop and maintain a nationally recognized program of research. Percentage Of Time 45 Duties/Responsibilities Support the service mission of the College of Pharmacy. Percentage Of Time 5 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478003": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Fungal Biology/Mycology", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant or Associate Professor - Fungal Biology/Mycology Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant or Associate Professor - Fungal Biology/Mycology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin on 15 October 2025; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Inquiries should be directed to Dr. Miaoying Tian, Chair of the Search Committee (mtian@uga.edu). Materials to be uploaded include i) cover letter addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relative to the responsibilities of the position, ii) curriculum vitae, iii) graduate-level academic transcripts, iv) statement of research interests, v) statement of teaching experience and interests, and vi) names and contact information of four professional references. Selected applicants will be required to submit a background investigation demonstrating eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2446P Working Title Assistant or Associate Professor - Fungal Biology/Mycology Department CAES-Plant Pathology About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department As one of the largest departments of plant pathology in the U.S., we are recognized internationally for our comprehensive and integrative research and outreach portfolio, spanning basic, translational and applied programs. Our scientists ensure the economic viability of agriculture, the largest sector of Georgia\u2019s economy, and contribute to national and global food security by reducing crop losses. Equally important, our research increases the understanding of basic biology through new discoveries in pathogen biology, resistance genetics and host-pathogen interactions College/Unit/Department website https://plantpath.caes.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Commensurate with Experience Anticipated Start Date 05/01/2026 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 08/08/2025 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin on 15 October 2025; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Inquiries should be directed to Dr. Miaoying Tian, Chair of the Search Committee (mtian@uga.edu). Materials to be uploaded include i) cover letter addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relative to the responsibilities of the position, ii) curriculum vitae, iii) graduate-level academic transcripts, iv) statement of research interests, v) statement of teaching experience and interests, and vi) names and contact information of four professional references. Selected applicants will be required to submit a background investigation demonstrating eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track or Tenured Minimum Qualifications The candidate must have a Ph.D. in plant pathology, mycology, one of the plant or microbial sciences, or a related discipline. Position Summary The Department of Plant Pathology in the College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences ( CAES ) at the University of Georgia is recruiting for the position of Assistant or Associate Professor in Fungal Biology/Mycology with 70% research, 25% teaching, and 5% service appointment. This is an academic-year (9-month), tenure- track appointment located at the Athens Campus. The successful candidate will develop a dynamic, innovative, internationally recognized, and extramurally funded research program in basic fungal biology. Areas of interest include computational biology and comparative, population, or functional genomics, with the goal of understanding ecological or evolutionary patterns and processes of plant-pathogenic fungi. Research using novel and contemporary approaches into the molecular, ecological, or evolutionary aspects of pathogenic fungal\u2013plant host interactions is also of interest. The position offers rich opportunities for collaborations with colleagues in the Department of Plant Pathology, the Fungal Biology Group, the Plant Center, and the Institute of Bioinformatics . There is an expectation of excellence in grantsmanship, timely communication of research findings via peer-reviewed journal articles, active participation in the mentoring of graduate students and postdoctoral scientists and contributing to a dynamic environment within the university. Initial instructional responsibilities will include teaching Mycology , a split-level graduate and undergraduate student course, and Fungi, Friends and Foes , a large lecture-format course on the impact of fungi on human civilization. Additional Requirements The candidate must have a Ph.D. in plant pathology, mycology, one of the plant or microbial sciences, or a related discipline. Applicants should have documented research background appropriate for the appointment rank, as evidenced by peer-reviewed publications in fungal biology/mycology. Demonstrated success teaching in a classroom setting for one or more semesters. To be considered for the rank of Associate Professor, candidates must have at least 5 full years in rank at the Assistant Professor level. To be eligible for tenure upon appointment, candidates must be appointed as an Associate Professor, have been tenured at a prior institution, and bring a demonstrably regional and/or national reputation to the institution. Candidates must be approved for tenure upon appointment before hire. The criteria for promotion and tenure in the Department of Plant Pathology are summarized at https://provost.uga.edu/wp-content/uploads/ptu-criteria-plant-pathology.pdf Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? Yes Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/CV Unofficial Transcripts List of References with Contact Information Research Portfolio/Philosophy Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478002": {"title": "Assistant/Associate Research Scientist for Advancing Circular Bioeconomy Systems", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant/Associate Research Scientist for Advancing Circular Bioeconomy Systems Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant/Associate Research Scientist for Advancing Circular Bioeconomy Systems Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2443P Working Title Assistant/Associate Research Scientist for Advancing Circular Bioeconomy Systems Department CAES-Assoc Dean for Research About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary $100,000 Anticipated Start Date 10/01/2025 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 08/05/2025 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Researcher AC FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications A Ph.D. in biochemical/chemical/agricultural/systems engineering, or agricultural science, or qualitative biology or equivalent. Position Summary The College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences ( CAES ) at the University of Georgia seeks to recruit an Assistant or Associate Research Scientist to work on the Circular Bioeconomy Systems ( CBS ) initiative. This is a non-tenured track position with 95% research and 5% service responsibility. The position will be housed in the UGA CAES ; however, the incumbent will be expected to work closely with faculty in the multidisciplinary teams from Colleges/Schools of Engineering, Forestry and Natural Resources, Arts and Sciences, Family and Consumer Sciences, and others. The candidate is expected to maintain an internationally renowned research program that produces and publishes work recognized and used by researchers and stakeholders around the world. The incumbent will report to the office of the CAES Associate Dean of Research. The incumbent will coordinate and draft proposals for external funding to support the CBS initiative. Although this position is predominantly a research appointment, the person will interact with undergraduate/graduate students and stakeholders, and contribute to teaching and outreach mission of the University. Additional Requirements Minimum Qualifications A Ph.D. in biochemical/chemical/agricultural/systems engineering, or agricultural science, or qualitative biology or equivalent with strong background and proven success in modeling biophysical systems is required. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification The chosen candidate will be expected to show evidence of expertise in biophysical modeling, life-cycle-analysis, big-data, building digital twins, and latest modeling and AI techniques. Candidates with postdoctoral training and a strong publication record will be preferred. Internship/hands-on skills in biosystems industries and proficiency in preparing interdisciplinary grant proposals for external funding will be favored. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies The incumbent should be knowledgeable of the systems that produce biomass on land, and in water and controlled environmental systems, and scientific and technical processes that use biomass as feedstock for synthesizing materials, chemical and products for human needs. They should possess excellent inter-personal skills to aid collaboration and build consensus.\u00a0The successful candidate will have excellent skills in written and oral communications and traits required to successfully work with multidisciplinary teams. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities The incumbent is expected to develop biophysical models and work with multidisciplinary teams, and coordinate and lead in building holistic, integrated biosystems, ecosystems, and socio-economic system models for identifying: a) grand challenges in advancing sustainable circular bioeconomy systems; b) critical knowledge, techniques and skills needed for addressing the challenges; c) priority actions for meeting short and long-term CBS goals; and d) methods to prototype and extend innovation for adoption by users. Percentage Of Time 100 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Research Portfolio/Philosophy Sample Publications Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/478001": {"title": "Louise McBee Distinguished Professor of Higher Education", "description": "University of Georgia | Louise McBee Distinguished Professor of Higher Education Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Louise McBee Distinguished Professor of Higher Education Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, submit a letter of interest, a curriculum vitae, and the names of three references. References will only be contacted with permission from finalists. General inquiries may be directed to the McBee Professor search committee at ihe@uga.edu. Review of applications will begin September 19 and continue until the position is filled; candidates who apply by October 10 will receive full consideration. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2440P Working Title Louise McBee Distinguished Professor of Higher Education Department SRVPAA-Institute of Higher Ed About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2026 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 07/30/2025 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants To apply, submit a letter of interest, a curriculum vitae, and the names of three references. References will only be contacted with permission from finalists. General inquiries may be directed to the McBee Professor search committee at ihe@uga.edu. Review of applications will begin September 19 and continue until the position is filled; candidates who apply by October 10 will receive full consideration. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenured Minimum Qualifications Candidates should have a doctoral degree in higher education or an equivalent terminal degree in a complementary field (e.g., economics, law, management, political science, public policy, sociology). Position Summary The Louise McBee Institute of Higher Education at the University of Georgia invites applications from senior higher education scholars to fill the Louise McBee Distinguished Professorship in Higher Education with a starting date of August 1, 2026. The professorship honors Dr. Louise McBee, who held multiple leadership positions at the University of Georgia before serving for over a decade as a champion for higher education in the Georgia legislature. As an administrator, she helped advance UGA\u2019s academic and service missions; as a legislator, she played important roles in ensuring the future of the HOPE Scholarship and launching initiatives such as the Governor\u2019s Teaching Fellows program. We seek a scholar who will advance the multi-disciplinary character of the McBee Institute, add to the depth and breadth of our faculty, and undertake work that furthers our understandings of higher education. The successful candidate will be expected to teach core graduate-level courses, advise and mentor doctoral students, pursue an active program of funded research, publish impactful scholarship, and participate in the ongoing academic and governance activities of the McBee Institute. Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Candidates should bring a distinguished record in instruction, scholarly research, and extramural funding focused on the study of higher education. We encourage applications from scholars with expertise in quantitative, qualitative, and/or mixed methods approaches. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477994": {"title": "Assistant Research Scientist", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant Research Scientist Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant Research Scientist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2349P Working Title Assistant Research Scientist Department VPR-Complex Carbohyd Rsch Ctr About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization None Advertised Salary Commensurate with experience. Anticipated Start Date 07/01/2025 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 04/15/2025 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Researcher AC FLSA Faculty Rank Assistant Research Scientist Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications PhD in Chemistry, glycobiology, biochemistry, Molecular biology or related studies. Position Summary Assistant Research Scientist position in CCRC\u2019s National Glycoscience Resources Laboratory. Conduct research for development of new tools and method for structural characterization of glycoproteins and polysaccharides using a of MS, HPLC , HPAEC or NMR techniques and subsequently publish and obtain independent funding. Write and edit manuscripts and reviewers on topics in glycoscience to increase the publication output. Supervise laboratory technicians, postdocs and research professions in service and research projects that includes characterization of glycoconjugates with collaboration from investigators from outside of UGA . Write detailed comprehensive reports on data produced in the laboratory on structural, characterization of polysaccharides and glycoproteins. Review reports produced by other laboratory members for accuracy and high quality so that the data can be used in a manuscript publication. Teach and organize on the hands-on and virtual training courses offered by the CCRC on glycoconjuagtes with participants from universities, research institutes and government agencies. Help organize workshops and tutorials on topics in glycoscience. Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Prior expertise in glycobiology, structural characterization of glycoconjugates using analytical techniques and project management and leadership positions. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Physical Demands Normal lab activity. Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities The position requires high level research on the development of novel methods to understand the detailed structure of polysaccharides and glycoproteins. Novel tools will need to be developed. The position entails detailed characterization using state of the art instrumentations. Percentage Of Time 40 Duties/Responsibilities The position requires supervision of scientific staff, technicians, postdocs and research professionals. Percentage Of Time 30 Duties/Responsibilities The position requires independent manuscript and review preparation for admission to scientific journals. Percentage Of Time 10 Duties/Responsibilities The position involves preparation of proposals to acquire independent funding for research activities and training courses. Percentage Of Time 10 Duties/Responsibilities The position requires that knowledge be passed along through teaching and organizing the hands-on and virtual training courses and workshops. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477992": {"title": "Public Service Faculty - Local Government Operations", "description": "University of Georgia | Public Service Faculty - Local Government Operations Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Public Service Faculty - Local Government Operations Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Compensation will be determined by the qualifications and experience of the successful applicant. Candidates will be considered for the position until it is filled. Application materials should include a cover letter, curriculum vita, a brief writing sample from a technical report, and three references with contact information. The finalists for the position will be required to provide three letters of recommendation. All applicants must apply through UGAJobs to be considered for the position. Possibility for the position be located in Athens or Atlanta. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2207P Working Title Public Service Faculty - Local Government Operations Department PSO-Carl Vinson Inst of Govt About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The UGA Carl Vinson Institute of Government \u2013 Who We Are As a Public Service and Outreach unit at the University of Georgia, the UGA Institute of Government contributes directly to the university\u2019s overarching public service mission of improving people\u2019s lives by helping to create jobs and prosperity, developing leaders, and addressing critical issues. This public service mission, and the Institute of Government\u2019s role in its success, is at the heart of UGA\u2019s land-grant and sea-grant mission to serve the State of Georgia and its residents. We have a wide range of experts who inform, inspire, and innovate every day so that governments, large and small, can be more efficient and responsive to their citizens, address current and emerging challenges, and serve the public with excellence. We are uniquely positioned to provide impartial support to local governments and state agencies and convene multi-disciplinary and intragovernmental groups to plan for and address many of the challenges faced by communities across Georgia. Our areas of expertise and focus include workforce and economic development; infrastructure and community resilience; government operations and organizational effectiveness; measuring and reporting on impact and outcomes; building skills, knowledge and capacity of government leaders and teams; and maximizing technology and data for governments and their leaders. Whether it is through our award-winning PROPEL (Planning Rural Opportunities for Prosperity and Economic Leadership) program for rural communities, our CyberArch student program that helps Georgia communities increase their cybersecurity, our efforts to build a visionary plan for military and community partnerships to spur economic prosperity and resilient infrastructure, our financial management certificate program to build the capacity of public officials, or hosting educational events about e-mobility strategies for local governments \u2026. We Know Georgia. Fulfilling our land-grant and sea-grant mission to serve the State of Georgia is more than a project. It\u2019s our purpose. We are growing and excited to add individuals to our team who share our commitment to public service \u2013 building stronger communities, inspiring economic resilience, and improving quality of life for communities across Georgia and beyond. Our Culture \u2013 How We Operate We disseminate knowledge through research, scholarship, and instruction. We collaborate internally across our areas of expertise and across the university with academic researchers to bring best practices and expert insights to the governments and communities we serve. We are committed to fielding a team of experts who have a variety of professional and academic experiences and are grounded in our culture of excellence and approach our work with Georgia\u2019s governments in a comprehensive and objective fashion. College/Unit/Department website www.CVIOG.uga.edu Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Compensation will be determined by the qualifications and experience of the successful applicant Anticipated Start Date 02/01/2025 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 11/08/2024 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Compensation will be determined by the qualifications and experience of the successful applicant. Candidates will be considered for the position until it is filled. Application materials should include a cover letter, curriculum vita, a brief writing sample from a technical report, and three references with contact information. The finalists for the position will be required to provide three letters of recommendation. All applicants must apply through UGAJobs to be considered for the position. Possibility for the position be located in Athens or Atlanta. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Public Service Professional AC FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Master\u2019s degree. Position Summary The Carl Vinson Institute of Government at The University of Georgia invites applications for a Public Service Faculty position in the Government Services and Research Division / Local Government Unit .\u00a0 The position will be available February 1, 2025 and carries rank in the public service faculty career ladder of the University. Helping local governments operate in the most financially prudent and efficient manner is a priority of the Carl Vinson Institute of Government. This position will provide technical assistance and conduct studies to help government leaders make data informed decisions. To be successful in this position will require a mix of both qualitative and quantitative research methods to address the needs of the government being assisted. We are looking for an experienced professional who is eager to assist local government leaders through financial analysis, policy analysis, feasibility studies, benchmarking and best practice research. This position will also work with public works directors and other local government leaders who work every day to maintain the critical infrastructure in their city and county. As a public service faculty member, this position will be part of one of the most trusted organizations in the state that provides objective research and analysis. This position is part of the Local Government Operations unit comprised of a team of faculty and staff. Public service faculty are responsible for understanding the needs of governments and developing and delivering programs and services to meet those needs. As a public service faculty member, this position has an opportunity to serve governments across the state and also develop and share their expertise through training, webinars, writing reports, and making professional presentations. Occasional overnight travel is required of this position. Additional Requirements The successful candidate will be appointed at the rank of Public Service Assistant, Public Service Associate, or Senior Public Service Associate. Rank on hire will depend on the candidate\u2019s qualifications and experience, according to Public Service and Outreach Appointment and Promotion Guidelines found here: https://outreach.uga.edu/resources/promotions/ Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Master\u2019s degree in, but not limited to, public administration, business, social work, sociology, law, economics, management information systems Five years of experience working in government operations or management Background with the maintenance and operations of public infrastructure Background doing financial analysis Background gathering data, writing reports and making presentations to elected officials Background facilitating groups. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Knowledge of state and local government political structure, functions, and operations. Knowledge of public management practices, emerging trends, issues, and challenges. Knowledge of local government operations, financial environment, and legal frameworks. Knowledge of public works and infrastructure including sewer and water, utilities, and maintenance and repair. Ability to develop and manage budgets associated with contracts or grant projects. Ability to manage complex long-term projects and client relationships. Ability to take initiative and work independently. Ability to develop and apply creative solutions to complex problems. Ability to explain complex methodologies and solutions in a practical manner. Advanced skills in establishing priorities and organizing work. Advanced administrative, management, and supervisory skills. Must have excellent oral and written communication skills. Strong interpersonal skills are necessary for client interactions and presentations. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? Yes Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Provide research and technical assistance services to local governments and other government organizations. Provide technical assistance and conduct studies to help government leaders make data informed decisions through financial analysis, feasibility studies, benchmarking and best practice research. Percentage Of Time 70 Duties/Responsibilities Meet with potential clients to determine needs and negotiate contracts. Establish and maintain relationships with existing clients, as appropriate. Percentage Of Time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Support the strategic projects of the Institute and collaborate across the Institute of Government and Public Service and Outreach. Percentage Of Time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Establish and maintain solid working relationships with personnel in state government and professional associations that align with the work of the Institute. Percentage Of Time 5 Duties/Responsibilities Conduct applied research and engage in scholarship on topics and issues of relevance to the mission of the Institute of Government and programs and services of governments in Georgia. Share expertise through training, webinars, writing reports, and making professional presentations. Percentage Of Time 5 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this vacant position? UGAJobs (UGA's job board) LinkedIn Handshake Indeed.com HigherEdJobs A current UGA employee Other (please provide resource) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Writing Sample List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477991": {"title": "Business Consultant-Macon", "description": "University of Georgia | Business Consultant-Macon Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Business Consultant-Macon Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The cover letter should address the following: Our employees say empathy\u2014an understanding of and service to others\u2014is important in their role at the SBDC. In your letter, please describe instances where empathy is evidenced in your work or elsewhere and discuss why you are interested in supporting the mission and culture of our organization. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2136P Working Title Business Consultant-Macon Department PSO-Small Business Dev Center About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary 80,000 Anticipated Start Date 12/01/2024 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/03/2024 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants The cover letter should address the following: Our employees say empathy\u2014an understanding of and service to others\u2014is important in their role at the SBDC . In your letter, please describe instances where empathy is evidenced in your work or elsewhere and discuss why you are interested in supporting the mission and culture of our organization. Location of Vacancy Macon Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Public Service Professional AC FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications A bachelor\u2019s degree in business or a related field is required. Position Summary Join an environment that has been named by Georgia Trend as a \u201cBest Place to Work\u201d. Our team consist of a well-respected and collaborative group of professionals committed to using their areas of expertise to enhance the economic well-being of the small business community. As a trusted Business Consultant, you will enjoy applying your knowledge to help small business clients reach their goals by providing a wide range of educational and consulting services. We are looking for trusted consultants who have a passion to serve and a desire to make a positive impact in the small business community. A Small Business Development Center ( SBDC ) Business Consultant is a public service faculty position responsible for providing counseling and delivering programs to individuals, businesses, communities, organizations, and other public agencies in their assigned geographic territory. This charge requires a broad base of business knowledge, excellent analytical skills, and the ability to effectively manage multiple projects simultaneously. These duties require the integration of business theory and practice, thus necessitating professional development activities. This position is located in Macon, Georgia. Multi-county travel is required. Salary is $80,000 and an excellent benefits package including a defined benefits retirement plan. Additional Requirements See the University of Georgia Guidelines for Appointments and Promotions for Public Service and Outreach Academic Rank for information regarding the Public Service Faculty ranks. Progression towards earning an advanced degree is expected while in a provisional faculty position. When a public service professional receives an advanced degree, recommendation for a public service faculty appointment can be initiated according to the public service faculty appointment process (see \u201cAppointment and Promotion upon Receiving an Advanced Degree\u201d on page 17 of the Guidelines ). Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification A master\u2019s degree in business or a related field is preferred. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Applicants must have a good working knowledge of all business functions, including: financial analysis, business research, marketing, and accounting. Knowledge of the area economic development community, prior banking or accounting background and the ability to network is a plus. Knowledge of University and SBDC programs and operating philosophy and/or relevant management background preferred. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Provide high quality individual instruction to entrepreneurs, business owners, and business managers. Analyze situations, make recommendations, and educate clients with regard to business plans, market feasibility, financial viability, operations management, and legal structures, to name but a few topics. Maintain an appropriate level and mix of clients as noted by annual goals and strategic plan objectives. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Develop and deliver high quality business training programs that are responsive to the needs of the business community served. Generate curricula for business programs, seminars, conferences, etc. for the local business interests. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Determine and initiate, topics, agendas, instructors, instructional materials, location, time and other resources required. Create and produce instructional materials. Serve as an instructor of business training programs and secure qualified outside instructors, as needed. Effectively market business training programs within assigned communities, so as to meet annual goals. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities In addition to maintaining a broad base of business knowledge, develop specific and relevant area(s) of expertise within the arena of business development. Apply this knowledge through development and delivery of new training programs, consulting tools, research projects, co-consulting and/or other impact measures. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Direct clients to other appropriate sources of business information and assistance. Disseminate pertinent information to the business community via various media. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Serve as an advocate of business development, expansion and retention in the area, thereby becoming a visible leader in the local business community. Work collaboratively with private-sector businesses, other economic development assistance units of the University System, and other units of State Government to further the economic well-being of Georgia\u2019s citizens. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Engage in public relations activities such as, speeches, presentations, active committee participation, and direct discussions. Relevant audiences include bankers, colleges and universities, chambers of commerce, economic development authorities, downtown development organizations, government agencies, local political offices, civic organizations, local media and potential program sponsors. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Assist in the continued development, implementation, and updating of the organization\u2019s strategic plan. Ensure that organizational goals and objectives are accomplished in a timely and thorough manner. Work with colleagues to develop and deploy annual action and marketing plans that align with the organizational strategic plan, are tailored to meeting the specific small business needs within the assigned geography, and capitalize on the skills of SBDC personnel. Prepare and execute individual work plans, including professional development initiatives, which align with area office objectives. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Support organizational improvement efforts through active involvement with internal committees, center reviews, special projects, and various assessments as directed by the state office. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Actively participate in the development and execution of sponsorship acquisition strategies in support of area office and state goals. Initiate co-sponsorship of programs with private businesses, economic development organizations, and other government entities. Seek and apply for grants relevant to entrepreneurship and business development. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Document activities via electronic information system (Unity) in a timely, accurate, and comprehensive manner. Maintain client files as per SBA and SBDC guidelines. Provide impact information for required SBA reporting including but not limited to success stories. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Perform all responsibilities efficiently and effectively within assigned area office. Ensure that administrative policies are followed, that programs are innovative and responsive, and that top quality services are delivered. Utilize client and management feedback in striving for continuous improvement. Maintain positive, professional relations with other institutions. Perform all responsibilities efficiently and effectively within assigned area office. Ensure that administrative policies are followed, that programs are innovative and responsive, and that top quality services are delivered. Utilize client and management feedback in striving for continuous improvement. Maintain positive, professional relations with other institutions. Represent the Area Director when required. Percentage Of Time Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477990": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant or Associate Professor Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant or Associate Professor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin October 15 and continue until the position is filled; candidates who apply by November 8 will receive full consideration. To apply, please submit a letter of interest, a curriculum vitae, and the names of three references . Other queries may be directed to Assistant/Associate Professor Search Committee at ihe@uga.edu. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2115P Working Title Assistant or Associate Professor Department SRVPAA-Institute of Higher Ed About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department Louise McBee Institute of Higher Education College/Unit/Department website ihe.uga.edu Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Commensurate with experience Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2025 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/17/2024 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin October 15 and continue until the position is filled; candidates who apply by November 8 will receive full consideration. To apply, please submit a letter of interest, a curriculum vitae, and the names of three references . Other queries may be directed to Assistant/Associate Professor Search Committee at ihe@uga.edu. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank (Tenure Track) Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Minimum Qualifications Candidates should have a doctoral degree in higher education or an equivalent terminal degree in a complementary field (e.g., economics, law, management, political science, public policy, sociology). Position Summary The Louise McBee Institute of Higher Education at the University of Georgia invites applications for an early or mid-career professor position (tenure-track at assistant or associate rank) to begin August 1, 2025. The successful candidate will be expected to support student research interests on critical issues in higher education, teach core graduate-level courses, advise and mentor doctoral students in their studies and research, engage in national and international partnerships that enhance the opportunities of students, pursue an active program of funded research; actively and effectively pursue and achieve publication in appropriate scholarly venues; and participate fully in the ongoing academic and governance activities of the McBee Institute. Additional Requirements Candidates should have a doctoral degree in higher education or an equivalent terminal degree in a complementary field (e.g., economics, law, management, political science, public policy, sociology) and a record of scholarship and research productivity commensurate with the rank of assistant or associate professor at the University of Georgia. Candidates also should have expertise in qualitative, quantitative, and/or mixed-methods research as evidenced by their cumulative research portfolio. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies We especially encourage applications from candidates who use critical methodologies and approaches. We seek candidates who will advance the multidisciplinary character of the Institute, add to the depth of the faculty, contribute to our pursuit of inclusive excellence, and bring innovative perspectives to the study of higher education. Preference is for candidates to have: Topical research interest and expertise in one or more of the following areas: Organizational change and governance in higher education HBCUs, HSIs, and other minority-serving institutions State and federal policy Prior history teaching and mentoring graduate students Demonstrated capability and willingness to teach courses in residential, low-residency, and online formats Evidence of and potential for attracting external funding Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477988": {"title": "Assistant or Associate Professor \u2013 Meat Science Extension and Teaching", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant or Associate Professor \u2013 Meat Science Extension and Teaching Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant or Associate Professor \u2013 Meat Science Extension and Teaching Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Inquiries about the position should be directed to search committee chair Alex Stelzleni ( astelz@uga.edu ). Materials to be uploaded include: (a) cover letter, (b) curriculum vita; (c) a list of 3 references with contact information, (d) a statement of Extension, teaching, and applied research philosophy (as Other Document #1; not to exceed three pages) addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relative to the responsibilities of the position, and (e) a copy of transcripts. Selected applicants will be required to submit to a background investigation demonstrating eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia and provide official transcripts. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2009P Working Title Assistant or Associate Professor \u2013 Meat Science Extension and Teaching Department CAES-Animal & Dairy Science About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website https://animaldairy.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 09/01/2024 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 06/21/2024 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Inquiries about the position should be directed to search committee chair Alex Stelzleni ( astelz@uga.edu ). Materials to be uploaded include: (a) cover letter, (b) curriculum vita; \u00a9 a list of 3 references with contact information, (d) a statement of Extension, teaching, and applied research philosophy (as Other Document #1; not to exceed three pages) addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relative to the responsibilities of the position, and (e) a copy of transcripts. Selected applicants will be required to submit to a background investigation demonstrating eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia and provide official transcripts. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank (Tenure Track) Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track or Tenured Minimum Qualifications Minimum qualifications: Applicants should hold a Ph.D. in animal science, meat science, or closely related fields. Position Summary Assistant or Associate Professor \u2013 Meat Science Extension and Teaching. This is a nine-month, tenure track or tenured appointment (65% Extension, 30% Teaching, 5% Service) with two months of summer salary (11.111% per month) guaranteed in the Department of Animal and Dairy Science ( ADS , ads.caes.uga.edu) in the College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences at the University of Georgia ( UGA ). The position will be located at the UGA Athens Campus. It is expected to develop and provide leadership for a relevant nationally/internationally recognized meat science Extension and teaching program. Major Responsibilities : The individual is expected to develop and provide leadership for a relevant nationally/internationally recognized meats Extension program. Extension activities include interacting with industry, county agents, and other scientists to develop a state-of-the-art information/technology transfer program for the meat industry. This faculty member will serve as a resource on meat processing, fresh and processed meat production, and meat evaluation for the meat industry, 4-H and FFA meat judging coaches, and HACCP training, and is expected to develop or contribute to a comprehensive meat science curriculum to include topics in meat evaluation, fresh meats, and processed meats; advise undergraduate and graduate students; mentor students interested in industry work experiences/internships; lead students in extracurricular learning experiences; and provide guest lectures to support existing courses. The specific Extension and applied research program will be determined based on the successful candidate\u2019s area(s) of expertise, but emphasis will be placed on the ability to develop an externally funded, applied research program. This faculty member will be expected to teach undergraduate courses in meat science, and a graduate course in their area of expertise within the department. Additional Requirements To be considered at the rank of Associate Professor, candidates must have at least 5 full years in rank at the Assistant Professor level. To be eligible for tenure upon appointment, candidates must be appointed as an Associate professor, have been tenured at a prior institution, and bring a demonstrably national reputation to the institution. Candidates must be approved for tenure upon appointment before hire. Please see UGA and Promotion and Tenure unit criteria for academic rank faculty at https://provost.uga.edu/faculty-affairs/promotion-tenure-evaluation/academic-rank/ Discipline-specific criteria and procedures for promotion and tenure with Animal and Dairy Science found here: https://provost.uga.edu/_resources/documents/ptucriteria/animal-and-dairy-science-ptu-2019.pdf . Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification A proven record of excellence in meat science is expected. Candidates with a proven record of carrying and publishing innovative research, securing extramural funding, and a background in intercollegiate meat judging are highly encouraged to apply. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies The ability to effectively communicate and collaborate with colleagues and meat industry professionals is essential. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/CV List of References with Contact Information Other Documents #1 Unofficial Transcripts Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477987": {"title": "OPEN RANK Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Diagnostic Imaging", "description": "University of Georgia | OPEN RANK Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Diagnostic Imaging Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits OPEN RANK Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Diagnostic Imaging Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Qualified applicants are invited to submit: (1) a letter of intent including professional interests and career goals, (2) a curriculum vitae, and (3) the name, mailing address, and contact information for three professional references. Questions regarding the position may be directed to ( quand003@uga.edu ) or telephone (706-202-5707). All applications received on or before March 1, 2024, will be fully considered; applications will be accepted until the position is filled. The successful candidate\u2019s employment starting date is negotiable; the position is available immediately. As required by the University of Georgia policy, the successful candidate will be subject to a background investigation. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F1846P Working Title OPEN RANK Assistant/Associate/Full Professor of Diagnostic Imaging Department VetMed-Small Animal Med & Surg About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The University of Georgia College of Veterinary Medicine, founded in 1946, is dedicated to training future veterinarians, providing services to animal owners and veterinarians, and conducting investigations to improve the health of animals as well as people. The college benefits pets and their owners, food-producing animals, and wildlife by offering the highest quality hospital and diagnostic laboratory services. Equipped with the most technologically advanced facilities located on a university campus, the college is dedicated to safeguarding public health by studying emerging infectious diseases that affect both animal and human health. The Department of Small Animal Medicine and Surgery consists of 50 faculty members, 50 clinical residents, 10 rotating interns,8 specialty interns, and 3 administrative staff members. Shared laboratory space and technical support are provided within the department, and there are 7 dedicated research technicians who assist in the research missions of the department\u2019s faculty. Other specialties within the department include anesthesia, dermatology, internal medicine, nutrition, medical and radiation oncology, ophthalmology, orthopedic surgery, radiology, soft tissue surgery, and zoological medicine, as well as a community practice program ( UGA Pet Health Center). The Department participates in the college-wide M.S. and Ph.D. programs. Members of the department also actively participate in highly successful collaborative efforts with faculty members from other departments within the college and other colleges on campus, including the College of Public Health, College of Engineering, and the Athens campus of the Medical College of Georgia. The department has a strong track record for teaching, research, and clinical service. The University of Georgia is located in Athens, Georgia, and is approximately a one-hour drive going northeast from Atlanta. The campus is the nation\u2019s first chartered state-supported university and home of excellent academic programs, the Peabody Awards, and nationally recognized athletic teams. Athens is centered among beautiful surrounding counties with quaint towns, rural landscapes, and rich history. The area abounds in local art, music, literature, and theater, and offers many performances by national and international touring artists ( https://www.visitathensga.com/media/rankings-press-coverages/ and https://www.visitathensga.com/ ). The cost of living in Athens compares favorably with much of the rest of the country, ranking 17.6% lower than the U.S. average http://www.bestplaces.net/zipcode/georgia/athens/30601 . College/Unit/Department website www.vet.uga.edu Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Commensurate with Experience Anticipated Start Date 06/01/2024 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 12/11/2023 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Qualified applicants are invited to submit: (1) a letter of intent including professional interests and career goals, (2) a curriculum vitae, and (3) the name, mailing address, and contact information for three professional references. Questions regarding the position may be directed to ( quand003@uga.edu ) or telephone (706-202-5707). All applications received on or before March 1, 2024, will be fully considered; applications will be accepted until the position is filled. The successful candidate\u2019s employment starting date is negotiable; the position is available immediately. As required by the University of Georgia policy, the successful candidate will be subject to a background investigation. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track, Tenure Track, or Tenured Minimum Qualifications All candidates must have a DVM or equivalent degree. Position Summary The University of Georgia College of Veterinary Medicine invites applications for two faculty positions in small animal diagnostic imaging at the rank of clinical (non-tenure) or tenure track/tenured assistant, associate, or full professor. To be considered for the tenure track or tenured faculty ranks, documented research productivity commensurate with rank and an interest in developing a research program is required. For all candidates, salary and entry rank will be commensurate with the applicant\u2019s experience and qualifications. The major responsibilities of this position are to teach and provide service in the Veterinary Teaching Hospital, to teach pre-clinical didactic and laboratory courses in diagnostic imaging to veterinary students, to actively participate in the training of diagnostic imaging and other house officers, and to develop a research program, which can be independent and/or collaborative with other faculty members. Proportionate assignments for each area are based on the interests of the candidate, faculty assignment, and the missions of the Diagnostic Imaging program and the Department. Successful candidates will join two full-time radiologists. Locum tenens support in ultrasound, and virtual locum tenens support of service and resident training with VetCT, will continue until all diagnostic imaging faculty positions are filled. Our team includes four residents (starting July 2022), eight skilled registered veterinary technicians (two VTS -DI), a veterinary assistant, a PRN MRI technologist, and a full-time diagnostic imaging systems administrator. The goal is to have five full-time radiologists. The service currently enjoys the following equipment: a Siemens Skyra 3.0 Tesla MRI magnet and Siemens Somatom Sensation 64 slice CT, both of which accommodate large and small animals; GE Logiq-S8, Canon Aplio i700 and Toshiba Xario; Canon fluoroscopy, Canon digital radiography (3 DR Rooms), Canon RadPro portable DR unit; a dedicated interventional radiology suite with OEC 9900 Elite mobile C-arm fluoroscopy; IS2 Research NuCamma SR 53cm x 39 cm Free Floater gamma camera (Mirage nuclear medicine software); integrated DICOM viewing and archival system (Hyland NilRead viewer and Mach 7 VNA ); and MedQ RIS and Reporting software. For all candidates, salary and entry rank will be commensurate with the applicant\u2019s experience and qualifications. Additional Requirements All candidates must have completed an approved residency of the American College of Veterinary Radiology or the European College of Veterinary Diagnostic Imaging, and have board certification or be eligible for board certification. Requirements for appointment for Clinical Assistant, Associate, and Full Professors (non-tenure track) can be found in the Guidelines for Appointment and Promotion of Non-tenure Track Clinical Faculty in the Department of Small Animal Medicine and Surgery: https://provost.uga.edu/ resources/documents\u200c/\u200c\u200cSAMS_Guidelines_non-tenure_track_Modified_Oct_31 2012.pdf . Requirements for appointment for Assistant, Associate, and Full Professors (tenure track or tenured) can be found in the Guidelines for Faculty Development in the Department of Small Animal Medicine: https://provost.uga.edu/ resources/documents/Small_Animal_Medicine_and_Surgery 2015.pdf . Please note that the academic home for diagnostic imaging is in the Department of Small Animal Medicine and Surgery ( https://vet.uga.edu/education/academic-departments/small-animal-medicine-and-surgery/ ). To be eligible for tenure upon appointment, candidates must be appointed as an associate or full professor, have been tenured at a prior institution, and bring a demonstrable national reputation to the institution. Candidates must be approved for tenure upon appointment before hire. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? Yes Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Responsibilities will include didactic teaching and clinical training of veterinary medical students, house officers, and radiology residents. Teaching, service activities, and clinical responsibilities will be shared with other faculty radiologists. Interested candidates will have the opportunity for independent and collaborative research, basic science or clinical. Percentage Of Time 100 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/477986": {"title": "Assistant Research Scientist", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant Research Scientist Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant Research Scientist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F1195P Working Title Assistant Research Scientist Department VPR-Inst of Bioinformatics About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 04/01/2022 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 02/23/2022 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Researcher AC FLSA Faculty Rank Assistant Research Scientist Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications PhD in Chemistry, Biochemistry, Molecular Biology or related field Position Summary Research Scientist combining wet lab and computational approaches to analysis and understanding of protein structure and function. Additional Requirements Must be able to fund \u226590% of salary from current research contracts and grants with continued expectation at this level. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification At least 5 years of postdoctoral experience conducting research on the structure and function of proteins and training PhD students in the laboratory and computational analysis of the structure and function of proteins. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Ability to conduct wet lab and computational analysis for the structure and function of kinases. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Percentage Of Time 100 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509415": {"title": "Area Director-Rome", "description": "University of Georgia | Area Director-Rome Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Area Director-Rome Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The cover letter of application should address the following: Our employees say empathy\u2014an understanding of and service to others\u2014is important in their role at the SBDC. In your letter, please describe instances where empathy is evidenced in your work and discuss why you are interested in supporting the mission and culture of our organization. This position is open until filled. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2843P Working Title Area Director-Rome Department PSO-Small Business Dev Center About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary 90,000 Anticipated Start Date 01/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/15/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants The cover letter of application should address the following: Our employees say empathy\u2014an understanding of and service to others\u2014is important in their role at the SBDC . In your letter, please describe instances where empathy is evidenced in your work and discuss why you are interested in supporting the mission and culture of our organization. This position is open until filled. Location of Vacancy Outside Athens EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Public Service Professional AC FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in business related field. Position Summary Would you like to have an impact on your community and make a difference? Are you committed to service? Are you a strategic thinker with strong business acumen and leadership experience? Do you excel at managing teams, analyzing complex business challenges, and driving results? The University of Georgia Small Business Development Center ( SBDC ) in Rome, GA is seeking a highly motivated individual for a management-level, public service faculty position dedicated to helping Georgia businesses grow and prosper. We seek a skilled professional for a management-level, public service faculty position focused on business development and operational leadership, dedicated to helping Georgia businesses grow and prosper. As an Area Director, you will apply your broad base of business knowledge to deliver high-impact consulting, training, and strategic guidance to small businesses across your assigned territory. Responsibilities also include managing the Rome SBDC territory and office personnel. You will lead the daily operations of the Rome office, supervise, and ensure program excellence within the Rome County SBDC service area. This position involves multi-county travel and offers the opportunity to apply your expertise in a dynamic, collaborative environment. The salary is $90,000 with a comprehensive benefits package, including a defined benefits retirement plan. Additional Requirements Please see the UGA guidelines for Public Service and Outreach Academic Ranks at http://outreach.uga.edu/policies/appointment-and-promotion-guidelines/ Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Three years\u2019 experience of position-related responsibilities is necessary . A solid business education is required to consult with and train small business owners and entrepreneurs. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies A background in team management, financial analysis, business strategy, or entrepreneurship is highly desirable. Ideal candidates will bring a solid foundation in business theory and practice, along with exceptional interpersonal and communication skills. This role requires strong analytical capabilities, sound judgment, and the ability to manage multiple priorities effectively. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Provide high quality individual instruction to entrepreneurs, business owners, and business managers. Analyze situations, make recommendations, and educate clients with regard to business plans, market feasibility, financial viability, operations management, and legal structures, to name but a few topics. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Develop and deliver high quality business training programs that are responsive to the needs of the business community served. Generate curricula for business programs, seminars, conferences, etc. for the local business interests. Determine topics, agendas, instructors, instructional materials, location, time, and other resources required. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Engage in public relations activities such as, speeches, presentations, active committee participation, and direct discussions. Relevant audiences include bankers, colleges and universities, chambers of commerce, economic development authorities, main street coordinators, government agencies, local political offices, civic organizations, and local media. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Document activities via Client Information System ( CIS ) in a timely, accurate, and comprehensive manner. Collect and transmit consolidated CIS data. Maintain adequate client files as per SBA and SBDC guidelines. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Maintain efficient and effective operation of assigned area office, including management of personnel, budget, and other resources. Ensure that administrative policies are followed, that programs are innovative and responsive, and that top quality services are delivered. Utilize client and management feedback in striving for continuous improvement. Uphold contractual obligations with other institutions. Percentage Of Time Duties/Responsibilities Prepare and deploy action plans and individual work plans, assist in the organization\u2019s strategic plan, prepare Semi-Annual Reports, ensure that organizational goals and objectives are accomplished in a timely and thorough manner, active involvement on internal committees or special projects, serve as a guide and mentor to Business Consultants, seek and apply for grants relevant to entrepreneurship and business development, represent the SBDC State Director when required, and other duties as required. Percentage Of Time Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How did you hear about this employment opportunity? Public Job Posting Internal Job Posting Agency Referral Advertisement/Publication Personal Referral Website Other Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509382": {"title": "Associate Professor in Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, Synthetic Biology, and Metabolic Engineering", "description": "University of Georgia | Associate Professor in Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, Synthetic Biology, and Metabolic Engineering Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Associate Professor in Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, Synthetic Biology, and Metabolic Engineering Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications must include: 1) cover letter, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) statement of research interests and goals (up to 2 pages), and 4) a combined teaching and mentoring statement (up to 2 pages), which should integrate ideas and efforts that support UGA\u2019s values and enrich our missions of teaching, research, and service ( https://uga.edu/about/mission ). Candidates should also submit names and contact information for three references. The search committee will contact references after the initial screening of applications. Review of applications will begin on November 30, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Informal inquiries and questions may be addressed to the chair of the search committee, Christopher West ( westcm@uga.edu ) or the Head of BCMB, Dr. David J. Garfinkel ( djgarf@uga.edu ). Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2839P Working Title Associate Professor in Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, Synthetic Biology, and Metabolic Engineering Department Franklin-Biochemistry About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology ( BCMB ) is a multidisciplinary research-intensive academic unit comprised of over 60 affiliated members who lead innovative research programs across the spectrum of biochemistry and molecular biology. BCMB maintains internationally recognized and extramurally funded research programs in areas such as bioinformatics, structural biology, enzymology, epigenetics, cancer biology, glycobiology, science education, infectious disease, and molecular medicine. Faculty benefit from extensive departmental and university resources in genomics, bioinformatics, cryo-electron microscopy, X-ray crystallography, NMR , and cell production, including a bioexpression and fermentation facility. BCMB is within the Franklin College of Arts and Sciences, which is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The College has a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation. The School of Chemical, Materials & Biomedical Engineering ( CMBE ) fosters engineering education in a liberal arts setting and research that meets critical societal needs. The School offers ABET -accredited B.S. degrees in Biochemical Engineering and Biological Engineering, an M.S. in Biomanufacturing and Bioprocessing, and M.S. and Ph.D. programs in biochemical and biomedical engineering. It has grown to more than 500 students and 20 faculty members, with expertise spanning biomanufacturing and bioprocessing, metabolic and biochemical engineering, biomaterials, therapeutic devices, and diagnostics. The successful candidate will contribute to teaching and mentoring in both BCMB and CMBE , including CMBE\u2019s engineering programs. CMBE is within the College of Engineering, which is one of the fastest-growing public colleges of engineering in the nation. Since its founding in 2012, it has grown to nearly 5,500 engineering and computing students. The College focuses on learning, discovery, and innovation at the confluence of disciplines, building on partnerships across UGA\u2019s comprehensive land-grant campus. UGA is a prominent research-intensive land-, sea- and space-grant university, ranked among the top 20 public universities, and reported over $600 million in research expenditures in the last fiscal year. UGA is located in the vibrant city of Athens in the northern Piedmont region of Georgia. Athens is 65 miles east of Atlanta, less than two hours from the Chattahoochee National Forest and southern Appalachian Mountains, and within easy driving distance of the Atlantic coast. Athens is home to a thriving arts and music community and prides itself on its cultural diversity ( http://www.visitathensga.com ). College/Unit/Department website www.bmb.uga.edu, https://engineering.uga.edu/schools/school-of-chemical-materials-biomedical-engineering/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/15/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications must include: 1) cover letter, 2) curriculum vitae, 3) statement of research interests and goals (up to 2 pages), and 4) a combined teaching and mentoring statement (up to 2 pages), which should integrate ideas and efforts that support UGA\u2019s values and enrich our missions of teaching, research, and service ( https://uga.edu/about/mission ). Candidates should also submit names and contact information for three references. The search committee will contact references after the initial screening of applications. Review of applications will begin on November 30, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Informal inquiries and questions may be addressed to the chair of the search committee, Christopher West ( westcm@uga.edu ) or the Head of BCMB , Dr. David J. Garfinkel ( djgarf@uga.edu ). Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Associate Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Associate Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track or Tenured Minimum Qualifications Successful candidates will have a Ph.D. or equivalent in biochemistry, microbiology, chemical or biological engineering, or a related field. Position Summary Associate Professor in Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, Synthetic Biology, and Metabolic Engineering The Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology ( BCMB ) in the Franklin College and Arts and Sciences and the School of Chemical, Materials & Biomedical Engineering ( CMBE ) in the College of Engineering at the University of Georgia invite applications for a tenured or tenure-track faculty position at the rank of Associate Professor with a primary appointment in BCMB , beginning August 1, 2027. Candidates will be expected to maintain an internationally recognized, externally funded research program; contribute to the intellectual communities of BCMB and CMBE ; mentor graduate students and postdoctoral researchers; participate in undergraduate and graduate education; and engage in collaborative research across the University of Georgia. Additional Requirements Applicants must have qualifications and academic credentials that are commensurate with the promotion and tenure (P&T) guidelines at the UGA ( https://provost.uga.edu/faculty-affairs/promotion-tenure-evaluation/promotion-and-tenure/promotion-guidelines/ ). To be eligible for tenure upon appointment, candidates must be appointed as an associate professor, have been tenured at a prior institution, and bring a demonstrably international reputation to the institution. Candidates must be approved for tenure on appointment before hire. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies We seek an outstanding scientist whose work advances fundamental understanding of biological systems using biochemical, structural, molecular, evolutionary, computational and/or genomic approaches applied to cell-based synthetic biology, metabolic engineering, and bioprocess/fermentation engineering. Examples include engineering cells from eukaryotes, prokaryotes, and archaea to produce chemicals, fuels, materials, or therapeutics, from strain and pathway design to scale-up in bioprocess and fermentation systems. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509359": {"title": "Associate Professor or Professor in Experimental Condensed Matter Physics", "description": "University of Georgia | Associate Professor or Professor in Experimental Condensed Matter Physics Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Associate Professor or Professor in Experimental Condensed Matter Physics Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of research accomplishments and future research plans, statement of teaching and mentoring philosophy, and contact information for at least three professional references through the University of Georgia\u2019s official faculty recruitment portal. Review of applications will begin on December 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2846P Working Title Associate Professor or Professor in Experimental Condensed Matter Physics Department Franklin-Physics & Astronomy About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The University of Georgia is a leading public research university committed to excellence in research, teaching, and service. The Department of Physics and Astronomy offers a vibrant research environment with opportunities for interdisciplinary collaboration across the physical sciences, engineering, and related disciplines. The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The College has a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation. College/Unit/Department website https://www.physast.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/15/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of research accomplishments and future research plans, statement of teaching and mentoring philosophy, and contact information for at least three professional references through the University of Georgia\u2019s official faculty recruitment portal. Review of applications will begin on December 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank (Tenure Track) Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track or Tenured Minimum Qualifications Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in Physics or a closely related field. Position Summary The Department of Physics and Astronomy at the University of Georgia ( UGA ) invites applications for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position at the rank of Associate Professor or Full Professor in Experimental Condensed Matter Physics, with an anticipated start date of August 2027. Additional Requirements Applicants must have qualifications and academic credentials that are commensurate with the promotion and tenure (P&T) guidelines at the UGA ( https://provost.uga.edu/faculty-affairs/promotion-tenure-evaluation/promotion-and-tenure/promotion-guidelines/ ). To be eligible for tenure upon appointment, candidates must be appointed as an associate professor, have been tenured at a prior institution, and bring a demonstrably national reputation to the institution. Candidates must be approved for tenure upon appointment before hire. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies We seek outstanding experimental physicists with internationally recognized research accomplishments and a strong record of scientific leadership in one or more of the following areas: Quantum Materials Synthesis Quantum Devices and Device Physics Quantum Technologies, particularly those involving advanced materials synthesis, integration, and device development All areas within Electronic, Functional, and Quantum Materials synthesis and device physics are of interest, and candidates across this breadth are encouraged to apply. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research advances the discovery, synthesis, and understanding of novel materials and their integration into next-generation electronic, quantum, analog-computing and functional devices. Research programs that bridge fundamental materials physics with emerging quantum technologies are especially encouraged. Successful candidates are expected to have an internationally recognized research record, a demonstrated ability to establish and sustain a vigorous, externally funded research program, and a strong commitment to excellence in teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students. Candidates should demonstrate the potential to provide scientific leadership, develop interdisciplinary collaborations, and contribute to the continued growth and prominence of experimental condensed matter physics at UGA . Candidates for the Associate Professor rank should demonstrate a strong record of independent research, scholarly achievement, and external funding commensurate with the rank. Candidates for the Full Professor rank should have an established record of sustained research excellence, international recognition, scientific leadership, and successful mentorship. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509355": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Microbial Interactions", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant Professor of Microbial Interactions Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant Professor of Microbial Interactions Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Candidates should submit the following application materials electronically: (1) a cover letter; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) a statement of research interests and goals, up to two pages; (4) a teaching and mentorship statement, up to one page, addressing approaches to fostering a supportive learning environment; and (5) the names and contact information of three references, who will be asked to provide letters of recommendation. Questions regarding the position may be directed to the Search Committee at: dmdowns@uga.edu. Completed applications received by November 20, 2026, are assured full consideration. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2842P Working Title Assistant Professor of Microbial Interactions Department Franklin-Microbiology About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The Department of Microbiology and Franklin College have a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration, and academic innovation. Athens is a culturally diverse city renowned for its music, arts, and food scenes. It is located approximately one hour from Atlanta, less than two hours from the Blue Ridge Mountains, and within easy driving distance of the Atlantic coast. College/Unit/Department website https://mib.uga.edu/, https://nursing.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/13/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Candidates should submit the following application materials electronically: (1) a cover letter; (2) curriculum vitae; (3) a statement of research interests and goals, up to two pages; (4) a teaching and mentorship statement, up to one page, addressing approaches to fostering a supportive learning environment; and (5) the names and contact information of three references, who will be asked to provide letters of recommendation. Questions regarding the position may be directed to the Search Committee at: dmdowns@uga.edu. Completed applications received by November 20, 2026, are assured full consideration. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Assistant Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Assistant Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications A PhD (or equivalent) in Microbiology, Nursing, or a related field. Position Summary The Department of Microbiology and the School of Nursing at the University of Georgia invite applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor position in the broad area of Microbial Interactions with a start date of August 1, 2027. The ideal candidate will strengthen and expand connections of our current faculty with industrial and clinical colleagues and clientele. The successful candidate will contribute to the teaching, research, and service missions of the Department of Microbiology and the School of Nursing. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in microbiology as well as participating in service and student mentoring. Additional Requirements 1 or more years of postdoctoral experience is required at the time of appointment. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Specific research areas include but are not limited to; microbial interactions with human cells/tissues, microbial interactions with abiotic surfaces, microbe-microbe interactions with implications on human health and disease, metabolic processes driving microbial interactions, and assessment of new drug targets. We are especially interested in biologists who combine wet-bench experimentation with cutting edge global approaches to address significant issues in bioengineering, therapeutics, and/or basic microbiology. The most competitive applicants will have a strong research record, demonstrate a well-developed research plan, and exhibit a commitment to teaching at the graduate and undergraduate levels. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509317": {"title": "Associate Professor in Experimental Soft Condensed Matter Physics", "description": "University of Georgia | Associate Professor in Experimental Soft Condensed Matter Physics Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Associate Professor in Experimental Soft Condensed Matter Physics Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of research accomplishments and future research plans, statement of teaching and mentoring philosophy, and contact information for at least three professional references through the University of Georgia\u2019s official faculty recruitment portal. Review of applications will begin on December 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2845P Working Title Associate Professor in Experimental Soft Condensed Matter Physics Department Franklin-Physics & Astronomy About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The University of Georgia is a leading public research university offering an interdisciplinary research environment with opportunities for collaboration across physics, chemistry, engineering, biological sciences, medicine, and agricultural sciences. The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. With a vision for high-impact research and education, Franklin College prepares students for leadership and global engagement in a sustainable future. The College has a strong commitment to multidisciplinary research, collaboration and academic innovation. College/Unit/Department website https://www.physast.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/14/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of research accomplishments and future research plans, statement of teaching and mentoring philosophy, and contact information for at least three professional references through the University of Georgia\u2019s official faculty recruitment portal. Review of applications will begin on December 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Associate Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Associate Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track or Tenured Minimum Qualifications Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in Physics or a closely related field. Position Summary The Department of Physics and Astronomy at the University of Georgia ( UGA ) invites applications for a tenure-track or tenured faculty position at the rank of Associate Professor in Experimental Soft Condensed Matter Physics, with an anticipated start date of August 2027. The successful candidate is expected to establish and sustain a vigorous, externally funded research program, advance fundamental understanding of soft and functional materials, and develop interdisciplinary collaborations across the university. The candidate will also be expected to contribute to undergraduate and graduate teaching, mentor students and postdoctoral researchers, and participate in departmental and university service. Additional Requirements Applicants must have qualifications and academic credentials that are commensurate with the promotion and tenure (P&T) guidelines at the UGA ( https://provost.uga.edu/faculty-affairs/promotion-tenure-evaluation/promotion-and-tenure/promotion-guidelines/ ). To be eligible for tenure upon appointment, candidates must be appointed as an associate professor, have been tenured at a prior institution, and bring a demonstrably national reputation to the institution. Candidates must be approved for tenure upon appointment before hire. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Applicants must demonstrate a strong record of independent research accomplishments, scholarly productivity, external funding, and successful student mentorship commensurate with appointment at the Associate Professor level. We seek an outstanding experimental physicist with a strong record of research excellence and scientific leadership in soft condensed matter physics, particularly in areas involving polymers, transport phenomena, soft materials, microfluidics, and functional devices. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to: Polymer Physics and Transport Phenomena : Fundamental studies of ionic, molecular, and fluid transport in polymers, polymer networks, membranes, and soft materials. Polymer Synthesis and Functional Soft Materials : Design, synthesis, and characterization of polymers, hydrogels, responsive materials, and functional interfaces. Microfluidics and Soft-Matter Devices : Development of microfluidic platforms, lab-on-a-chip technologies, and soft-matter-based devices for transport, sensing, and manipulation of fluids and biological systems. Sensing and Biointegrated Devices : Development of novel sensing technologies, biosensors, and functional devices based on soft materials and polymeric systems. Surface and Interface Physics : Experimental investigations of polymer surfaces, interfaces, interfacial transport, and surface functionalization. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research combines fundamental soft condensed matter physics with innovative experimental approaches and applications at the interfaces of physics, medicine, biological sciences, plant biology, and agriculture. Candidates whose research can leverage UGA\u2019s interdisciplinary strengths and advanced research infrastructure, including its cleanroom and microfabrication facilities, are especially encouraged to apply. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509220": {"title": "Mary Frances Early Teacher Education Chair", "description": "University of Georgia | Mary Frances Early Teacher Education Chair Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Mary Frances Early Teacher Education Chair Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit all the following: A letter of application specifically responsive to the position\u2019s responsibilities and required qualifications as described above Statement of research interests describing current projects and activities as well as future plans and interests Curriculum vita Three most significant publications (combined and uploaded as one PDF) Contact information for three references (References will not be contacted until the applicant is notified) Questions regarding the position may be directed to Search Committee Chair, Dr. Shelby Cosner at Shelby.Cosner@uga.edu Priority consideration will be given to applications received by November 13, 2026. The search will remain open until the position is filled. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2844P Working Title Mary Frances Early Teacher Education Chair Department COE-Education Dean's Office About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Mary Frances Early College of Education is the fourth largest public college of education in the United States and the third largest college at the University of Georgia. Through instruction, research, and service, the College improves the lives of residents of Georgia and communities beyond the state. The College is comprehensive in scope, with academic disciplines encompassing teacher preparation, counseling and human development, communication sciences, human movement sciences, career development, student affairs, and educational administration and policy. Graduate education is a particular strength of the College, with approximately 40% of its students enrolled at the graduate level. The College provides a rich environment for interdisciplinary scholarship and collaboration, with opportunities for faculty to work across programs, departments, colleges, and professional communities to address complex educational and societal challenges. The University provides an intellectually vibrant environment for interdisciplinary scholarship, innovation, and engagement with communities throughout Georgia and beyond. College/Unit/Department website https://coe.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Commensurate with Experience Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/14/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit all the following: A letter of application specifically responsive to the position\u2019s responsibilities and required qualifications as described above Statement of research interests describing current projects and activities as well as future plans and interests Curriculum vita Three most significant publications (combined and uploaded as one PDF ) Contact information for three references (References will not be contacted until the applicant is notified) Questions regarding the position may be directed to Search Committee Chair, Dr. Shelby Cosner at Shelby.Cosner@uga.edu Priority consideration will be given to applications received by November 13, 2026. The search will remain open until the position is filled. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenured Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate in teacher education or a related field Position Summary The Mary Frances Early College of Education at the University of Georgia ( UGA ) invites applications and nominations for the Mary Frances Early Teacher Education Chair. This endowed faculty position, at the rank of professor, recognizes an accomplished scholar and leader in educator preparation, broadly construed to include teacher education fields (e.g., elementary education, secondary content areas, preK-12 fields such as special education, physical education) and other educator preparation fields (e.g., educational leadership, counselor education, school psychology). The successful candidate will be an established scholar and leader in an educator preparation field with a distinguished record of scholarship and demonstrated potential for advancing the national and international visibility of the Mary Frances Early College of Education and the University of Georgia. The Mary Frances Early Teacher Education Chair will develop and sustain a high-impact research agenda, contribute to innovative and bold approaches to educator preparation, mentor students and faculty, and build meaningful partnerships with educators and schools throughout Georgia. The appointment will be for a nine-month academic-year appointment, beginning August 1, 2027, or another mutually agreed-upon date. Additional Requirements An extensive and sustained program of research and a record of high-impact scholarly productivity in educator preparation Established record of securing external funding for research Eligibility for tenure and appointment at the rank of Professor Demonstrated record of teaching/mentoring graduate students and early career faculty National visibility and leadership in the field of educator preparation Evidence of developing productive partnerships among universities, schools, communities, or other educational organizations Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Sample Publications List of References with Contact Information Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509205": {"title": "Associate Vice President and Director of the Equal Opportunity Office (EOO)/Title IX Coordinator", "description": "University of Georgia | Associate Vice President and Director of the Equal Opportunity Office (EOO)/Title IX Coordinator Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Associate Vice President and Director of the Equal Opportunity Office (EOO)/Title IX Coordinator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicant screening will begin immediately. Candidates are encouraged to submit their materials by Sunday, October 25, 2026; however, screening will continue until the position is filled. The application packet should include a cover letter detailing how the applicant\u2019s credentials and experience meet the needs, responsibilities, and qualifications stated above; a current resume; and contact information for three references (who will not be contacted without further correspondence with the applicant). To request a descriptive Opportunity Profile for this position, provide a nomination, or seek additional information, please contact Paige Gates, Primary Consultant with the UGA Search Group, 229-326-5370 or Paige.Gates@uga.edu . Letters of recommendation or a simple nomination should include the name and contact information for the nominee. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2798P Working Title Associate Vice President and Director of the Equal Opportunity Office (EOO)/Title IX Coordinator Department UHR-HR Search Services About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 20 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department Equal Opportunity Office College/Unit/Department website https://eoo.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Commensurate with Experience Anticipated Start Date 01/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/11/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicant screening will begin immediately. Candidates are encouraged to submit their materials by Sunday, October 25, 2026; however, screening will continue until the position is filled. The application packet should include a cover letter detailing how the applicant\u2019s credentials and experience meet the needs, responsibilities, and qualifications stated above; a current resume; and contact information for three references (who will not be contacted without further correspondence with the applicant). To request a descriptive Opportunity Profile for this position, provide a nomination, or seek additional information, please contact Paige Gates, Primary Consultant with the UGA Search Group, 229-326-5370 or Paige.Gates@uga.edu . Letters of recommendation or a simple nomination should include the name and contact information for the nominee. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Director, Division / Department AD FLSA Faculty Rank Administrative Faculty Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Law degree (JD) from an American Bar Association accredited law school and an active member in good standing of the State Bar of Georgia or another state bar. Six years of progressive experience in the legal or compliance field. Position Summary The University of Georgia ( UGA ) invites applications and nominations for the position of Associate Vice President and Director of the Equal Opportunity Office/Title IX Coordinator. The Associate Vice President and Director of the Equal Opportunity Office ( EOO ) is responsible for ensuring the University provides a fair and respectful environment for students, faculty, and staff that is free from discrimination and harassment on the basis of protected categories. The Director also holds the positions of Title IX Coordinator and ADA /Section 504 Coordinator. The Associate Vice President and Director supervises the Equal Opportunity Office and is responsible for managing, and providing analysis and guidance with respect to, all institutional compliance efforts with federal and state laws and regulations addressing discrimination and harassment, as well as with University System of Georgia and UGA nondiscrimination policies, including the development of policies and procedures governing the reporting, investigation, and adjudication of claims of discrimination, harassment, and sexual misconduct. The Associate Vice President and Director also oversees EOO\u2019s mission to educate the University community about discrimination and harassment, as well as participating in the University\u2019s prevention programs. The Associate Vice President and Director reports directly to the President of the University with a dotted-line report to the Vice President and Chief Human Resources Officer. The Associate Vice President and Director supervises the staff of the Equal Opportunity Office, including several investigators, an associate director for informal resolution and conflict management, a case manager, and an office manager. Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Experience with civil rights, employment law, equal opportunity work, and/or higher education. Proven experience and technical expertise in investigation, resolution, and remediation of complaints of discrimination and harassment. Experience with building and delivering education, training, and prevention programs in the areas of non-discrimination and harassment. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Knowledge of the organizational environment of higher education and large research universities. Proven ability to serve as the principal campus advisor to senior management regarding policies, procedures, and programs that have a campus-wide impact. Subject matter expert on civil rights, anti-discrimination, and harassment matters in higher education as they relate to the University community and experience managing institutional compliance and providing guidance on relevant antidiscrimination, harassment, and civil rights laws, including, but not limited to, Title IX, Title VII , the ADA , and other applicable laws and regulations. Demonstrated analytical, communication, problem-solving, project planning and implementation skills and ability to lead a team of investigators and trainers. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? Yes Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Develops and maintains campus-wide non-discrimination, anti-harassment, and sexual misconduct policies and procedures governing the reporting, investigation, and adjudication of complaints of discrimination and harassment on the basis of an individual\u2019s age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status (\u201cprotected status\u201d), including the determination and implementation of supportive or interim measures; oversight of the investigation process; implementation of remedies and sanctions; and responding to requests for access to relevant records. Provides strategic guidance, decision-making, and necessary training pertaining to compliance with all federal and state laws and regulations, Board of Regents policies, and University policies relating to discrimination and harassment on the basis of an individual\u2019s protected status. Advises appropriate units, including the Accessibility and Testing office and the Division of Human Resources, on employee, student and external guest and visitor requests for accommodations under the ADA , Section 504, and other applicable disability laws. Manages University\u2019s response to federal and state civil rights investigations. Selects, trains, and oversees EOO staff members, including investigators and specialists. Oversees the University\u2019s compliance with applicable affirmative action requirements, coordinating with the Division of Human Resources and the Office of Faculty Affairs to ensure that employment practices operate in a nondiscriminatory manner and that applicable procedures are followed. Serves on various University committees, as requested, particularly those related to the prevention of prohibited discrimination and harassment. Percentage Of Time 100 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/CV List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Other Documents #1 Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/510385": {"title": "Assistant Research Scientist in Herpetology", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant Research Scientist in Herpetology Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant Research Scientist in Herpetology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To ensure full consideration, candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of research interests, unofficial transcripts of all college-level work, copies of up to three recent relevant publications, and contact information for three references. Review of complete applications will begin on November 22, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Individuals considered for potential interviews will be required to submit official college transcripts and three reference letters. University policy requires all candidates to consent to a background investigation (www.hr.uga.edu). Finalists will be required to provide a signed consent form authorizing the University to conduct a background check. The background investigation will be conducted on a post offer/pre-employment basis. The starting date is negotiable but a spring 2027 start date is desired. All applicants MUST apply online. No paper applications will be accepted. For further questions, please contact Dr. XIAOYU XU, Chair, Assistant Research Scientist in Herpetology Search Committee, Savannah River Ecology Laboratory, Drawer E, Aiken, SC29802, xiaoyuxu@UGA.EDU Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2856P Working Title Assistant Research Scientist in Herpetology Department VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department Savannah River Ecology Laboratory : The successful candidate will be located at the Savannah River Ecology Laboratory in Aiken, SC. The Savannah River Ecology Laboratory is a research unit of the University of Georgia located on the 300 mi2 Savannah River Site, a Department of Energy facility near Aiken, SC. With a staff of over 200 faculty members, postdocs, research professionals, technicians, and graduate students, the laboratory pursues basic and applied research at multiple levels of ecological organization, from atoms to ecosystems. SREL also provides opportunities for graduate and undergraduate research training, and service to the community through environmental outreach. Throughout its 75+ year history SREL has strived to acquire and communicate knowledge that contributes to sound ecological stewardship. College/Unit/Department website srel.uga.edu Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 01/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/23/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants To ensure full consideration, candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of research interests, unofficial transcripts of all college-level work, copies of up to three recent relevant publications, and contact information for three references. Review of complete applications will begin on November 22, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Individuals considered for potential interviews will be required to submit official college transcripts and three reference letters. University policy requires all candidates to consent to a background investigation (www.hr.uga.edu). Finalists will be required to provide a signed consent form authorizing the University to conduct a background check. The background investigation will be conducted on a post offer/pre-employment basis. The starting date is negotiable but a spring 2027 start date is desired. All applicants MUST apply online. No paper applications will be accepted. For further questions, please contact Dr. XIAOYU XU, Chair, Assistant Research Scientist in Herpetology Search Committee, Savannah River Ecology Laboratory, Drawer E, Aiken, SC29802, xiaoyuxu@UGA. EDU Location of Vacancy Augusta Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Researcher AC FLSA Faculty Rank Assistant Research Scientist Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Applicants must have a PhD in an appropriate field (Biology, Wildlife Ecology, Ecology, or related field). Position Summary The University of Georgia\u2019s Savannah River Ecology ( SREL ) invites applications for an Academic-Year (9-month) position as an Assistant Research Scientist. The successful applicant will be located at the Savannah River Ecology Laboratory in Aiken, S.C. and will report to the Director of the Savannah River Ecology Laboratory. This position will be 0.11 FTE in Instruction, 0.67 FTE in research, 0.11 FTE in Service, and 0.11 FTE in Program Administration. Funding for this position will be provided by SREL , which is supported in part through a cooperative agreement with the Department of Energy, and the University of Georgia Research Institute, a research unit focused on enhancing UGA\u2019s relationships with federal mission driven agencies. The successful candidate is expected to develop an extramurally funded and internationally recognized research program focused in herpetology, with focal disciplinary expertise in ecophysiology, ecotoxicology, risk assessment, and conservation. The successful candidate will be expected to serve as courtesy faculty and a member of the graduate faculty in an applicable department or school at UGA and will be involved in graduate instruction via advising of graduate students and service on graduate student committees. Professional service to groups such as state and federal agencies, non-governmental organizations, professional societies, and the public also is expected, as is significant interaction with colleagues and students in other disciplines represented at SREL , UGA , and the broader academic community. The successful candidate also will be expected to maintain a research program that complies with all applicable regulatory and reporting requirements pertinent to the Savannah River Site, state, and federal regulations. Must possess a valid drivers license. Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Applicants must have a . The candidate should have a , as well as demonstrated expertise in ecophysiology and ecotoxicology and a broad understanding of risk assessment as related to the biotic fate and transport of contaminants in the environment. Preference will be given to candidates having a record of excellence in research and service commensurate with time since degree, and postdoctoral experience is highly desired. Past funding success with federal mission agencies such as SERDP and DOE is preferred. Applicants with expertise in ecophysiology, ecotoxicology, and risk assessment in turtles and snakes are especially encouraged to apply. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Knowledge of research methods in ecophysiology and ecotoxicology Knowledge of conservation concerns for reptiles Knowledge of statistical analyses for ecotoxicological risk assessment Technical and Laboratory skills needed to conduct field and laboratory studies on reptiles Technical writing skills for publication of manuscripts in the peer reviewed scientific literature Technical skills in project development and management Technical skills in grant writing for acquisition of external funding to support research efforts, graduate students, and technical staff Critical thinking ability for identification of complex problems, formation of research hypotheses, and development of innovative research studies and experiments Ability to communicate complex scientific concepts clearly both in writing and verbally Ability to collaborate productively within multidisciplinary teams and as a mentor to graduate students and technical research staff Demonstrated potential for research Strong background in herpetology and species conservation Demonstrated expertise in ecophysiology and ecotoxicology Broad understanding of risk assessment as related to the biotic fate and transport of contaminants in the environment Ability to interact with colleagues from a diversity of disciplines on the development of research proposals related to the conservation of reptile species as well as to the quantification of the physiological and toxicological risks of contaminant exposure in reptiles Preference will be given to candidates having a record of excellence in research and service commensurate with time since degree, and postdoctoral work is highly desired. Past funding success with federal mission agencies such as SERDP and DOE is preferred. Applicants with expertise in ecophysiology, ecotoxicology, and risk assessment in turtles and snakes are especially encouraged to apply. Physical Demands Lift 50 pounds Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? Yes Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Develop a well funded, productive research program that leads to the development of successful grant proposals, publication of peer reviewed journal articles, and advisement and successful communication of research results to stakeholders and the general public. Percentage Of Time 67 Duties/Responsibilities Develop a funded research program that involves advising and mentoring of graduate students leading to successful completion of graduate degree programs and publication of research results Percentage Of Time 11 Duties/Responsibilities Engage in service to SREL , UGA , professional scientific societies, and similar entities that enhances scientific reputation and professional development as a research scientist and faculty member at SREL . Percentage Of Time 11 Duties/Responsibilities Operate a research and graduate education program that complies with all regulatory compliance requirements mandated by applicable state, federal and university sources. Perform administrative tasks associated with permitting, regulatory compliance, and reporting in a timely manner that meets established deadlines as applicable. Operate a graduate advising program that meets the expectations and deadlines for degree granting units on the main UGA campus in a timely manner. Perform all required supervisory tasks as required by UGA pertinent to hiring, disciplinary actions, annual reviews, and other related tasks as mandated by UGA policies and in a timely manner. Percentage Of Time 11 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you possess a valid driver's license? No Response No Yes Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Sample Publications Unofficial Transcripts List of References with Contact Information Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/510379": {"title": "Open Rank Faculty - Hardware for AI, Smart Sensors and Microelectronics", "description": "University of Georgia | Open Rank Faculty - Hardware for AI, Smart Sensors and Microelectronics Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Open Rank Faculty - Hardware for AI, Smart Sensors and Microelectronics Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants are asked to submit the following information along with their application: A detailed curriculum vita. A cover letter (not to exceed one page) addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relative to the responsibilities of the position. A teaching statement not to exceed 2 pages. A statement of research expertise not to exceed 2 pages The names, titles, and contact information for a minimum of three professional references. Inquiries about the position should be directed to the chair of the search committee Dr. Kyle Johnsen ( kjohnsen@uga.edu ) in the College of Engineering. Review of applications will begin on December 1st, 2026; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Selected applicants will be required to submit transcripts and a background investigation demonstrating eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2857P Working Title Open Rank Faculty - Hardware for AI, Smart Sensors and Microelectronics Department ENGR-Electrical & Computer About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department Faculty hired as part of this initiative will join a rapidly growing College of Engineering that combines interdisciplinary research and scholarship with excellent instruction and service. The UGA College of Engineering currently enrolls over 3,000 engineering majors and has 121 full-time engineering faculty across 15 degree programs. The college also jointly administers the School of Computing in collaboration with the UGA Franklin College of Arts and Sciences, an academic unit that comprises over 1800 computer science majors and 45 full-time faculty. The College of Engineering is comprised of four interdisciplinary schools: the School of Chemical, Materials, and Biomedical Engineering; School of Electrical and Computer Engineering; School of Environmental, Civil, Agricultural, and Mechanical Engineering; and School of Computing. Significant investments in infrastructure have resulted in an expansion of laboratory facilities for research and scholarship and new classrooms and instructional labs. College of Engineering faculty have space in two major capital projects on campus to create interdisciplinary research facilities. Our main instructional facility, Driftmier Engineering Center, has also undergone a complete renovation to create flexible classrooms that enable a range of teaching modalities and the incorporation of interdisciplinary instructional labs. The common instructional facilities also foster collaboration by allowing faculty, staff, and students to interact and collaborate in a single facility. College/Unit/Department website engr.uga.edu/schools/sece Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/23/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants are asked to submit the following information along with their application: A detailed curriculum vita. A cover letter (not to exceed one page) addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relative to the responsibilities of the position. A teaching statement not to exceed 2 pages. A statement of research expertise not to exceed 2 pages The names, titles, and contact information for a minimum of three professional references. Inquiries about the position should be directed to the chair of the search committee Dr. Kyle Johnsen ( kjohnsen@uga.edu ) in the College of Engineering. Review of applications will begin on December 1st, 2026; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Selected applicants will be required to submit transcripts and a background investigation demonstrating eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track or Tenured Minimum Qualifications All candidates must have a Ph.D. in electrical engineering, computer engineering, computer science or related discipline. Position Summary The College of Engineering at the University of Georgia invites applications for a single position at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor with expertise in hardware for engineering applications of Artificial Intelligence (AI) systems, smart sensors, or modern microelectronic devices and systems. The College seeks qualified applicants to fill an open-rank, 9-month tenured or tenure-track faculty position beginning August 1, 2027. The position will have the opportunity to supplement salary during the summer. This position will be centered in the College of Engineering\u2019s School of Electrical & Computer Engineering ( ECE ) and will be supervised by the School Chair of ECE . The new faculty member will be expected to develop a vigorous, high-impact, externally funded research program; work closely with existing faculty; effectively mentor graduate students and postdoctoral scientists; and effectively support our teaching mission at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Additional Requirements Candidates considered for the associate or full professor ranks must have qualifications and academic credentials commensurate with the promotion and tenure guidelines at the University of Georgia . To be eligible for tenure upon appointment, candidates must be appointed as an associate or full professor, have been tenured at a prior institution, and bring a demonstrably national reputation to the institution. Candidates must be approved for tenure upon appointment before hire. For information about the requirements for each faculty rank, please see the UGA Guidelines for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies A demonstrated record of research and scholarly achievement appropriate to rank (evidenced by peer-reviewed publications). Building on its areas of key research strength, the College seeks to identify highly qualified candidates with expertise in sensors, microelectronics or hardware for future engineering applications of AI such as edge AI accelerators, low-power sensor nodes, or in-sensor computing with a research focus in current areas of high societal impact. The ideal candidate also has interests that support application of their research expertise in areas of strength within the UGA College of Engineering including Integrative Precision Agriculture, Advanced Manufacturing or Electric Mobility. Furthermore, the ideal candidate has demonstrated capacity to work collaboratively with existing faculty at the University of Georgia, including faculty in cross-cutting units such as the new Institute for Integrative Precision Agriculture , the Advance Manufacturing and Innovation Factory, the Georgia Network for E-Mobility and the Institute for Artificial Intelligence , among others. Applicants with strong background developing industry collaborations are highly encouraged to apply. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/510325": {"title": "Assistant Research Scientist", "description": "University of Georgia | Assistant Research Scientist Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Assistant Research Scientist Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested individuals should apply along with the following information as a single PDF file in the \u201cOther Documents #1\u201d section: A detailed curriculum vitae A cover letter addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relating to the responsibilities of the position with a summary of research accomplishments and future goals (2-page max) The names, titles, and contact information for three professional references Questions about the position should be directed to: Duo Zhang, Ph.D. Associate Professor The University of Georgia College of Pharmacy 1120 Fifteenth St. HM Bldg Rm 117 Augusta, GA 30912 Email: duozhang@uga.edu Phone: 706-721-6491 Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2775P Working Title Assistant Research Scientist Department Pharmacy-Clin & Admin Pharmacy About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The College of Pharmacy at the University of Georgia ( UGA ) is a distinguished institution known for its excellence in pharmacy education, research, and community service ( https://rx.uga.edu/ ). We are at the forefront of pharmaceutical research, with faculty and students engaged in groundbreaking studies that contribute to advancements in healthcare and medicine. Research areas include drug discovery, pharmacology, and clinical pharmacy. The college is highly ranked, placing 16th out of 140 pharmacy programs nationwide according to US News & World Report, underscoring our reputation for excellence. These elements make the UGA College of Pharmacy a unique and enriching place for students to pursue their pharmacy education and careers. College/Unit/Department website https://rx.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 05/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 08/18/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Interested individuals should apply along with the following information as a single PDF file in the \u201cOther Documents #1\u201d section: A detailed curriculum vitae A cover letter addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relating to the responsibilities of the position with a summary of research accomplishments and future goals (2-page max) The names, titles, and contact information for three professional references Questions about the position should be directed to: Duo Zhang, Ph.D. Associate Professor The University of Georgia College of Pharmacy 1120 Fifteenth St. HM Bldg Rm 117 Augusta, GA 30912 Email: duozhang@uga.edu Phone: 706-721-6491 Location of Vacancy Augusta Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Researcher AC FLSA Faculty Rank Assistant Research Scientist Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Should be Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in Pharmaceutical Sciences, Biomedical Sciences, Pharmacology, Molecular Biology, Cell Biology, Physiology, or a closely related field. Position Summary The University of Georgia College of Pharmacy seeks an outstanding candidate for a full-time Assistant Research Scientist position to contribute to the College\u2019s expanding biomedical and translational research mission at the UGA Augusta Campus . This is a 12-month, non-tenure-track faculty appointment within the University of Georgia Research Scientist Track. The successful candidate will lead and support innovative research focused on the molecular, cellular, and physiological mechanisms underlying pulmonary diseases, including inflammatory, infectious, fibrotic, and chronic respiratory disorders. The Assistant Research Scientist will be responsible for designing and executing laboratory-based studies, developing novel scientific approaches, analyzing and interpreting complex datasets, and disseminating research findings through peer-reviewed publications and scientific presentations. Additional responsibilities include contributing to sponsored research programs through the preparation of grant proposals and progress reports, collaborating with faculty, research staff, students, and external partners, and providing mentorship and scientific guidance to research trainees. Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Minimum 1 year of postdoctoral research experience in biomedical, pharmaceutical, translational, or pulmonary research. Must possess a strong foundation in molecular biology, cell biology, pharmacology, and translational biomedical research. Preference will be given to candidates with expertise in pulmonary biology, respiratory disease, inflammation, fibrosis, infectious diseases, asthma, COPD , acute lung injury, ARDS , or related disciplines. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Comprehensive knowledge of molecular, cellular, and translational biomedical research, including pulmonary disease mechanisms, inflammatory signaling, infectious disease biology, tissue remodeling, and therapeutic development. Demonstrated ability to formulate scientific hypotheses, design and conduct independent research studies, analyze data, and translate findings into publications, presentations, and funding opportunities. Expertise in molecular and cellular laboratory techniques, including PCR , qPCR, cloning, gene and protein expression analysis, Western blotting, mammalian cell culture, functional assays, flow cytometry, histology, immunohistochemistry, and related methodologies. Demonstrated proficiency in animal research models and procedures relevant to pulmonary and translational biomedical research. Strong scientific writing and communication skills, with a record of preparing manuscripts, abstracts, technical reports, presentations, and grant applications. Proven ability to manage multiple research priorities, projects, and deadlines effectively. Demonstrated ability to establish productive interdisciplinary collaborations within a team-based research environment. Strong mentoring and leadership capabilities that support the development of undergraduate, graduate, professional, and postdoctoral trainees. Knowledge of laboratory safety requirements, biosafety standards, animal research regulations, research integrity principles, and regulatory compliance requirements. Record of scholarly achievement demonstrated through peer-reviewed publications, scientific contributions, and grant-supported research activities. Potential to contribute to the growth and sustainability of an externally funded, nationally recognized research program. Physical Demands Ability to perform laboratory-based research activities for extended periods. Ability to safely handle laboratory equipment, biological materials, and research specimens. Ability to lift and transport laboratory supplies and equipment up to established University guidelines. Ability to work in laboratory environments involving exposure to chemicals, biological agents, and animal research facilities while adhering to established safety procedures. Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Research Program Development and Execution Design, develop, and conduct independent and collaborative research studies focused on pulmonary disease mechanisms and therapeutic interventions. Develop innovative experimental approaches utilizing molecular, cellular, biochemical, and translational research methodologies. Generate, analyze, interpret, and present complex scientific data to support project objectives and scientific advancement. Ensure compliance with sponsor requirements, regulatory standards, and institutional research policies. Contribute scientific expertise to multidisciplinary research collaborations. Percentage Of Time 60 Duties/Responsibilities Scholarship and Sponsored Research Prepare and submit manuscripts, abstracts, technical reports, and scientific communications for dissemination of research findings. Present research findings at scientific meetings, seminars, and professional conferences. Assist in the preparation and submission of extramural funding proposals, renewal applications, and progress reports. Generate preliminary data and scientific rationale to support future funding initiatives. Contribute to activities that enhance the national visibility and scholarly reputation of the College of Pharmacy. Percentage Of Time 20 Duties/Responsibilities Mentorship and Research Training Mentor undergraduate students, PharmD students, graduate students, and other trainees participating in research programs. Provide instruction and guidance regarding laboratory procedures, research methodologies, data analysis, and scientific communication. Foster a collaborative and inclusive research environment that supports trainee development and scientific excellence. Assist trainees with research presentations, publications, and professional development activities. Percentage Of Time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Laboratory Administration and Research Service Assist with laboratory operations, equipment management, procurement, and resource coordination. Ensure compliance with laboratory safety standards, biosafety requirements, animal care regulations, and institutional research policies. Support departmental and college research initiatives through participation in committees, research meetings, and collaborative activities. Contribute to strategic efforts that enhance research productivity, infrastructure, and multidisciplinary collaborations. Percentage Of Time 10 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Other Documents #1 Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/510305": {"title": "Open Rank - AI-Enabled Robotics and Advanced Manufacturing", "description": "University of Georgia | Open Rank - AI-Enabled Robotics and Advanced Manufacturing Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Open Rank - AI-Enabled Robotics and Advanced Manufacturing Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2026; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Inquiries about the position should be directed to Dr. Jaime Camelio, chair of the search committee, at jcamelio@uga.edu. Applicants are asked to submit the following information along with their application: A cover letter (not to exceed two pages) addressing the candidate's experience relative to the responsibilities of the position. A detailed curriculum vitae. A research statement (not to exceed three pages) that includes the candidate's vision for building collaborative, externally funded programs at UGA. A teaching statement (not to exceed two pages). The names, titles, and contact information for five professional references. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2860P Working Title Open Rank - AI-Enabled Robotics and Advanced Manufacturing Department ENGR-Civil & Environmental About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The UGA College of Engineering currently enrolls over 3,000 engineering majors and has 125 full-time engineering faculty across 15 degree programs. The College also jointly administers the School of Computing in collaboration with the UGA Franklin College of Arts and Sciences, an academic unit that comprises over 1,700 computer science majors and 44 full-time faculty. Beginning in January 2027, the College of Engineering will comprise five interdisciplinary schools: the School of Computing, the School of Chemical, Materials, and Biomedical Engineering; the School of Electrical and Computer Engineering; the School of Civil and Environmental Engineering; and the School of Mechanical and Agricultural Engineering. Faculty hired as part of this initiative will join a rapidly growing College of Engineering that combines interdisciplinary research and scholarship with excellent instruction and service. Significant investments in infrastructure have resulted in an expansion of laboratory facilities for research and scholarship and new classrooms and instructional labs. College of Engineering faculty have space in two major capital projects on campus to create interdisciplinary research facilities. Our main instructional facility, Driftmier Engineering Center, has also undergone a complete renovation to create flexible classrooms that enable a range of teaching modalities and the incorporation of interdisciplinary instructional labs. The common instructional facilities also foster collaboration by allowing faculty, staff, and students to interact and collaborate in a single facility. College/Unit/Department website engr.uga.edu/schools/ecam Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/23/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2026; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Inquiries about the position should be directed to Dr. Jaime Camelio, chair of the search committee, at jcamelio@uga.edu. Applicants are asked to submit the following information along with their application: A cover letter (not to exceed two pages) addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relative to the responsibilities of the position. A detailed curriculum vitae. A research statement (not to exceed three pages) that includes the candidate\u2019s vision for building collaborative, externally funded programs at UGA . A teaching statement (not to exceed two pages). The names, titles, and contact information for five professional references. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank (Tenure Track) Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track or Tenured Minimum Qualifications An earned doctorate in mechanical, industrial, electrical, agricultural, or a closely related engineering field, or in computer science or robotics. Position Summary The College of Engineering at the University of Georgia invites applications for a nine-month (academic year), tenure-track or tenured faculty position at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor in artificial intelligence enabled robotics and advanced manufacturing, to begin August 1, 2027. We seek an energetic, accomplished researcher who builds programs, teams, and partnerships, and who will help shape a fast-growing manufacturing and robotics cluster at UGA . The position will be housed in the School of Environmental, Civil, Agricultural, and Mechanical Engineering ( ECAM ), which is reorganizing into two schools; this position will reside in the new School of Mechanical and Agricultural Engineering and report to its School Chair. The position includes the opportunity to supplement salary during the summer. Candidates considered for the associate or full professor rank must have qualifications and academic credentials commensurate with promotion guidelines at the University of Georgia. The successful candidate will lead an externally funded research program at the intersection of artificial intelligence, robotics, and advanced manufacturing, and will serve as principal investigator or lead investigator on large, multi-institution proposals such as NSF Industry-University Cooperative Research Centers, Department of Energy and Department of Defense manufacturing programs, USDA coordinated agricultural projects, and industry consortia. The College has established strength in AI for manufacturing systems, digital twins, and manufacturing testbeds through the Manufacturing Living Labs, along with programs in additive manufacturing and composites, optical sensing for manufacturing, smart manufacturing, and nanomanufacturing for flexible sensing. We are especially interested in candidates whose work complements these strengths through physical robotic systems and automation. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, robotic manipulation and grasping; robot learning and perception; mobile and field robotics for unstructured environments; human-robot collaboration; intelligent and adaptive manufacturing processes; in-process sensing, monitoring, and control; and automation for agricultural, food processing, and other biological systems. Agriculture is Georgia\u2019s largest industry, and poultry, produce, and food processing operations across the state are seeking automation that works in variable, unstructured settings. UGA is unusually well positioned to lead in this area, with a College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences, a statewide Cooperative Extension network, and an engineering school with agricultural engineering in its faculty. The successful candidate will engage with Georgia AIM , the University\u2019s Institute for Artificial Intelligence, and partners in the College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences, and will mentor early-career faculty and doctoral students. This position is part of a campus-wide presidential hiring initiative that builds on the economic development opportunities within Georgia and the southeast region. Georgia\u2019s manufacturing base is growing rapidly, with major recent investments in vehicles, batteries, and energy technologies, including Hyundai Motor Group Metaplant America near Savannah, SK Battery America in Commerce, and Qcells solar manufacturing in Dalton and Cartersville. These are joined by established sectors in aerospace, food processing, and advanced materials. The state\u2019s multimodal transportation network, including Hartsfield-Jackson Atlanta International Airport, an expanding port in Savannah, and a robust interstate highway system, makes Georgia a manufacturing and logistics hub for the region. The University of Georgia\u2019s statewide reach into industry and communities positions it to help these employers adopt AI and robotics and to train the workforce they need. Additional Requirements A record commensurate with appointment at the rank of Associate Professor or Professor with tenure at a research university, including sustained external funding as principal investigator and a strong record of peer-reviewed publication. Demonstrated expertise at the intersection of artificial intelligence or machine learning and robotics, automation, or advanced manufacturing. Candidates must also have a documented research background appropriate for the appointment rank, as evidenced by peer-reviewed publications. For information about the requirements for each faculty rank, please see the UGA Guidelines for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure . To be eligible for tenure upon appointment, candidates must be appointed at the rank of associate professor or professor, have been tenured at a prior institution, and bring a demonstrable national reputation to the institution. Candidates must be approved for tenure upon appointment before hire. Specific criteria for Associate Professor and Professor level are summarized here . Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies A demonstrated record of leading collaborative research teams and large, multi-investigator proposals; a demonstrated record of building partnerships with industry; a demonstrated record of mentoring junior faculty and doctoral students; a demonstrated record of research or applied work in agricultural, food systems, or biological applications; strong communication and leadership skills to represent the program to industry, government, and the public. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/510261": {"title": "Lecturer", "description": "University of Georgia | Lecturer Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Lecturer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications received by November 23, 2026, are assured of full consideration; however, applications will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Interested candidates should upload a cover letter, a vitae, a teaching portfolio/philosophy, and contact information for three references (including email address). References will be contacted at the appropriate time during the search process. Applications submitted in other ways will not be considered. Review of applications will continue until the position has been filled. Initial interviews will be conducted via Skype or Zoom. Review of applications will continue until the position has been filled. Questions about the position can be directed to the search committee chair, Professor Greg Eaton (geaton@uga.edu). Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2859P Working Title Lecturer Department Terry-Finance About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website https://www.terry.uga.edu/departments/finance/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 01/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/22/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applications received by November 23, 2026, are assured of full consideration; however, applications will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Interested candidates should upload a cover letter, a vitae, a teaching portfolio/philosophy, and contact information for three references (including email address). References will be contacted at the appropriate time during the search process. Applications submitted in other ways will not be considered. Review of applications will continue until the position has been filled. Initial interviews will be conducted via Skype or Zoom. Review of applications will continue until the position has been filled. Questions about the position can be directed to the search committee chair, Professor Greg Eaton (geaton@uga.edu). Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Lecturer FLSA Faculty Rank Lecturer Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Doctoral degree in finance or a related discipline from an AACSB accredited institution or international equivalent. See Additional Requirements for more information. Position Summary The Department of Finance in the Terry College of Business at The University of Georgia invites applications for a full-time non-tenure-track faculty position at the lecturer level. The position will begin in the spring semester of 2027, with an anticipated employment start date of January 1, 2027. Additional Requirements Candidates should have a Master\u2019s or doctoral degree in finance or a related discipline from an AACSB accredited institution or international equivalent. Candidates with a master\u2019s degree must document exceptional accomplishments in finance or a related area and must be approved for a terminal degree exception before hire. The position is renewable based on performance and promotion to Senior Lecturer is possible after six years of service. For information regarding the requirements for each faculty rank, please see the University of Georgia Guidelines for Appointment and Promotion of Lecturers . Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification The successful candidate will have ten or more years of working experience in the investment banking or private equity areas. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Demonstrated ability to teach investment banking or private equity materials to undergraduate students. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/CV Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/510239": {"title": "Associate Professor - Materials Engineering - Next Generation Materials for Advancing Health", "description": "University of Georgia | Associate Professor - Materials Engineering - Next Generation Materials for Advancing Health Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Associate Professor - Materials Engineering - Next Generation Materials for Advancing Health Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants are asked to submit the following information along with their application: A cover letter (not to exceed two pages) addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relative to the responsibilities of the position. A detailed curriculum vita A research plan not to exceed three pages. A combined teaching and mentoring statement not to exceed two pages. The names, titles, and contact information for three professional references. All these materials should integrate ideas and efforts that support UGA\u2019s values and enrich our missions of teaching, research, and service ( https://uga.edu/about/mission ). Questions related to the position may be directed to the Search Committee member, Dr. Hitesh Handa ( hhanda@uga.edu ) or to Dr. Robert Woods ( rwoods@ccrc.uga.edu ). Applications received by December 01, 2026, will receive full consideration; review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. References will be contacted only after initial screening. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2854P Working Title Associate Professor - Materials Engineering - Next Generation Materials for Advancing Health Department ENGR-Chem Material & Biomed About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department About the School of Chemical, Materials, and Biomedical Engineering The College of Engineering is one of the nation\u2019s fastest-growing public colleges of engineering, with nearly 5,000 engineering and computing students since its founding in 2012. Within it, CMBE fosters engineering education in a liberal arts setting and research that meets critical societal needs. The School offers ABET -accredited B.S. degrees in Biochemical Engineering and Biological Engineering, along with M.S. and Ph.D. programs and has grown rapidly to over 500 undergraduate and graduate students and 20 faculty members. Faculty expertise spans biomaterials, therapeutic devices, diagnostics, biochemical engineering, biomanufacturing, and sustainable materials. Additional information is available at https://engineering.uga.edu/schools/school-of-chemical-materials-biomedical-engineering/ About the Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology The Franklin College of Arts and Sciences is the heart of UGA\u2019s learning environment, advancing knowledge, research, and creative activity across more than 40 departments, schools, and institutes. Within it, BCMB is a multidisciplinary, research-intensive department of over 60 affiliated members who lead innovative programs across the spectrum of biochemistry, including bioinformatics, structural biology, enzymology, epigenetics, cancer biology, glycobiology, science education, infectious disease, and molecular medicine. Faculty have access to extensive resources in genomics, bioinformatics, cryo-electron microscopy, X-ray crystallography, NMR , cell production, and mass spectrometry. Additional information is available at https://www.bmb.uga.edu College/Unit/Department website https://engineering.uga.edu/schools/school-of-chemical-materials-biomedical-engineering/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/22/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants are asked to submit the following information along with their application: A cover letter (not to exceed two pages) addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relative to the responsibilities of the position. A detailed curriculum vita A research plan not to exceed three pages. A combined teaching and mentoring statement not to exceed two pages. The names, titles, and contact information for three professional references. All these materials should integrate ideas and efforts that support UGA\u2019s values and enrich our missions of teaching, research, and service ( https://uga.edu/about/mission ). Questions related to the position may be directed to the Search Committee member, Dr. Hitesh Handa ( hhanda@uga.edu ) or to Dr. Robert Woods ( rwoods@ccrc.uga.edu ). Applications received by December 01, 2026, will receive full consideration; review will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. References will be contacted only after initial screening. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Associate Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Associate Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track or Tenured Minimum Qualifications Candidates must hold a Ph.D. or equivalent terminal degree in Materials Science and Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Chemistry, Biochemistry, or another field closely related to the position. Position Summary The University of Georgia invites applications for an academic-year (9-month), tenured or tenure-track Associate Professor position in Materials Engineering to begin August 1, 2027, with the opportunity to supplement salary during the summer. The position is part of the 2026\u20132027 President\u2019s Strategic Faculty Hiring Initiative ( PHI ) , which invests in interdisciplinary faculty clusters addressing problems of state and national importance. This position will hold a joint appointment with the School of Chemical, Materials, and Biomedical Engineering ( CMBE ) in the College of Engineering as the primary unit and the Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology ( BCMB ) in the Franklin College of Arts and Sciences as the secondary unit. The successful candidate will be a member of both units and will be assigned Graduate Faculty Status in both units upon appointment. This position will be supervised by the Chair of the School of CMBE and the Department Head of BCMB . This search is part of UGA\u2019s broader Next-Generation Materials for Advancing Health initiative. The successful candidate will be expected to establish and sustain an internationally recognized, externally funded research program; build strong collaborations across CMBE , BCMB , and related materials and health-science programs at UGA ; mentor undergraduate, graduate, and postdoctoral researchers; and contribute to undergraduate and graduate education. The successful candidate will also teach core engineering courses and participate in the School\u2019s curriculum and program-assessment work, given that CMBE\u2019s undergraduate programs are ABET -accredited. UGA has substantial interdisciplinary strengths in materials, including expertise within CMBE , BCMB , Chemistry, Physics, and the New Materials Institute, together with growing connections to health-related research and the Victoria Kay Ivester School of Nursing. The successful candidate will have opportunities to help strengthen these connections and contribute to the continued development of materials education and research across the University. Additional Requirements Candidates considered for the associate professor rank must have qualifications and academic credentials that are commensurate with promotion guidelines at the University of Georgia. Tenured candidates must satisfy University of Georgia requirements for tenure. For information about the requirements for each faculty rank, please see the UGA Guidelines for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies We seek an accomplished scholar whose research develops innovative materials at the interface of engineering, materials science, biology, and human health. Areas of particular interest include: Biomimetic and bio-responsive materials; Antimicrobial materials and strategies for preventing implant-associated infections; Materials and interfaces for medical implants and devices; Biosensors and responsive diagnostic materials; Bio-interfaces and the interactions among materials, cells, proteins, and microorganisms; Advanced material platforms that address clinically important challenges in infection, tissue integration, sensing, or therapeutic delivery. Outstanding candidates whose research complements these areas and strengthens interdisciplinary materials research at UGA are also encouraged to apply. Additional Qualifications: A sustained record of high-quality scholarly research and peer-reviewed publication, success in obtaining extramural research support, and effective teaching and graduate mentoring. Ability to contribute effectively to interdisciplinary research and education spanning engineering and the molecular and biological sciences. Ability to teach core undergraduate engineering courses in ABET -accredited programs and to contribute to curriculum development and program assessment. Strong record of interdisciplinary research connecting fundamental materials design with biological mechanisms and/or translational applications. Demonstrated success in building collaborative research programs, including multi-investigator initiatives and externally funded partnerships. A proven track record translating fundamental materials discoveries toward applications in human health. Demonstrated excellence in teaching and mentoring undergraduate and graduate students. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/510225": {"title": "Instructor and Associate Director of Dean Rusk International Law Center", "description": "University of Georgia | Instructor and Associate Director of Dean Rusk International Law Center Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Instructor and Associate Director of Dean Rusk International Law Center Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, 3 letters of recommendation, and a teaching philosophy statement. This position is based on-site at the University of Georgia School of Law in Athens, Georgia. The regular work schedule is Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2855P Working Title Instructor and Associate Director of Dean Rusk International Law Center Department Law School-Rusk Intl Law Ctr About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary $72,050 per year Anticipated Start Date 07/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/22/2026 Job Closing Date 12/05/2026 Open until filled No Special Instructions to Applicants Interested applicants should submit a cover letter, resume, 3 letters of recommendation, and a teaching philosophy statement. This position is based on-site at the University of Georgia School of Law in Athens, Georgia. The regular work schedule is Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Instructor FLSA Faculty Rank Instructor Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Master of Laws (LL.M.) degree Position Summary This position supports the International Professional Education ( IPE ) and Global Practice Preparation portfolios within the Dean Rusk International Law Center at the University of Georgia School of Law. The primary focus of the role is instruction, with responsibility for developing and providing LL.M. and other courses related to international and comparative law. The position also contributes to the academic success of LL.M. students through advising and mentorship, while supporting the Center\u2019s educational mission and global engagement initiatives under the supervision of the Director of the Dean Rusk International Law Center. Additional Requirements Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Demonstrated expertise in global legal education, particularly how it pertains to foreign-trained law graduates. Prior role related to international law. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies The ability to engage and collaborate with various groups of stakeholders. Demonstrated understanding of the career landscape for foreign-trained law graduates, whether seeking employment abroad or stateside. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Instruction Serve as instructor of record for School of Law courses, estimated at a total of 16 academic credits per fiscal year. The curricular focus will include the required Master of Laws (LL.M.) academic courses, and various international and comparative law electives as assigned by the Associate Dean of Academic Affairs. The Associate Director will also be the instructor of record for independent projects for Global Externships Overseas. Percentage Of Time 50 Duties/Responsibilities Administration Academic Advising & Registration for LL.M. Students (20%) Offer academic course advising to individual students pre-registration Draft and distribute graduate assistant and graduate assistant supervisor guidelines Lead class meetings a minimum of 2x per year Provide ongoing academic support Update and distribute registration instructions to students, including experiential learning offerings Create course lists for concentrations as necessary Coordinate with the law school registrar to reserve places for students and to update academic schedules Respond to student questions and concerns, liaising with the law school\u2019s Director of Student Affairs and other on-campus partners as necessary Career Development for LL.M. Students (10%) Organize 2 workshops in coordination with the law school\u2019s Career Development Office ( CDO ) Provide students with individual resume & LinkedIn review and feedback Assist with coordinating ISIP interview program Plan a minimum of 2 professional development trips per year Develop programming with alumni/ae and/or faculty Investigate OPT placement opportunities and send postings to CDO Bar Exam Advising for LL.M. Students (10%) Advise students on curricular requirements Provide documents to the bar as necessary (certification; transcript copies) Research bar options/ procedures; troubleshoot individual scenarios Assist alumni/ae seeking to qualify to take a bar exam Stay up to date on bar requirements; liaise with CDO accordingly Dean Rusk Center Support (10%) Assist the Rusk Center team with advising and projects as needed, including international legal trainings Percentage Of Time 50 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Unofficial Letters of Recommendation Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/510158": {"title": "Open Rank - Clinical Track - Aerospace Engineering Instruction and Industry Engagement", "description": "University of Georgia | Open Rank - Clinical Track - Aerospace Engineering Instruction and Industry Engagement Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Open Rank - Clinical Track - Aerospace Engineering Instruction and Industry Engagement Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants are asked to submit the following information along with their application: A detailed curriculum vitae describing professional experience, major programs and projects, and any publications, patents, or technical reports. A cover letter (not to exceed one page) addressing the candidate's experience relative to the responsibilities of the position. A teaching statement (not to exceed two pages) describing the candidate's approach to teaching, any teaching, training, or mentoring experience, and the aerospace and mechanical engineering courses the candidate is prepared to teach. A statement of industry engagement and research (not to exceed two pages) describing how the candidate would connect UGA with industry partners, including former employers where appropriate, through sponsored capstone projects, internships, and collaborative research. The names, titles, and contact information for three professional references. Inquiries about the position should be directed to Dr. Ben Davis, chair of the search committee, at ben.davis@uga.edu. Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2026; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Selected applicants will be required to submit transcripts and a background investigation demonstrating eligibilityfor employment with the University of Georgia. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2853P Working Title Open Rank - Clinical Track - Aerospace Engineering Instruction and Industry Engagement Department ENGR-Civil & Environmental About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The College of Engineering has growing strength in areas that support aerospace engineering, including combustion,acoustics and vibration, controls, robotics and autonomous systems, lightweight and advanced materials, andadvanced manufacturing. Expertise within the College is supported by an extensive network across campus inbusiness, policy, law, and outreach. Faculty hired as part of this initiative will join a rapidly growing College of Engineering that combines interdisciplinary research and scholarship with excellent instruction and service. The UGA College of Engineering currently enrolls over 3,000 engineering majors and has 125 full-time engineering faculty across 15 degree programs. The college also jointly administers the School of Computing in collaboration with the UGA Franklin College of Arts and Sciences, an academic unit that comprises over 1700 computer science majors and 44 full-time faculty. Beginning in January 2027, the College of Engineering will comprise four interdisciplinary schools: theSchool of Chemical, Materials, and Biomedical Engineering; the School of Electrical and Computer Engineering; the School of Civil and Environmental Engineering; and the School of Mechanical and Agricultural Engineering. Significant investments in infrastructure have resulted in an expansion of laboratory facilities for research and scholarship and new classrooms and instructional labs. College of Engineering faculty have space in two major capital projects on campus to create interdisciplinary research facilities. Our main instructional facility, Driftmier Engineering Center, has also undergone a complete renovation to create flexible classrooms that enable a range ofteaching modalities and the incorporation of interdisciplinary instructional labs. The common instructional facilities also foster collaboration by allowing faculty, staff, and students to interact and collaborate in a single facility. College/Unit/Department website engr.uga.edu/schools/ecam Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/22/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants are asked to submit the following information along with their application: A detailed curriculum vitae describing professional experience, major programs and projects, and any publications, patents, or technical reports. A cover letter (not to exceed one page) addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relative to the responsibilities of the position. A teaching statement (not to exceed two pages) describing the candidate\u2019s approach to teaching, any teaching, training, or mentoring experience, and the aerospace and mechanical engineering courses the candidate is prepared to teach. A statement of industry engagement and research (not to exceed two pages) describing how the candidate would connect UGA with industry partners, including former employers where appropriate, through sponsored capstone projects, internships, and collaborative research. The names, titles, and contact information for three professional references. Inquiries about the position should be directed to Dr. Ben Davis, chair of the search committee, at ben.davis@uga.edu. Review of applications will begin on December 1, 2026; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Selected applicants will be required to submit transcripts and a background investigation demonstrating eligibilityfor employment with the University of Georgia. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Ph.D. in aerospace engineering, mechanical engineering, or a closely related field. Position Summary The College of Engineering at the University of Georgia invites applications for a full-time, nine-month (academic year) clinical faculty position at the rank of Clinical Associate Professor or Clinical Professor in aerospace and mechanical engineering, to begin August 1, 2027. We seek an accomplished aerospace professional, typically with 15 or more years of experience in industry, at a national laboratory, or in a government aerospace organization, who is ready to bring that experience to the classroom. Many engineering schools call this role a Professor of Practice. The position is non-tenure-track, with a career progression path through the clinical ranks. It will be housed in the School of Environmental, Civil, Agricultural, and Mechanical Engineering ( ECAM ), which is reorganizing into two schools; this position will reside in the new School of Mechanical and Agricultural Engineering and report to the School Chair. The position includes the opportunity to supplement salary during the summer through teaching or sponsored projects. Teaching is the primary responsibility of this position. The successful candidate will typically teach five to six courses per academic year, drawn from the undergraduate certificate in aerospace engineering (such as aerodynamics, propulsion, flight mechanics, aerospace structures and materials, and stability and control), required and elective mechanical engineering courses, and senior capstone design. The candidate will also help coordinate and grow the aerospace certificate, recruit industry-sponsored capstone projects, build an aerospace industry advisory group, develop internship and co-op pipelines, and advise student organizations such as the AIAA student chapter. Research is a smaller component of the role and is expected to take place largely during the summer. We are especially interested in candidates who can build partnerships between UGA and their former employers and professional networks, leading to sponsored projects, student opportunities, and collaborative research with tenure-track colleagues. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to, aerodynamics and computational fluid dynamics, propulsion, aerospace structures and structural dynamics, guidance, navigation, and control, autonomous and uncrewed aircraft systems, flight test, systems engineering, and advanced manufacturing for aerospace. The College seeks an experienced and inspiring educator committed to excellence in teaching, student success, and industry engagement. The successful candidate will work with faculty across the University of Georgia, including in cross-cutting units such as the University of Georgia Research Institute, the Advanced Manufacturing Living Lab, the Institute for Artificial Intelligence, and the Georgia Network for Electric Mobility. This position is part of a campus-wide presidential hiring initiative that builds on the economic development opportunities within Georgia and the southeast region. Aerospace is among Georgia\u2019s largest export sectors, and the state has a concentrated aerospace presence that includes Gulfstream Aerospace in Savannah, Lockheed Martin Aeronautics in Marietta, Delta TechOps in Atlanta, Robins Air Force Base in middle Georgia, and Archer Aviation in Covington. Hartsfield-Jackson Atlanta International Airport, the busiest airport in the world, anchors a multimodal transportation network that also includes an expanding port in Savannah and a robust interstate highway system. UGA\u2019s undergraduate certificate in aerospace engineering gives mechanical, electrical, and computer systems engineering students a path to aerospace credentials within their major. This position will expand that pathway and connect UGA students with the state\u2019s aerospace employers. Additional Requirements At least ten years of professional engineering experience in the aerospace industry, at a national laboratory, or in a government aerospace organization, including demonstrated technical leadership on aerospace systems, programs, or research. Candidates considered for the associate or full clinical professor rank must have qualifications and credentials commensurate with the University of Georgia Guidelines for Appointment, Promotion, and Tenure of Academic Rank Faculty . Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification 15 or more years of experience in the aerospace industry, at a national laboratory, or in a government aerospace organization Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Preferred qualifications include: Applicants with a strong record of building industry collaborations and an active professional network in the aerospace sector are especially encouraged to apply. A demonstrated record of university teaching, including adjunct or visiting appointments, or of delivering professional training, short courses, or mentoring of early-career engineers A demonstrated record of sponsoring, mentoring, or managing student design projects, internships, or co-op programs A demonstrated professional network in the aerospace sector, particularly in Georgia and the Southeast A record of technical contributions such as publications, technical reports, patents, or sponsored research Evidence of teaching effectiveness or clear potential for excellence in teaching is required . Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509973": {"title": "Open Rank Faculty - Geotechnical Engineering for Resilient Infrastructure", "description": "University of Georgia | Open Rank Faculty - Geotechnical Engineering for Resilient Infrastructure Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Open Rank Faculty - Geotechnical Engineering for Resilient Infrastructure Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin on December 1st, 2026; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Inquiries about the position should be directed to the chair of the search committee, Stephan Durham (sdurham@uga.edu), in the College of Engineering. Applicants are asked to submit the following information along with their application: A cover letter (not to exceed one page) addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relative to the responsibilities of the position. A detailed curriculum vita. A teaching statement not to exceed 2 pages. A research statement not to exceed 2 pages. The names, titles, and contact information for five professional references. Selected applicants will be required to submit transcripts and a background investigation demonstrating eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2852P Working Title Open Rank Faculty - Geotechnical Engineering for Resilient Infrastructure Department ENGR-Civil & Environmental About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The College of Engineering has significant expertise in basic and translational research that supports programs in resilient infrastructure, transportation systems, smart structures and autonomous construction. Especially noteworthy is the Institute for Resilient Infrastructure Systems, which has become a global leader in resilience and engineering of integrated conventional and natural infrastructure systems. Building on these strengths, the College has established nationally recognized capabilities in transportation engineering, including infrastructure resilience, transportation asset management, intelligent transportation systems, safety, and data-driven approaches to planning, design, and operations. The UGA College of Engineering currently enrolls over 3,700 engineering majors and has 125 full-time engineering faculty across 15-degree programs. The college also jointly administers the School of Computing in collaboration with the UGA Franklin College of Arts and Sciences, an academic unit that comprises over 1700 computer science majors and 44 full-time faculty. The College of Engineering is currently comprised of four interdisciplinary schools: the School of Chemical, Materials, and Biomedical Engineering ; School of Electrical and Computer Engineering ; School of Environmental, Civil, Agricultural and Mechanical Engineering; and School of Computing . However, as of January 2027, the School of Environmental, Civil, Agricultural and Mechanical Engineering will be reorganized into two new schools: the School of Civil and Environmental Engineering, and the School of Mechanical and Agricultural Engineering. Significant investments in infrastructure have resulted in an expansion of laboratory facilities for research and scholarship, and new classrooms and instructional labs. College of Engineering faculty have interdisciplinary research facilities in two major capital projects on campus. Our main instructional facility, Driftmier Engineering Center , has also undergone a complete renovation to create flexible classrooms that enable a range of teaching modalities and the incorporation of interdisciplinary instructional labs. The common instructional facilities also foster a sense of community by allowing faculty, staff, and students to interact and collaborate in a single facility. College/Unit/Department website engr.uga.edu/schools/ecam Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/21/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Review of applications will begin on December 1st, 2026; however, applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Inquiries about the position should be directed to the chair of the search committee, Stephan Durham (sdurham@uga.edu), in the College of Engineering. Applicants are asked to submit the following information along with their application: A cover letter (not to exceed one page) addressing the candidate\u2019s experience relative to the responsibilities of the position. A detailed curriculum vita. A teaching statement not to exceed 2 pages. A research statement not to exceed 2 pages. The names, titles, and contact information for five professional references. Selected applicants will be required to submit transcripts and a background investigation demonstrating eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia. Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Open Rank FLSA Faculty Rank Open Rank (Tenure Track) Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenure Track or Tenured Minimum Qualifications All candidates must have a Ph.D. in civil engineering or related discipline. Position Summary The College of Engineering at the University of Georgia invites applications for an open rank, academic year (9-month) faculty position in civil engineering with a focus on geotechnical engineering for resilient infrastructure to begin August 1, 2027. Preference is for candidates at the rank of Assistant Professor (tenure-track) or Associate Professor (tenure-track or tenured), although exceptionally strong candidates at the Full Professor rank will be considered. This position will be centered in the College of Engineering\u2019s School of Civil and Environmental Engineering ( CEE ) and supervised by the CEE School Chair. This position is part of a campus-wide presidential hiring initiative that builds on the economic development opportunities that exist within Georgia and the southeast region. The state has an extensive multi-modal transportation network that includes the busiest airport in the world \u2013 Atlanta-Hartsfield Jackson International Airport \u2013 an expanding port in Savannah, and a robust interstate highway system that serves as a hub of the region. With the State of Georgia and the federal government investing heavily in infrastructure renewal, the University of Georgia is well-positioned to make significant contributions to the development of sustainable and resilient infrastructure due to the comprehensive nature of the university and its network across the State and region. Faculty hired as part of this initiative will join a rapidly growing College of Engineering that combines interdisciplinary research and scholarship with excellent instruction and service. Additional Requirements Candidates considered for the associate professor or professor rank must have qualifications and academic credentials that are commensurate with the Guidelines for Appointment, Promotion and Tenure of Academic Rank Faculty at the University of Georgia. Candidates must also have a documented research background appropriate for the appointment rank. To be eligible for tenure-upon-appointment, candidates must be appointed as an associate professor or higher rank, have been tenured at a prior institution, and bring a demonstrable national reputation to the institution. Candidates must be approved for tenure upon appointment prior to hire. Specific criteria for Associate Professor and Professor level are summarized here . Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Candidates with a Professional Engineering (PE) license or completion of the FE examination with plans to pursue PE registration are encouraged to apply. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies The successful applicant will have a strong foundation in geosystems engineering or a closely related discipline along with specific research expertise in one or more of the following areas: geohazards, groundwater and seepage, foundation engineering, soil-structure interaction, coastal geotechnical systems under extreme events, and advanced numerical modeling to design safer and more resilient geotechnical structures. We seek highly qualified candidates with specific research expertise in areas including, but not limited to, artificial intelligence and machine learning for geotechnical engineering, smart sensing and infrastructure monitoring, digital geotechnics, analysis and optimization for resilient geosystems, and transportation geotechnics. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter List of References with Contact Information Teaching Portfolio/Philosophy Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509914": {"title": "E. Garrard Hall Professor in Early Childhood Education", "description": "University of Georgia | E. Garrard Hall Professor in Early Childhood Education Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits E. Garrard Hall Professor in Early Childhood Education Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants should submit: Letter of application Curriculum Vitae Five recent publications, combined and uploaded as one PDF Contact information for five references. References will not be contacted until the candidate, if a finalist, has been notified. All materials should be submitted electronically via this application. Applications received by Monday, October 26, 2026 will be assured full consideration, but this position is open until filled. Address questions to the search committee chair, Dr. Kyunghwa Lee ( kyunghwa@uga.edu ). Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2815P Working Title E. Garrard Hall Professor in Early Childhood Education Department COE-Educational Theory & Pract About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department As the 4th largest public college of education in the country and the 3rd largest college at UGA , the MFECOE improves the lives of residents of Georgia and beyond through our instruction, research, and service. The MFE COE is a comprehensive college with disciplines focused on teacher preparation, counseling and human development, communication sciences, human movement sciences, career development, student affairs, and educational administration and policy. We place significant emphasis on graduate education with approximately 40% of our students at the graduate level, making us the second largest college at UGA with respect to graduate education. ETAP has contributed to this stature locally, nationally, and internationally. The department is characterized by critical, forward-thinking research and innovative, dynamic teaching. ETAP is committed to making equity, access, and belonging visible in its courses, programs, policies, and practice. Our outreach and research include a variety of multifaceted collaborations, including those with local school districts and local community-based informal education projects, as well as projects that extend across the state of Georgia, the United States, and a variety of international contexts. The Elementary Education program at UGA , which includes Early Childhood Education, has been ranked among the nation\u2019s top 10 elementary education programs by U.S. News and World Report for more than a decade. Our mission in the Elementary Education program is to blend theory and practice grounded in our shared philosophy of critical pedagogy. Upon program completion, we expect our students to demonstrate teaching competencies related to habits of reflexive practice, integrating scholarship and research, engaging in professional collaboration, and appreciating and supporting multiple backgrounds and perspectives. These elements of thought and action are viewed as key to supporting critically informed and equitable teacher decision-making. The Elementary Education program is designed to offer theoretically and clinically rich experiences in diverse environments. By the end of the program, teachers are prepared to enact these commitments as leaders in their classrooms, schools, and communities. The Elizabeth Garrard Hall Professor will be expected to advance and extend the program\u2019s national and international visibility and reputation by producing high-quality and rigorous research and actively participating in the broad community of scholars in education in general, and early childhood/elementary education in particular. College/Unit/Department website https://coe.uga.edu/directory/educational-theory-and-practice/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 08/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 09/23/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicants should submit: Letter of application Curriculum Vitae Five recent publications, combined and uploaded as one PDF Contact information for five references. References will not be contacted until the candidate, if a finalist, has been notified. All materials should be submitted electronically via this application. Applications received by Monday, October 26, 2026 will be assured full consideration, but this position is open until filled. Address questions to the search committee chair, Dr. Kyunghwa Lee ( kyunghwa@uga.edu ). Location of Vacancy Athens Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Professor FLSA Faculty Rank Professor Contract Type Academic (9 mo.) Tenure Status Tenured Minimum Qualifications Earned doctorate in early childhood education, elementary education, or a related field. Position Summary The University of Georgia Department of Educational Theory and Practice ( ETAP ) invites applications for the Elizabeth Garrard Hall Professorship in Early Childhood Education. The candidate for this endowed position must be eligible for appointment at the rank of Full Professor at the University of Georgia beginning August 2027 (or a date to be negotiated with the candidate). The successful candidate will conduct high-impact, collaborative research and provide intellectual leadership in the Mary Frances Early College of Education ( MFE COE ) and beyond. The Elizabeth Garrard Hall Professor will receive endowment support to engage in innovative teaching and scholarship, including mentoring graduate students, preparing teachers and other educational professionals, and collaborating with faculty on research related to the mission of the Department of Educational Theory and Practice and the MFE COE . Elizabeth Garrard Hall was an extraordinary Georgia native whose experiences growing up during the Great Depression shaped her into a hardworking, resourceful, and deeply compassionate person. After earning her B.A. in Latin from the UGA College of Arts and Sciences in 1934 and beginning her career as a high school teacher in Fayetteville, GA, she and her husband, a chemist with the Coca-Cola Company, shared a commitment to expanding educational opportunities for young people. Having supported an orphaned child, she later continued this effort by generously helping impoverished children in Haiti. Ms. Hall\u2019s love for education, respect for intellectual curiosity, and innate pragmatism has been honored through this permanent endowment. Additional Requirements Established program of research through strong publications and presentations Record of externally funded research Record of service and leadership in national and international organizations in the field Eligibility for tenure and appointment at the rank of Full Professor in the Department of Educational Theory and Practice Please review the Department of Educational Theory and Practice\u2019s promotion and tenure guidelines and the University of Georgia Guidelines for Appointment, Promotion, and Tenure of Academic Rank Faculty for more information on requirements for tenure and the rank of Professor. Any request for tenure must be approved before hiring. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies We seek an established scholar and leader in early childhood education with expertise in grades PreK-5. The candidate will have a strong, sustained record of research, including outstanding scholarly accomplishments through publications and presentations, as well as an active research agenda that includes developing proposals for external funding and overseeing project implementation. The candidate will also demonstrate a strong record of professional service and leadership within national and international professional organizations in the field. Physical Demands Work is primarily sedentary and performed in an office, classroom, or digital environment. Requires extended periods of sitting, standing, and using standard office equipment and technologies (such as computers and projectors) throughout the workday. May involve occasional movement within campus facilities and the ability to lift or move light materials (e.g., laptops, textbooks, or instructional supplies) weighing up to 25 pounds. Is this a Position of Trust? No Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? No Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? No Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Sample Publications List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Other Documents #1 Other Documents #2 Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509633": {"title": "Associate Director-Research", "description": "University of Georgia | Associate Director-Research Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits Associate Director-Research Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To ensure full consideration, candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of research interests, unofficial transcripts of all college-level work, copies of up to three recent relevant publications, and contact information for three references. Review of complete applications will begin on November 18, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Individuals considered for potential interviews will be required to submit official college transcripts and three reference letters. University policy requires all candidates to consent to a background investigation (www.hr.uga.edu). Finalists will be required to provide a signed consent form authorizing the University to conduct a background check. The background investigation will be conducted on a post offer/preemployment basis. The starting date is negotiable but a spring 2027 start date is anticipated. All applicants MUST apply online. No paper applications will be accepted. For further questions, please contact Dr. Olin E. Rhodes, Jr., Chair, Associate Director for Research Search Committee, Savannah River Ecology Laboratory, Drawer E, Aiken, SC 29802. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2849P Working Title Associate Director-Research Department VPR-Savannah River Ecology Lab About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department The Savannah River Ecology Laboratory is a research unit of the University of Georgia located on the 300 mi2 Savannah River Site, a Department of Energy facility near Aiken, SC. With a staff of over 200 faculty members, postdocs, research professionals, technicians, and graduate students, the laboratory pursues basic and applied research at multiple levels of ecological organization, from atoms to ecosystems. SREL also provides opportunities for graduate and undergraduate research training, and service to the community through environmental outreach. Throughout its 75+ year history SREL has strived to acquire and communicate knowledge that contributes to sound ecological stewardship. College/Unit/Department website srel.uga.edu Posting Type External Retirement Plan TRS or ORP Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Anticipated Start Date 12/01/2026 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/19/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants To ensure full consideration, candidates must submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of research interests, unofficial transcripts of all college-level work, copies of up to three recent relevant publications, and contact information for three references. Review of complete applications will begin on November 18, 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Individuals considered for potential interviews will be required to submit official college transcripts and three reference letters. University policy requires all candidates to consent to a background investigation (www.hr.uga.edu). Finalists will be required to provide a signed consent form authorizing the University to conduct a background check. The background investigation will be conducted on a post offer/preemployment basis. The starting date is negotiable but a spring 2027 start date is anticipated. All applicants MUST apply online. No paper applications will be accepted. For further questions, please contact Dr. Olin E. Rhodes, Jr., Chair, Associate Director for Research Search Committee, Savannah River Ecology Laboratory, Drawer E, Aiken, SC 29802. Location of Vacancy Outside Georgia EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Assoc/Asst Dept Chair/Director/Head AC FLSA Faculty Rank Senior Research Scientist Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Applicants must have a PhD in an appropriate field (biological, ecological, or environmental sciences). Position Summary The University of Georgia\u2019s Savannah River Ecology Laboratory invites applications for a fiscal-year (12-month) position as a Senior Research Scientist with a primarily administrative appointment as an Associate Director for Research. The successful applicant will be located at the Savannah River Ecology Laboratory in Aiken, S.C. and will report to the Director of the Savannah River Ecology Laboratory. This position will be 0.85 EFT in administration, 0.10 EFT in research, and 0.05 EFT service. This position is intended to provide administrative support to the Director of the Savannah River Ecology Laboratory ( SREL ) for meeting contractual obligations to the Department of Energy in providing research and education activities in the general areas of environmental characterization, ecological risk assessment, environmental stewardship and environmental remediation and restoration. This is a highly responsible supervisory position requiring oversight of SREL technical research staff, evaluation of research infrastructure and equipment needs, development and pursuit of research funding opportunities, evaluation and revision of SREL policies, and strategic planning for SREL research programs. This position will be responsible for assisting the Director of SREL with management and growth of the SREL research programs, including service as a liaison to DOE , the SRS site contractors and various administrative units on the main UGA campus for the achievement of specific tasks. This position also will provide support to the Director of SREL , both as the Assistant Director for SREL Research Programs as well as a member of the SREL Management Team. Additional Requirements Ph.D. degree and 10 years of experience in research administration or similar activities. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification A record of sustained research productivity and evidence of excellence in research administration commensurate with time since degree. The candidate must have a minimum of 10 years of administrative experience demonstrated with personnel, budgets, facilities and funding development. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies The candidate should have the ability to interact with colleagues from a diversity of disciplines on the planning, logistics, infrastructure, and implementation of research programs conducted by the Savannah River Ecology Laboratory faculty. Preference will be given to candidates who have an administrative background within or in close interface with federal research programs, including the development and administration of multi-year Cooperative Agreements with federal partners. Considerable knowledge of the principles and concepts of research administration. Knowledge of basic personnel management and evidence of supervisory skills. Critical thinking skills including process improvement and basic knowledge of strategic planning for research programs. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with SREL faculty staff, Savannah River Site Contractors, NNSA , DOE , and the general public. Previous administrative role(s) within or in close interface with federal research programs and prior role(s) with the development and administration of multi-year Cooperative Agreements with federal partners. Practice good stewardship regarding federal and university resources. Ability to serve as a mentor to graduate students through service on graduate student committees or as co-advisor of graduate student thesis or dissertation research. Ability to contribute to the development and preparation of scientific manuscript as a subject matter expert in research efforts pertinent to scientific disciplines relevant to SREL Ability to work with funding agencies to develop research funding opportunities for SREL faculty, staff, and students. Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? Yes Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? No Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) No Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Administrative Responsibilities : The successful candidate will serve as Associate Director for Research for the Savannah River Ecology Laboratory and will support the SREL Director in a variety of administrative duties, including: Development of external funding opportunities for faculty, staff and graduate students, strategic planning for development of facilities and equipment to support ongoing and new research initiatives at SREL , supervision and evaluation of research professionals, support staff, and other positions related to supporting the research mission of SREL , and development and updating of policies and procedures governing SREL\u2019s compliance with DOE , UGA , and other applicable regulatory entities related to SREL\u2019s research mission, assisting with the compilation and writing of annual reports to DOE , UGA , or other applicable entities, budget development, and other duties as assigned. The successful candidate will also assist the SREL Director with oversight of DOE funded research programs including but not limited to timely reporting, staff oversight, research accountability, student success, and attention to DOE , regulatory and university requirements. In addition, the successful candidate will provide oversight and optimization of all internal SREL processes for safety, reporting, regulatory oversight, onboarding and offboarding, Savannah River Site interfaces, and general business processes as needed. Percentage Of Time 85 Duties/Responsibilities Research Responsibilities : The successful candidate is expected to serve as an adjunct professor and member of the graduate faculty in an appropriate department or school at UGA and will be involved in graduate education via co-advising of graduate students and service on graduate student committees. These efforts will include participation in research development and publication as required through participation with graduate student research. Percentage Of Time 10 Duties/Responsibilities Service: Professional service to groups such as state and federal agencies, non-governmental organizations, professional societies, and the public also is expected as is significant interaction with colleagues and students in other disciplines represented at SREL , UGA , and the broader academic community. Percentage Of Time 5 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you possess a valid driver's license? No Response No Yes Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Sample Publications Unofficial Transcripts List of References with Contact Information Research Portfolio/Philosophy Optional Documents Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509620": {"title": "District Extension Director - SW District", "description": "University of Georgia | District Extension Director - SW District Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits District Extension Director - SW District Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicant screening will begin immediately. Candidates are encouraged to submit their materials by November 15, 2026 to ensure review; however, screening will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit formal applications including a current resume, cover letter expressing their interest and qualifications for the position, and a one-page statement summarizing their philosophy for the position. Include names and addresses of four references (who will not be contacted without further correspondence with the applicant). Please direct questions about the position to Ms. Cheryl Poppell, Southeast District Extension Director, at cashburn@uga.edu or 912-478-8991. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2847P Working Title District Extension Director - SW District Department CAES-Southwest District CES About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website https://extension.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Minorities & Females Advertised Salary Commensurate with Qualifications and Experience Anticipated Start Date 03/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/16/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicant screening will begin immediately. Candidates are encouraged to submit their materials by November 15, 2026 to ensure review; however, screening will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit formal applications including a current resume, cover letter expressing their interest and qualifications for the position, and a one-page statement summarizing their philosophy for the position. Include names and addresses of four references (who will not be contacted without further correspondence with the applicant). Please direct questions about the position to Ms. Cheryl Poppell, Southeast District Extension Director, at cashburn@uga.edu or 912-478-8991. Location of Vacancy SW District EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Assoc/Asst Dept Chair/Director/Head AC FLSA Faculty Rank Senior Public Service Associate Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Master\u2019s degree from an accredited university in a field related to Cooperative Extension, Management and/or Public Administration. Position Summary The District Extension Director ( DED ) is a member of the Extension Leadership Team in the College of Agricultural & Environmental Sciences ( CAES ), at the University of Georgia, responsible for administering the Extension program in one of four districts across the state. The College is one of the largest colleges of agriculture in the nation and supports a $100.4 billion agricultural industry, the largest sector of the economy in the state of Georgia. For over 100 years, UGA Cooperative Extension has provided free, reliable, research-based information to farmers and businesses and has taught life skills and lessons to millions of young people. This is a University of Georgia College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences 12-month Public Service faculty position located in the Northeast District of Georgia. To see the district map and counties visit: https://extension.uga.edu/about/districts\u2014facilities\u2014and-centers/northeast-district.html The Southwest District of Georgia is comprised of 41 primarily rural counties including the larger cities of Valdosta and Albany. The Southwest District Extension Director is responsible for approximately 180 employees and oversees a budget of approximately $7 million. The District Headquarters office is located on the University of GA Campus in Tifton, Georgia. This position will lead the Southwest Extension District staff under the supervision of the Associate Dean for Extension and the Director of County Operations. Additional Requirements See the University of Georgia Guidelines for Appointments and Promotions for Public Service and Outreach Academic Rank for information regarding the Public Service Faculty ranks. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Have the rank or be able to qualify for the rank of Senior Public Service Associate (or equivalent rank) at the University of Georgia. Doctorate highly preferred. Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Ability to provide strong visionary and progressive administrative leadership Substantial knowledge and understanding of Extension organization, operation, philosophy, and objectives Demonstrated abilities in the areas of planning, organizing, budgeting, personnel management, motivating employees, and team building Ability to effectively relate to and communicate with staff, faculty and the public Knowledge and proficiency in the use of technology in support of program delivery, training and staff development Demonstrated knowledge in at least one core area of Agriculture and Natural Resources, Family and Consumer Sciences or 4-H Youth High degree of competency in human relations skills County Extension competency, especially as a County Coordinator, is highly desirable but not mandatory Computer skills including knowledge of Microsoft Office suite Ability to speak to/teach large groups Ability to organize and carry out activities and programming for youth Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with county, district, and state staff, local government employees, and clientele Ability to show high standards of professionalism in personal contacts, appearance, and work habits Ability to express thoughts clearly and concisely through written and verbal communication Ability to work as a team member and engage with groups and committees Ability to design, coordinate, and teach educational programs to meet community needs Skills in leadership and management Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? Yes Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? Yes Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Position responsibilities include budget management, personnel administration, performance evaluations, employee relations, staff recruitment & development, liaison with organizations serving urban and rural environments, and serving as a liaison to local governments. The Director provides administrative leadership for the district team, which consists of County Extension Coordinators, county and district Extension staff and Program Development Coordinators in each of the following areas: Agriculture and Natural Resources, Family and Consumer Sciences and 4-H Youth. The position guides county Extension faculty in the Public Service promotion process and the implementation and management of multi-county programming. The successful candidate will oversee all phases of program planning, including needs assessment, program development, implementation, evaluation, and fund development. The successful candidate will be expected to oversee the delivery of high-quality extension programs in cooperation with appropriate extension and research leaders. The individual will also be expected to work effectively with, and represent faculty to, University of Georgia administrators, UGA Public Service Units, Fort Valley State University Extension, state and federal agency personnel, industry clientele and local governments. Assume other duties as directed by the Director of County Operations, Associate Dean for Extension, and Dean of CAES . Percentage Of Time 100 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Public Svc/Extension Philosophy List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Other Documents #1 Other Documents #2 Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509619": {"title": "District Extension Director - NW District", "description": "University of Georgia | District Extension Director - NW District Skip to Main Content 215 S. Jackson St. Athens, GA 30602 Tel (706) 542-2222 Email: hrweb@uga.edu Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help UGA Home UGA Human Resources About UGA Living in Athens Benefits District Extension Director - NW District Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicant screening will begin immediately. Candidates are encouraged to submit their materials by November 15, 2026 to ensure review; however, screening will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit formal applications, including a current resume, cover letter expressing their interest and qualifications for the position, and a one-page statement summarizing their philosophy for the position and other supporting materials. Include names and addresses of four references (who will not be contacted without further correspondence with the applicant). Please direct questions about the position to Denise Everson, Northeast District Extension Director, at deverson@uga.edu , or by phone at 706-542-3179. Posting Details Posting Details Posting Number F2848P Working Title District Extension Director - NW District Department CAES-Northwest District CES About the University of Georgia Chartered by the state of Georgia in 1785, the University of Georgia is the birthplace of public higher education in America and is the state\u2019s flagship university (https://www.uga.edu/) . The proof is in our more than 240 years of academic and professional achievements and our continual commitment to higher education. UGA is currently ranked among the top 20 public universities in U.S. News & World Report. The University\u2019s main campus is located in Athens, approximately 65 miles northeast of Atlanta, with extended campuses in Atlanta, Griffin, Gwinnett, and Tifton. UGA employs approximately 3,100 faculty and more than 7,700 full-time staff. The University\u2019s enrollment exceeds 41,000 students including over 31,000 undergraduates and over 10,000 graduate and professional students. Academic programs reside in 19 schools and colleges, including our newly established School of Medicine. About the College/Unit/Department College/Unit/Department website https://extension.uga.edu/ Posting Type External Retirement Plan Employment Type Employee Benefits Eligibility Benefits Eligible Underutilization Advertised Salary Commensurate with Qualifications and Experience Anticipated Start Date 03/01/2027 Effective End Date (for Limited-Term postings) Job Posting Date 10/16/2026 Job Closing Date Open until filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants Applicant screening will begin immediately. Candidates are encouraged to submit their materials by November 15, 2026 to ensure review; however, screening will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should submit formal applications, including a current resume, cover letter expressing their interest and qualifications for the position, and a one-page statement summarizing their philosophy for the position and other supporting materials. Include names and addresses of four references (who will not be contacted without further correspondence with the applicant). Please direct questions about the position to Denise Everson, Northeast District Extension Director, at deverson@uga.edu , or by phone at 706-542-3179. Location of Vacancy Griffin Area EEO Statement The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact Central HR ( hrweb@uga.edu ). USG Core Values Statement The University System of Georgia is comprised of our 25 institutions of higher education and learning, as well the System Office. Our USG Statement of Core Values are Integrity, Excellence, Accountability, and Respect. These values serve as the foundation for all that we do as an organization, and each USG community member is responsible for demonstrating and upholding these standards. More details on the USG Statement of Core Values and Code of Conduct are available in USG Board Policy 08.02.18.01.02 . Additionally, USG supports Freedom of Expression as stated in Board Policy 06.05 Freedom of Expression and Academic Freedom . Position Details Position Information Classification Title Assoc/Asst Dept Chair/Director/Head AC FLSA Faculty Rank Senior Public Service Associate Contract Type Fiscal (12 mo.) Tenure Status Non-Tenure Track Minimum Qualifications Master\u2019s degree or higher from an accredited university in a field related to Cooperative Extension, Management, or Public Administration. Position Summary The District Extension Director ( DED ) is a member of the Extension Leadership Team ( ELT ) in the College of Agricultural & Environmental Sciences ( CAES ) at the University of Georgia, responsible for administering the Extension program in the Northwest District of the state. The College is one of the largest Land Grant colleges of agriculture in the nation and supports $100.4 billion agricultural industry, the largest sector of the economy in the state of Georgia, as well as provides outreach for families and communities and administers the 4-H Youth program which is the largest youth development organization in Georgia. For over 100 years, UGA Cooperative Extension has provided free, unbiased, reliable, research-based information to farmers, families, communities and businesses and has taught life skills and positive youth development lessons to millions of young people. The Northwest District of Georgia is comprised of a mix of 39 urban and rural counties. As the urban center of Georgia, the Metro Atlanta area serves as home to more than 50% of the total population of Georgia. The Northwest District Extension Director is responsible for approximately 300 employees and oversees a budget of approximately $7 million. The office is located on the UGA Griffin Campus in Griffin, Georgia. The Director will lead the Northwest Extension District staff under the supervision of the Associate Dean for Extension and the Director of County Operations. This is a University of Georgia College of Agricultural and Environmental Sciences 12-month Public Service faculty position located in the Northwest District of Georgia, which consists of 39 counties. To see the district map and counties visit: https://extension.uga.edu/about/districts\u2014facilities\u2014 and-centers/northwest-district.html Additional Requirements Have the rank or be able to qualify for the rank of Senior Public Service Associate (or equivalent rank) at the University of Georgia. See the University of Georgia Guidelines for Appointments and Promotions for Public Service and Outreach Academic Rank for information regarding the Public Service Faculty ranks. Relevant/Preferred Education, Experience, Licensure, and/or Certification Preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities and/or Competencies Ability to provide strong visionary and progressive administrative leadership Substantial knowledge and understanding of Extension organization, operation, philosophy, and objectives Demonstrated abilities in the areas of planning, organizing, budgeting, personnel management, motivating employees, and team building Ability to effectively relate to and communicate with staff, faculty, and the public Knowledge and proficiency in the use of technology in support of program delivery, training, and staff development Demonstrated knowledge in at least one core area of Agriculture and Natural Resources, Family and Consumer Sciences, or 4-H Youth Development High degree of competency in human relations skills County Extension competency, especially as a County Coordinator, is highly desirable Computer skills including knowledge of Microsoft Office suite Ability to speak to/teach large groups Ability to organize and carry out activities and programming for youth Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with county, district, and state staff, local government employees, and clientele Ability to show high standards of professionalism in personal contacts, appearance, and work habits Ability to express thoughts clearly and concisely through written and verbal communication Ability to work as a team member and engage with groups and committees Ability to design, coordinate, and teach educational programs to meet community needs Skills in leadership and management Physical Demands Is this a Position of Trust? Yes Does this position have operation, access, or control of financial resources? Yes Does this position require a P-Card? No Is having a P-Card an essential function of this position? No Is driving a responsibility of this position? Yes Does this position have direct interaction or care of children under the age of 18 or direct patient care? Yes Does this position have Security Access (e.g., public safety, IT security, personnel records, patient records, or access to chemicals and medications) Yes Credit and P-Card policy Be advised a credit check will be required for all positions with financial responsibilities. For additional information about the credit check criteria, visit the UGA Credit Background Check website . Background Investigation Policy Offers of employment are contingent upon completion of a background investigation including, a criminal background check demonstrating your eligibility for employment with the University of Georgia; confirmation of the credentials and employment history reflected in your application materials (including reference checks) as they relate to the job-based requirements of the position applied for; and, if applicable, a satisfactory credit check. You may also be subject to a pre-employment drug test for positions with high-risk responsibilities, if applicable. Please visit the UGA Background Check website . Duties/Responsibilities Duties/Responsibilities Position responsibilities include budget management, personnel administration, performance evaluations, employee relations, staff recruitment & development, liaison with organizations serving urban environments, and serving as a liaison to local governments. The Director provides administrative leadership for the district team, which consists of County Extension Coordinators, county and district Extension staff and Program Development Coordinators in each of the following areas: Agriculture and Natural Resources, Family and Consumer Sciences and 4-H Youth Development. The position guides county Extension faculty in the Public Service promotion process and the implementation and management of multi-county programming. The successful candidate will oversee all phases of program planning, including needs assessment, program development, implementation, evaluation, and fund development. The successful candidate will be expected to oversee the delivery of high-quality extension programs in cooperation with appropriate extension and research leaders. The individual will also be expected to work effectively with, and represent faculty to, University of Georgia administrators, UGA Public Service Units, Fort Valley State University Extension, state and federal agency personnel, industry clientele and local governments. Assume other duties as directed by the Director of County Operations, Associate Dean for Extension, and Dean of CAES . Percentage Of Time 100 Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Public Svc/Extension Philosophy List of References with Contact Information Optional Documents Other Documents #1 Other Documents #2 Persons needing accommodations or assistance with the accessibility of materials related to this search are encouraged to contact University HR (hrweb@uga.edu). The University of Georgia is an Equal Opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to age, color, disability, genetic information, national origin, race, religion, sex, or veteran status or other protected status. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}}, "rows": {"https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509062": {"school_id": 272, "posting_url": "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509062", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Forest Productivity and Management", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Associate_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "School of Medicine", "area_key_words": "Forest Productivity and Management; outcomes relevant; natural resources conservation", "deadline_of_application": "", "posted_date": "10/12/2026", "position_start_date": "August 1, 2027"}, "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509037": {"school_id": 272, "posting_url": "https://www.ugajobsearch.com/postings/509037", "job_title_in_post": "Associate Professor: Discipline-Based Education Research in Computational Biology, Biochemistry, or Chemistry", "position_type": "Associate_Professor", "job_te